\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Milei would not encourage diplomatic ties with China, but neither would he stand in the way of its investments.\b0\par\par\uc2 633 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 August 2023\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The leading candidate in Argentina's presidential elections, the libertarian Javier Milei, did not deviate from his ideals and said that in mining and metals he would leave the markets to their fate.\par \par \uc2 In his first interview with foreign media Javier Milei promises to pay Argentina's debt and close the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The government has been working to prevent Latin American resources from suffering the same fate again and is trying to turn Argentina's lithium rush into a local electric vehicle battery manufacturing industry. When asked if he would abandon those efforts, Milei said he would not pick winners and that batteries should be made where people want to make them.\par \par \uc2 Milei indicated in an interview Wednesday at \uc2 Bloomberg\uc2 's Buenos Aires offices that he would not encourage diplomatic ties with China because of what he called encroachments on personal freedoms. But neither would he stand in the way of trade and investment between China and Argentina. China is a major buyer of Argentina's soybeans and unprocessed beef, and a leading developer of its Andean lithium deposits.\par \par \uc2 The candidate argued that he would eliminate state \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the country's giant agricultural industry to unleash an export boom.\par \par \uc2 Milei, a free-market devotee, promised to quickly end the policies that have held back agricultural investment this century. He would unify exchange rates, eliminate export taxes and quotas, and end direct meddling in food prices.\par \par \uc2 "It's part of our deregulation program," Milei told \uc2 Bloomberg\uc2 . "Those are all the regulations we have to get rid of as quickly as possible."\par \par \uc2 Argentina is one of the world's leading suppliers of beef as well as soybean meal and corn to feed livestock in other countries. But farmers have been unable to fully tap the potential of the vast plains due to years of market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  designed to boost tax revenues and quell inflation. Milei says Argentina's high poverty rates prove the policy has been a failure.\par \par \uc2 Given that he plans to reduce government spending and end inflation by getting rid of \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in addition to running counter to his libertarian values, would, in theory, be redundant. A free market system could achieve an explosion in agricultural activity, according to Milei's manifesto.\par \par \uc2 Still, the path to such radical change is likely to be difficult: if there are street protests or dissent in Congress, that could stop investors in their tracks.\par \par \uc2 Agricultural exports surged during former President \uc2 Mauricio Macri\uc2 's government's brief experiment with market-oriented policies. But Milei would take things a step further by eliminating billions of dollars in annual taxes on soybean exports.\par \par \uc2 In a transition period, farmers would pay soybean taxes in exchange for lower income tax collections, Milei said. They would become so wealthy under Milei, they would even be willing to fund their government, he said, a notion that is anathema to them under the current administration.\par \par \uc2 In the oil sector, Milei said investors should have no doubt that he would re-privatize \uc2 YPF S.A\uc2 ., which was nationalized in 2012 to spearhead the development of Patagonia's shale riches. But privatization would not happen for about two years, as a Milei government would need time to prepare for the shift to freer energy markets.\par \par \uc2 "We need \uc2 YPF\uc2  and \uc2 Enarsa\uc2  to finish adjusting the imbalances in the energy sector," Milei said.\par \par \uc2 Argentina's booming shale oil industry has been constrained by capital, price and export controls that Milei aims to banish. Restrictions on cash flows recently led Exxon Mobil Corp. to put its shale assets up for sale, according to the governor of Neuqu\u233\'00\'E9n, the country's oil heartland.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020230817ej8h009wg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
