\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 More spending adjustment, dollar  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  and new reserves target: what  \highlight22\uc2 Argentina \highlight\uc2  agreed with the \uc2 IMF\uc2  - By Melina Manfredi\b0\par\par\uc2 717 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Juli 2023\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 On the verge of the July maturity date, the Government and the \uc2 IMF\uc2  reached an agreement that will unblock a disbursement of US$ 7.5 billion that Argentina was waiting for to cancel part of the debt with the multilateral organization, as well as to strengthen international reserves and provide predictability.\par \par \uc2 The discussion was long, much longer than expected, and the parties had to compromise on some issues. Although the Government succeeded in getting the \uc2 IMF\uc2  to acknowledge the impact of the drought and not to ask for further cuts in the deficit for this year, Sergio Massa had to accept some conditions in exchange.\par \par \uc2 In the communiqu\u233\'00\'E9 issued by the \uc2 IMF\uc2  are the first clues of what the Government promised to the organization to unblock the discussion. "Given the economic challenges, the authorities agreed to firmly implement the policy package in the coming weeks and months, and to adapt proactively to the evolution of external and domestic conditions," said \uc2 IMF\uc2  officials following the Argentine case.\par \par \uc2 The cuts committed to by Sergio Massa\par \par \uc2 According to the \uc2 IMF\uc2  communiqu\u233\'00\'E9, the fiscal deficit target for this year remains at 1.9%. However, at the current pace of the public accounts, economists assure that it will be very difficult to meet.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 IMF\uc2  itself acknowledged that "meeting the target requires a further tightening of fiscal policy in the second half of this year supported by a series of agreed revenue and expenditure measures, protecting priority social and infrastructure programs".\par \par \uc2 In this sense, the agency highlighted that, on the revenue side, the Government has already implemented new taxes on imports and an extension of the agricultural dollar. On the expenditure side, meanwhile, the \uc2 IMF\uc2  said that efforts are still needed to:\par \par \uc2 Contain wage bill growth.\par \par \uc2 Update energy tariffs to better reflect changes in production costs, while improving the progressivity of the system.\par \par \uc2 Strengthen spending controls through better targeted social assistance and further rationalization of current transfers to provinces and state-owned enterprises.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, the \uc2 IMF\uc2  remarked that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not have to issue more pesos to comply with the agreement. "The agreed fiscal path does not imply additional reliance on direct monetary financing of the fiscal deficit," it said.\par \par \uc2 How the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will be managed after the agreement with the \uc2 IMF\par \par \uc2 Regarding official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in alternative dollar markets, the \uc2 IMF\uc2  stated that "it will remain a key instrument to contain market pressures, with \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the parallel and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures markets focused on addressing situations of disorderly conditions."\par \par \uc2 However, it asked Massa that official involvement in the bond segment should focus "on ensuring the normal functioning of the market, while protecting the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's balance sheet."\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, the \uc2 IMF\uc2  reminded that it is essential to harmonize and strengthen the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. At the same time, the organization acknowledged that the rate of devaluation of the official dollar will continue to be managed to preserve competitiveness and support reserve accumulation objectives.\par \par \uc2 Reserve accumulation, a little more flexible\par \par \uc2 A relative victory for the Government in the negotiation was in the net reserves accumulation target, which went from US$8 billion to US$1 billion at the end of this year, due to the impact of the drought on the exportable balance.\par \par \uc2 However, it is still a challenging target, given that today the BCRA's net reserves are negative by about US$7 billion. This means that, even if the \uc2 IMF\uc2  lowered the bar, the Government will have to raise the same amount of dollars as originally planned.\par \par \uc2 "This accumulation is expected to be supported by improvements in the energy balance (resulting from the completion of the first phase of the gas pipeline) and by the expected recovery from the drought starting in the latter part of this year," the \uc2 IMF\uc2  stated.\par \par \uc2 What will happen to the fixed term rate\par \par \uc2 In order to sustain the demand for pesos and address high inflation, the Argentine authorities committed to the \uc2 IMF\uc2  to ensure that the interest rate remains in positive territory in real terms.\par \par \uc2 Currently, the fixed term rate is above 8% per month and is above the last two inflation data recorded.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020230730ej7u0079v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
