\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Argentina hopes to close \uc2 IMF\uc2  staff deal by Friday\b0\par\par\uc2 345 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juli 2023\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Argentine authorities hope to close a team-level deal with the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  by Friday after months of negotiations over the $44 billion program, according to Economy Ministry officials.\par \par \uc2 Economy Minister Sergio Massa held talks with \uc2 IMF\uc2  Managing Director \uc2 Kristalina Georgieva\uc2  on Sunday, according to one of the officials, who asked not to be identified.\par \par \uc2 Argentina will send a delegation to Washington on Monday evening to speed up the negotiations, they added, although a trip has been suggested several times in recent weeks by ministry officials, then postponed.\par \par \uc2 As of Sunday evening, some Argentine government officials had not yet been told whether they would fly on Monday, according to one person. Three weeks ago, Massa promised a deal would be announced in "hours" but that has not happened.\par \par \uc2 The Argentine government needs to pay about $2.6 billion to the \uc2 IMF\uc2  by the end of July to stay in good standing with the multilateral lender. The country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  made a similar-sized payment in June, using its \uc2 IMF\uc2  special drawing rights and yuan from a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap line with Beijing.\par \par \uc2 Massa wants to revise the \uc2 IMF\uc2  deal amid a record drought affecting the country's agricultural sector and "political setbacks". At the same time, negotiations have been stalled for political reasons because Massa is now the ruling party's presidential candidate.\par \par \uc2 Massa and his team are trying to receive advances from the \uc2 IMF\uc2  after the drought destroyed $20 billion in agricultural exports. They are also pressing the \uc2 IMF\uc2  to allow \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  to use some of the money to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 , an economic policy the \uc2 IMF\uc2  has criticized in the past.\par \par \uc2 An \uc2 IMF\uc2  spokesman declined to comment when reached on Sunday. Julie Kozack, the \uc2 IMF\uc2 's communications director, declined to give details of the talks at a news conference last week, noting that the two sides were working "intensively".\par \par \uc2 Argentines will go to the polls to choose a new president, congressmen and governors of several provinces on October 22.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020230717ej7h0077p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
