\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Record  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 : the government used the largest monthly amount of its entire administration to contain the dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 786 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juli 2023\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 In May alone, the Government used US$ 759 million of the scarce reserves of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BCRA) to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in financial dollar rates and contain the exchange rate gap. This was the highest monthly amount of the entire Alberto Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez administration, in which more than US$ 4,500 million were used for the same purpose. According to the official view, keeping calm in the exchange market is the key to control inflation until the elections, even at the cost of putting even more pressure on the weakened coffers of the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In the midst of the April run, which took the blue dollar to the $500 level, the Minister of Economy and presidential pre-candidate of the ruling party, Sergio Massa, ordered the BCRA to begin to carry out \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  with bonds held by the entity in order to cut devaluation pressures. This decision went against the request made by the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  (\uc2 IMF\uc2 ) during the review of the Argentine program corresponding to the first quarter and reinstated a practice that was used in the times of \uc2 Martin Guzman\uc2  before the 2021 elections.\par \par \uc2 In detail, the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  used US$ 115 million in April to contain the gap, but in May the number shot up to US$ 759 million. Romano Group economist , Salvador Vitelli, pointed out that this amount was a new maximum for Alberto Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez's administration. The fact that net reserves are negative today is partly due to this," Vitelli pointed out.\par \par \uc2 Beyond the picture that May left, economist Fernando Marull stated that the Government used almost US$ 4,500 million to contain the parallel dollars. With those dollars 1.5 gas pipelines could have been built, such as the N\u233\'00\'E9stor Kirchner pipeline which was inaugurated this Sunday", detailed the consultant.\par \par \uc2 The big question going forwardis what will be the margin Sergio Massa will have to contain future exchange rate pressures, even more so in a context of elections in which the dollarization of portfolios tends to accelerate and a second semester in which the supply of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  falls seasonally. In addition, the drought will mean a US$20 billion drop in income from agricultural exports this year. The truth is that the BCRA's firepower is decreasing and negotiations with the \uc2 IMF\uc2  to obtain an advance of disbursements continue to be delayed.\par \par \uc2 In this regard, Cohen's chief strategist, Mart\u237\'00\'EDn Polo, commented: "Specifically, in the last week, the BCRA sold more than US$500 million in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market -a much larger amount than reported so far- with the agricultural sector liquidating only US$233 million. These \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , added to the net debt payments of US$750 million, implied a decrease of US$1,314 million in the international reserves, which closed the week with a gross stock of US$26,612 million, while the net reserves extended the negative balance to US$6,600 million. Let us remember that US$ 3.4 billion more remain to be paid until the PASO and, with the dynamics of the exchange market, they could reach -US$ 11 billion. Although we believe that the panic will act as a "disciplinarian" to find a point of agreement, this context challenges more and more our scenario of no exchange rate jump during the electoral process?\par \par \uc2 Sergio Massa's team has a simple calculation: in April, the run-up in inflation peaked at 8.4%, while the record \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in May allowed a deceleration of the CPI to 7.8% per month. This hypothesis does not take into account the fiscal and monetary imbalances accumulated by the local economy. Econviews consulting firm estimated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  used US$ 100 million in June to curb financial exchange rates.\par \par \uc2 So far in July, the exchange rate gap has remained low, as reviewed by the consulting firm Ecolatina: "In the last week the alternative dollars remained relatively stable. While the blue dollar ($492) and MEP ($485) remained practically at the same levels in the last week, the CCL showed an advance of 2.6% ($495). Consequently, the average exchange rate gap ended the week at 88%, slightly lower than last Friday's 89.4%?\par \par \uc2 Let us remember that keeping the exchange rate gap contained is an essential part of the?Massa plan? and a transversal challenge to the ?dollar front?, the ?peso front? and the ?price front?: currently, a jump in the parallel dollars filters more easily the inflation (as we already saw in the April figures) and increases the devaluation expectations, reducing even more the net supply of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ? concluded Ecolatina.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020230710ej7a00bln\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
