\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Dollar, inflation and debt: the economic variables that drove \uc2 Martin Guzman\uc2  out of office remain in crisis one year after his resignation\b0\par\par\uc2 1,227 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juli 2023\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 "The first time I spoke to Argentina as Minister of Economy of the Nation, I said that our goal was to calm the economy. This concept may not generate much enthusiasm for many people, but it always seemed to me (and it seems to me) that calming the economy would be a true epic". With these words, expressed in a letter he shared on his \uc2 Twitter\uc2  account exactly one year ago, \uc2 Mart\u237\'00\'EDn Guzm\u225\'00\'E1n\uc2  left his post as Minister of Economy amidst strong questioning from the hard-line Kirchnerism. His departure triggered an institutional crisis within the Government and also a strong economic and financial volatility.\par \par \uc2 After a few days of uncertainty, Silvina Batakis took over the management of Argentina's economic destiny. She even met with the Managing Director of the \uc2 IMF\uc2 , \uc2 Kristalina Georgieva\uc2 . However, she did not manage to stabilize the markets and was only in office for 24 days. As of July 28 last year, she was replaced by the now presidential pre-candidate, Sergio Massa.\par \par \uc2 The merit of the current minister had to do, above all, with stopping the exchange rate run that had been unleashed when he took office, but he did not manage to avoid a deterioration of the main economic variables, despite the measures he took.\par \par \uc2 What happened to the dollar since the departure of \uc2 Mart\u237\'00\'EDn Guzm\u225\'00\'E1n\uc2  and the measures taken by Sergio MassaIn the weeks prior to Guzm\u225\'00\'E1n's departure, alternative exchange rates had started to overheat. On Friday, July 1st, the last day of his administration, the blue dollar closed at $239, while the MEP was quoted at $248.03 and the cash with liquidation was $252.22.\par \par \uc2 Throughout this year, all these quotes continued to rise. The blue dollar closed this Friday at $494, which represents an increase of 106.7% in the last year. Financials also rose. The MEP dollar rose 94.54% and the cash with liquidation increased 103%.\par \par \uc2 On the official side, the devaluation of the peso continued, at different rates: some months it matched inflation and others it was somewhat below it. However, the price of the wholesale dollar went from $125.45 to $256.75, which resulted in an increase of 104.6% in 12 months, similar to that of the blue.\par \par \uc2 In order to try to contain the gap, a variety of measures were taken in the last year. Some of these decisions sought to contain demand. Among them, we can mention:\par \par \uc2 The creation of the Qatar dollar, to apply a more expensive exchange rate to consumption abroad. The surcharge on luxury goods and the so-called cultural dollar, for international shows coming to the country -called Coldplay dollar- were also implemented.Restrictions on the purchase of some products in foreign platforms (e.g. gift cards).Greater restrictions to operate with the MEP dollar and cash with liquidation.Making some imports more difficult.Companies and provinces were forced to refinance their debts in dollars.What happened to the reserves and the \uc2 IMF\uc2  agreement?Other key issues for the Ministry of Economy -both in Guzm\u225\'00\'E1n's and Sergio Massa's administration- have to do with the accumulation of reserves and the maintenance of the agreement with the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  (\uc2 IMF\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 When Massa arrived at the Treasury Palace, he insisted on the need to create a "dollar factory" to allocate BCRA reserves. Under that objective, he implemented a series of rules that tried to increase the supply of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 The three soy dollar schemes (the last one also included other agricultural products) to give exporters a more competitive exchange rate.Monotributo tech, to favor the liquidation of dollars in the country by freelance workers rendering services abroad. This initiative was approved by the Chamber of Deputies and has been approved by the Senate, but is still awaiting approval.Differential dollar for tourists arriving in Argentina, in line with the MEP price instead of the official one, to prevent those foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  from escaping to the illegal market.In any case, reserves dropped by more than US$14 billion in the last year -if Friday's last cut is taken as a reference, where reserves closed at US$27,933 million- and several payments to the \uc2 IMF\uc2  are still pending for the remainder of 2023, in addition to the amortization of a bond for around US$1 billion in July.\par \par \uc2 The accumulation of reserves is one of the pillars of the agreement with the \uc2 IMF\uc2  -in addition to the reduction of the fiscal deficit and the control of the BCRA's assistance to the Treasury-, which after Guzm\u225\'00\'E1n's departure also underwent some changes.\par \par \uc2 Already with Massa in Economy, the Government moved forward in the removal of subsidies to the tariffs for the higher income sectors, started audits on the delivery of the Potenciar Trabajo plans and suspended the assistance to some 160,000 people.\par \par \uc2 However, this year it failed to comply with the planned guidelines -so far this year, the BCRA transferred $670,000 million and the primary deficit accumulated $1.2 trillion during the first five months of the year-, so that since April the economic team has been negotiating a modification of the understanding under the argumentation of the losses caused by the drought.\par \par \uc2 In addition, one of the last conditions that the Fund had imposed on \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the impossibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the financial market with the BCRA reserves, but after the run that left the blue dollar on the verge of $500, the Government rejected this requirement and resigned part of the reserves to avoid a more abrupt jump in the exchange rate front.\par \par \uc2 What has happened to inflation since \uc2 Mart\u237\'00\'EDn Guzm\u225\'00\'E1n\uc2  resigned?The last inflation figure for \uc2 Mart\u237\'00\'EDn Guzm\u225\'00\'E1n\uc2 's administration was 5.3% monthly in June, which translated into a year-on-year increase of 64%. Although these were high numbers, they continued to rise after his departure.\par \par \uc2 Over the last 12 months, the government achieved some monthly decreases, but the price index accelerated monthly since the beginning of this year and reached a monthly high of 8.4% in April. On the other hand, year-on-year inflation never stopped rising and according to the latest INDEC data, between June 2022 and May this year, prices rose 114.2%.\par \par \uc2 The measures taken by the Government to try to curb the price increase were based on agreements with the private sector, but they proved to be insufficient. It also appealed to monetary decisions.\par \par \uc2 Precios Justos (Fair Prices) was launched to replace the former Precios Cuidados (Cared Prices) program, with a basket of grocery and cleaning items at prices whose monthly increase is capped. It is available in large supermarkets.In the same spirit, a seasonal basket of fruits and vegetables was added, which changes every month, and an attempt was made to bring a similar version to local stores.Fuel increases were also limited and work is being done to renew the price agreement for white goods, clothing and electronics until after the PASO.The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised the interest rate by 45 percentage points to try to increase the attractiveness of peso deposits. Thus, the reference yield went from 52% to 97% since the resignation of \uc2 Mart\u237\'00\'EDn Guzm\u225\'00\'E1n\uc2  until now.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020230702ej72005hx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
