\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 The costs of Massa's strategy to contain free dollars and "make it" to December\b0\par\par\uc2 990 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juni 2023\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The blue dollar is sold this Tuesday without changes at $486 in the caves of the microcenter of Buenos Aires. In the last few weeks, the Government managed to achieve an exchange rate stability that surprised the Buenos Aires city without drawing up a new soybean dollar 4 program, by means of a tightening of the exchange rate, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the dollar futures market and betting heavily on foreign financing.\par \par \uc2 In this way, the national government is playing an "all or nothing" game to try to avoid new scenarios of exchange rate stress that could have a full impact on an already accelerated inflation, putting one foot (or both) in a hyperinflationary terrain.\par \par \uc2 To this end, Massa drew up a plan with his team to, at least, reach the next Simultaneous and Mandatory Open Primary Elections (PASO) with the official dollar "accompanying" inflation and the free dollars strongly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The only money the government really has today to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  the CCL and the MEP is the swap it got from China. From the \uc2 IMF\uc2  disbursement, it will be necessary to see how the negotiations turn out to determine whether or not \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  could use part of those funds to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange market", expressed the economic analyst, Sergio Rodriguez. The clamp for provinces and industries\par \par \uc2 The worrying exchange rate situation led to a new restriction by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and this time the provinces were the ones affected. As it was already applied to the private sector in 2021, now the provinces will only be able to access the MULC to face debt maturities for 40% of the capital amortizations.\par \par \uc2 Although there are 14 provinces that issued debt in hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , only seven of them have to pay principal maturities in 2023 for a total of u$s462 million, so the savings of the measure is less than 280 million dollars, affecting mainly C\u243\'00\'F3rdoba, which will have to face its maturities of a little more than u$s70 million with its own resources.\par \par \uc2 Furthermore, the new restrictions of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to access the MULC not only affect the forms of financing, but also directly compromise the industry, since the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Market Evolution Report shows the evolution of the debt forced to importers.\par \par \uc2 In this context, since February 2022 a difference can be seen between imports accrued and those effectively paid. This represents a forced debt accumulated by the private sector because they are not granted access to foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the MULC. Thus, the importers' commercial debt increased by u$s370 million, accumulating u$s2,700 million so far in 2023 and u$s10,600 million since February 2022. Costs of the measure\par \par \uc2 Analysts of the Buenos Aires city warned that the successive regulations on foreign trade force the readjustment of the market, but "it manages to rearm itself and, logically, it presses again to obtain dollars at half the price".\par \par \uc2 If access to the official dollar is perceived as inaccessible, importers will use financial dollars as a reference to fix the replacement cost and this will have an impact on inflation. Thus, a supine victory in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market may have its correlate in inflationary acceleration.\par \par \uc2 For Rodriguez, the macroeconomic fundamentals are increasingly complicated: the nominal rate is accelerating, net reserves are not increasing in real terms at the pace needed, affected by the terrible drought that promises that this year's harvest will be considerably lower than last year's, leading our country to enter a recessionary terrain in economic activity due to the strong restrictions imposed on imports.\par \par \uc2 "In this context, it is not surprising the greater restrictions to the provinces and imports in order to manage the meager stock of reserves, which we estimate at -US$1,600 million", warned the economic consultant. \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the Rofex\par \par \uc2 Futures contracts continue to fall and in the last 30 days they plummeted 34% on average. The drop was seen almost exclusively in the longest contracts, while the June and July contracts maintain a high implicit devaluation rate of 10% and 12%, respectively.\par \par \uc2 "Short contracts continue to 'price' such high devaluations, that the fall is due to the BCRA \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and that exchange rate tensions are still in force", explained a recognized Alyc.\par \par \uc2 The broker pointed out that the average implicit devaluation rate for the next 12 months plummeted to 9.1% monthly and 185% annualized, while "a week ago it was 10.0% monthly and 214% annualized.\par \par \uc2 "Thus, the implied rate curve compressed by another 453 basis points and looks flatter than ever with the BCRA \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the long side. Contracts yield 121% and 138% between June and July, 150% and 152% between August and November, 165% and 175% from December onwards", said Alyc. How much is the blue dollar quoted today\par \par \uc2 The blue dollar is at $486 for sale and $482 for purchase. How financial dollars trade\par \par \uc2 In the stock market, the cash settled dollar (CCL) is traded at $495.84; while the MEP is offered at $472.29. What is the price of the official dollar?\par \par \uc2 The retail dollar trades at $253.83 average.\par \par \uc2 In the wholesale market, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is around $242.50.\par \par \uc2 Thus, the dollar with the 30% surcharge -included in the PA\u205\'00\'CDS tax-, averages $329.98 per unit, and with the 35% advance payment on account of Income Tax on the purchase of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , at $418.82.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the dollar for tourism abroad -which has a 45% tax rate- is at $444.20, while for purchases over 300 dollars -which has an additional tax of 25%- it is at $507.66. The exchange rate gap\par \par \uc2 Finally, the exchange rate gap between the average retail dollar published by the BCRA and the different exchange rates is as follows: Blue: 91%. CCL: 95%. MEP: 89%.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020230606ej6600eou\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
