\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Massa ratified that the swap is to consolidate the yuan "as an investment instrument".\b0\par\par\uc2 904 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juni 2023\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The Minister of Economy, Sergio Massa, assured before the 40 largest companies in China that the hydrocarbons sector "is experiencing an explosion" with Vaca Muerta, said that in three years the country's economic matrix will have "a turnaround" due to lithium exports, and said that the recent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap extended and renewed with Beijing "is key" because it consolidates "the yuan as an investment instrument".During a forum organized by the embassy in Beijing, Massa stated that Argentina is going through a process of transformation of its economic matrix, which until now only had the agro-industrial complex as the main export pole.\par \par \uc2 He also highlighted the importance of having renewed the swap between the BCRA and the \uc2 People's Bank of China\uc2 , a measure that strengthens the reserves.\par \par \uc2 In a 27-minute speech before construction, telecommunications and mining giants such as \uc2 Huawei\uc2 , PowerChina, Gezhouba and Tibet Summit Resources, the Minister pointed out that the extension of the BCRA agreement with the Chinese counterpart entity is "key" for investments from that country and, at the same time, "enables \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 " to "use mechanisms for all kinds of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ".\par \par \uc2 On that point, he said that the three-year extension of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  agreement "allows companies from the People's Republic of China the opportunity to develop a flow of investments (to Argentina) on the basis of the mobilization of the yuan", and at the same time "enables Argentina, not only to use it for commercial and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  investment flows, but also to use mechanisms of our \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  for all kinds of investments".\par \par \uc2 The agreement with the Popular Bank of China (\uc2 PBoC\uc2 ) signed yesterday implied the renewal for three years of the swap for a total amount of 130 billion yuan (equivalent to US$ 19 billion) and with a free availability percentage of US$ 10 billion, with US$ 5 billion deposited in the BCRA and a second tranche of US$ 5 billion already approved for all uses.\par \par \uc2 During his presentation, Massa also referred to the prospects that are opening up for Argentina going from being "an energy importer to a net energy exporter", with an export potential of US$ 20 billion for the next three years.\par \par \uc2 The head of the Treasury Palace also mentioned "the critical processes" that the country is cyclically going through in economic matters: he attributed them to the trade deficit and indebtedness, but also indicated that the process of asset formation abroad (capital flight) is a consequence of the lack of credibility in the peso.\par \par \uc2 Referring to Argentina and "the recurrent changes in debt programs", Massa affirmed that the trigger for the country to take on debt is the impossibility of "financing public expenditure".\par \par \uc2 For this reason, he considered it necessary that "the State invests well, with balance and responsibility".\par \par \uc2 Regarding foreign trade, and with dozens of representatives of Chinese companies present in the auditorium of the Seasons Hotel, Massa proposed that the commercial relationship between Buenos Aires and Beijing progressively advance towards "a balanced trade balance".\par \par \uc2 This, he said, will allow Argentina to "project a trade surplus so as not to experience situations of (financial) stress".\par \par \uc2 Massa was accompanied by the Argentine ambassador in Beijing, Sabino Vaca Narvaja; the head of \uc2 YPF\uc2 , \uc2 Pablo Gonz\u225\'00\'E1lez\uc2 ; the Minister of Transportation, Diego Giuliano; the Secretary of Energy, Flavia Royon; the Secretary of International Financial Relations and head of Indec, Marco Lavagna, and the Secretary of Agriculture, Livestock and Fisheries, Juan Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Bahillo.\par \par \uc2 The event was attended by the innovation giant \uc2 Huawei\uc2 , as well as the construction companies Gezhouba, \uc2 China Energy Engineering Corporation\uc2 , China Machinery Engineering and PowerChina, all four in the engineering sector.\par \par \uc2 Other companies present were \uc2 China Railway Construction\uc2  (railways), China Electric Power Equipment and Technology (electricity), ZTE (telecommunications), DiDi (digital mobility application) and \uc2 Xiaomi\uc2  (cell phones).\par \par \uc2 Also in attendance were Tibet Summit Resources (the world's largest nickel and stainless steel miner), CNNC China Zhongyuan Engineering (nuclear power), Chery (automotive), \uc2 Shandong Gold Group\uc2  (gold mining) and Norinco (defense technology).\par \par \uc2 Other companies represented at the forum were China National Machinery Import and Export (infrastructure), Citic Construction (construction), CRRC Sifang (railway equipment), Great Wall (automotive), CETC (telecommunications) and \uc2 Tsingshan\uc2  (mining).\par \par \uc2 The list was completed with Oppo electronics, Goldwing (wind energy) and Ganfeng (mining company specialized in lithium), as part of a list of more than forty private and public companies, which also included Argentine wineries with presence in the Chinese market, such as Colom\u233\'00\'E9 and Catena Zapata.\par \par \uc2 In the final part of his speech, Massa valued the fact that more and more tourists from China are visiting Argentina, and said that the Government is working together with \uc2 Aerol\u237\'00\'EDneas Argentinas\uc2  so that the company can make the first direct flight to Beijing with a stopover in Auckland, which will reduce the flight time by ten hours (to travel between Buenos Aires and the Chinese capital today it is essential to make a stopover).\par \par \uc2 Finally, the Minister of Economy acknowledged as a problem that the entry of Chinese citizens into the country requires a visa application process that can take up to 90 days.\par \par \uc2 On this point, he promised that Argentina will make an effort to reduce the processing time to 15 days.\par \par \uc2 The entry Massa ratified that the swap is to consolidate the yuan "as an investment instrument" was posted first on Diario San Rafael.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020230604ej64006c6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
