\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Massa stated that the swap with China is to strengthen the yuan "as an investment instrument".\b0\par\par\uc2 734 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juni 2023\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Sergio Massa, stated this Saturday before the 40 largest hydrocarbon companies in China that the sector "is experiencing an explosion" with Vaca Muerta. The Minister of Economy estimated that in three years the Argentine economic matrix will have "a turnaround" due to lithium exports, and said that the recent extended and renewed \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap with Beijing "is key" because it consolidates "the yuan as an investment instrument".\par \par \uc2 During a forum organized by the embassy in Beijing, the minister stated that Argentina is going through a process of transformation of its economic matrix, which until now only had the agro-industrial complex as the main export pole. And he highlighted the importance of having renewed the swap between the BCRA and the \uc2 People's Bank of China\uc2 , a measure that strengthens the reserves.According to a T\u233\'00\'E9lam article signed by Mart\u237\'00\'EDn Piqu\u233\'00\'E9, Massa spoke for 27 minutes before representatives of companies such as \uc2 Huawei\uc2 , PowerChina, Gezhouba and Tibet Summit Resources. He pointed out that the extension of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's agreement with its Chinese counterpart is "key" for the Asian giant's investments and "enables \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 " to "use mechanisms for all kinds of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ".On that point, he said that the three-year extension of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  agreement "allows companies from the People's Republic of China the opportunity to develop an investment flow (to Argentina) on the basis of the mobilization of the yuan", and in parallel "enables Argentina, not only to the use for commercial and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  flows of investments, but also to mechanisms of use of our \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  for all kinds of investments".Regarding foreign trade, and with dozens of representatives of Chinese companies present in the auditorium of the Seasons Hotel, Massa proposed that the commercial relationship between Buenos Aires and Beijing progressively advance towards "a balanced trade balance". This, he said, will allow Argentina to "project a trade surplus so as not to experience situations of (financial) stress".\par \par \uc2 With the tourism sectorLater, Massa closed his tour by participating in the Investment and Tourism Business Forum, where he presented the opportunities offered by Argentina.\par \par \uc2 On his last day of activities in the city of Beijing, the national official was present at the meeting that gathered the main tourism agencies of the Asian giant. In this framework, the head of the Treasury Palace emphasized that more and more Chinese tourists choose Argentina because of its natural destinations and the possibility of making payments in their local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  thanks to the promotion of direct exchange of yuan.\par \par \uc2 "This phenomenon leads to a positive impact on the country's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  income, since today China is one of the world's main tourist issuers and one of the biggest spenders," the Ministry of Economy remarked in a statement.\par \par \uc2 During his presentation, Massa anticipated that the first direct flight to China will be launched this year, in principle with code-sharing, which will reduce the flight time by 10 hours and will improve connectivity between both countries.\par \par \uc2 He also commented that the aim is to facilitate the granting of visas, seeking to reduce the process to one week. In addition, the most popular electronic payment methods in China will be allowed to be used in Argentina.\par \par \uc2 He also remarked that Argentina is the first South American country authorized by China to receive its tourists within the framework of a pilot program presented to relaunch global tourism.\par \par \uc2 According to data from Argentina's Tourism Information System, 7.4 million foreign tourists will enter Argentina during 2022. Meanwhile, China ranks 16th in the ranking of inbound tourism in Argentina (same position as 2018) with a total of almost 76 thousand arrivals in 2019, with an average spending per stay per person of US$ 1,860 and an average daily expenditure of US$ 122.\par \par \uc2 The development of Chinese tourism in Argentina is one of the strategic vectors to solve the income of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and through these incentives the country could go from receiving an average of 70 thousand tourists per year to almost 500 thousand, which would imply a strong income of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to the spending made on average by visitors coming from the Asian country: only in the weekend of May 1, about 274 million people made tourism trips in China.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020230603ej63008nv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
