\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Massa ratified that part of the swap with China is "freely available".\b0\par\par\uc2 1,073 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juni 2023\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The Minister of Economy, Sergio Massa, closed his tour in China with a balance of the work agenda he developed during five days in Shanghai and Beijing. There he referred to the swap and ratified that the increase of 5,000 million dollars are freely available and can be used to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the price of the dollar. This is in response to the criticism of the opposition and the request of Juntos por el Cambio to go to Congress to report on the agreement.\par \par \uc2 Before 40 businessmen who attended the Investment and Tourism Business Forum held at the \uc2 Four Seasons Hotel\uc2  in the Chinese capital, the same hotel where the Argentine National Team will stay on June 15, he assured that both the current 5,000 million and the new 5,000 billion can be used "for all kinds of financial \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 ". In other parts of his speech, he highlighted the complementarity and opportunities for both economies and announced that in order to promote tourism they are working on a direct flight from the Asian country to Argentina and on reducing the visa time from 90 to 15 days.\par \par \uc2 Regarding the new agreement for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap, he said: "It enables the Argentine Republic not only to use it for trade flows but also to use the instrument as an instrument for the flow of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for investments and also for mechanisms to use our \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  for all kinds of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ". Later on, he added: "\b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  has two great challenges to overcome, and undoubtedly, the appearance of investment flows, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps, and above all, exports and imports, using the yuan, allows us to break the idea that the cycles of difficulty are tied to two issues: to the formation of foreign assets, due to lack of confidence in our \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and there the swap and the use of the yuan as an instrument or mechanism for investments and, on the other hand, in the formation of domestic assets, the recurring mechanisms or changes in debt programs based on the financing of public spending.\par \par \uc2 After the announcement made by Massa yesterday with the President of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \uc2 Miguel Pesce\uc2 , the opposition asked for answers on the details of the new swap that will have a three-year term for 19 billion dollars. Congressman Martin Tetaz requested to summon both officials to confirm not only the renewal of the loan with the \uc2 People's Bank of China\uc2  but also the term, the interest rate and the new conditions.\par \par \uc2 Flights to ChinaDuring his presentation, Massa anticipated that \uc2 Aerol\u237\'00\'EDneas Argentinas\uc2  is working for the first direct flight to China this year, in principle with code-sharing, with a stopover in Auckland (New Zealand), which will reduce the flight time by 10 hours. The flights, which cost around one million dollars according to the estimates of the delegation, will take place every 15 days.\par \par \uc2 In line with this timeframe, the granting of visas will be reduced from 90 to 15 days. This is subject to a resolution of the Foreign Ministry, which has already been requested by the embassy and which Massa will try to speed up in the next few days. In addition, the most popular electronic means of payment in China will be allowed to be used in Argentina. "That this back and forth that we feel far away because of the distance that separates us is reduced by the political decision, by the investment, but above all by the intelligence to connect us", said Massa.\par \par \uc2 Among the companies that listened to the Minister, from the Chinese tourism sector, Ctrip, UTour and Qunar participated. Also present were the energy companies \uc2 China Energy\uc2  and Powerchina, the engineering and construction company \uc2 China Gezhouba Group\uc2 , the construction company China Machinery Enginecring Corporation (CMEC), the transport company DIDI, the electronics manufacturer \uc2 Xiaomi\uc2  and the cell phone company \uc2 Huawei\uc2 , among others. The Minister of Economy was accompanied by the Argentine Ambassador to China, Sabino Vaca Narvaja; the Minister of Transportation, Diego Giuliano; the Secretary of Agriculture, Livestock and Fisheries, Juan Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Bahillo; and the President of \uc2 YPF\uc2 , \uc2 Pablo Gonz\u225\'00\'E1lez\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The head of the Palace of Finance emphasized that more and more Chinese tourists are choosing Argentina because of its natural destinations and the possibility of making payments in their local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  thanks to the promotion of direct exchange of yuans. According to data from the Argentine Tourism Information System, 7.4 million foreign tourists entered Argentina in 2022. China ranks 16th in the ranking of inbound tourism in the country with a total of almost 76 thousand arrivals, with an average spending per stay per person of 1,860 dollars.\par \par \uc2 InvestmentsIn his speech, Massa highlighted the investments made during these days. Regarding mining, he explained that he expects the development of the sector to allow a change in the energy matrix and to be a pillar in the country's economy. "We aspire to have exports for 20 billion dollars in 2026 and that from 203 they will have added value for another 20 billion", specified the minister.\par \par \uc2 Then, he affirmed that "gas is going to be the transition energy in the coming years" towards renewable energies. He reminded that Argentina has the second shale gas field and the fourth shale oil field. Energy was one of the main topics of the official's tour. "In terms of investments, investment in the sector grew 42% and it is one of the great tractors that compensates one of the worst situations that Argentina is going through due to the drought", he mentioned.\par \par \uc2 Massa pointed out that in the next three years the country will achieve "a turnaround" in terms of energy balance. "We are going to go from being energy importers for almost 20 billion dollars to being exporters for more than 20 billion dollars", he assured. And he highlighted the developments of the N\u233\'00\'E9stor Kirchner gas pipeline and the northern reversal.\par \par \uc2 Finally, he sent a message to businessmen inviting them to look at the long term: "The Chinese culture, its government and reform project looks at development thought and planned for generations. Development is built thinking in the long term, added value is built thinking intergenerationally. Cooperation and brotherhood between countries is built on the basis of the strength of a bond on several fronts as we have to face it".\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020230603ej63007hk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
