\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Alberto Fernandez\uc2  met with Lula and reached agreement for Brazil to finance imports\b0\par\par\uc2 588 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Mai 2023\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Alberto Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez\uc2  and the Brazilian President, \uc2 Luiz In\u225\'00\'E1cio Lula da Silva\uc2 , held a bilateral meeting on Tuesday, during which the leader of the Petista party confirmed that the National Bank for Economic and Social Development (BNDES) will finance the imports of pipes and steel sheets manufactured by Brazilian companies to be used in the N\u233\'00\'E9stor Kirchner Gas Pipeline.\par \par \uc2 The meeting took place at the end of the summit of South American presidents held in Brasilia, where the Brazilian head of state told his Argentine counterpart that there are no longer any obstacles for the BNDES to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in foreign trade transactions with \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  and that progress will be made with the financing to allow the importation of Brazilian products.\par \par \uc2 According to the \uc2 Brazilian Foreign Ministry\uc2 , financing will be provided for the export of pipes and steel plates produced in Brazil to be used in the second phase of the President N\u233\'00\'E9stor Kirchner gas pipeline (Saliquel\u243\'00\'F3 - San Jeronimo section), and other parts of the northern gas pipeline, Salta - GNEA, Aldea Brasileira - Uruguaiana and San Jeronimo - Santa Fe.\par \par \uc2 In this way, the financing could reach an amount of up to u$s600 million and would allow Argentina to avoid the use of \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves in times of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  shortage.\par \par \uc2 Credit from the \uc2 BRICS bank\uc2  Regarding the possibility that the \uc2 BRICS Bank\uc2  led by Dilma Rouseff may facilitate financing to Argentina, Lula revealed that there are difficulties for the entity to change its regulations to proceed with the granting of a credit to the Argentine government, one of the items on the agenda of the Minister of Economy, Sergio Massa, during his visit to China .\par \par \uc2 The president recalled that at the \uc2 G7\uc2  meeting in Japan he spoke "with many presidents" to intercede with the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  (\uc2 IMF\uc2 ) to help Argentina "not to have a knife in its neck".\par \par \uc2 In this sense, he added that the same request and the argument to renegotiate new conditions after the drought was made to the head of the \uc2 IMF\uc2 , \uc2 Kristalina Georgieva\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Lula assured, in this sense, that the expectations that the \uc2 New Development Bank (NDB)\uc2 , the Bank of the Brics (Brazil, Russia, India, China and South Africa) could act as a guarantor for the exports of Brazilian companies to Argentina in view of the problems in collecting payment due to the restrictions of dollars were reduced.\par \par \uc2 "We agreed with the president of China, Xi Jinping, to talk to the \uc2 Brics Bank\uc2  to change an article (number 7) that prohibits financing to countries not affiliated to the bank. That meeting of the bank took place and there seems to be difficulty in doing so," Lula said.\par \par \uc2 Energy integration In addition, the presidents also discussed different mechanisms to deepen energy integration between the two countries, so that Argentina can improve the terms of payment for thermal energy imports.\par \par \uc2 President Lula celebrated that, thanks to the availability of Brazilian generators, Brazil will be able to guarantee the supply of electricity from thermal sources to Argentina in the coming months and expressed the expectation that the Argentine government will find prices and conditions with Brazilian suppliers that imply the least impact on Argentine foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, they discussed the progress of the bilateral talks on the future management model of the S\u227\'00\'E3o Borja-Santo Tom\u233\'00\'E9 Bridge, whose current concession expires in August. There is agreement between the two presidents that the bridge is strategic for bilateral trade.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020230531ej5u008f2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
