\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 The Government decided to cut "the financial dollar "loop" and another fight broke out between Massa and Pesce.\b0\par\par\uc2 442 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Mai 2023\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 This Thursday, the Government gave the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BCRA) the order not to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in bond trading and allowed the MEP and cash with settlement dollar prices to rise. Financial dollars jumped 6.6% and 2.5% respectively and set a record closing price. The case generated a new fight between the Minister of Economy, Sergio Massa, and the head of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \uc2 Miguel Pesce\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 According to TN, the decision to let prices move without the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  responded to the Government's intention to make its actions in the market less predictable in order to cut some speculative maneuvers that began to take place and also to take maximum care of the dollars, when the net reserves were negative.\par \par \uc2 The Economy detected that there were \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  that took advantage of the Government's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to make a money difference. In stock market jargon, these transactions are known as "rulo".\par \par \uc2 One of these strategies was to buy Mep dollars with the AL30 bond, in which the Government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  and therefore has a cheaper exchange rate. After the 24-hour parking, those dollars were used to buy a bill in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which was then sold in pesos at a higher exchange rate. Thus, the investor took the difference.\par \par \uc2 The one who gave the order was Massa, who called directly to the vice-president of the BCRA, Lisandro Cleri, early in the morning. Before the opening of the markets, Cleri checked again with Massa. The answer was blunt: "Get out of the market".\par \par \uc2 The measure provoked the anger of the stockbrokers and the cueveros, who had losses for about U$S 45 million and went to complain to the head of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Pesce sent a message to Massa and then tried to call him on his cell phone. But Massa gave him a ticking off.\par \par \uc2 Hours later, Massa finally answered the phone. There were cross reproaches and Massa told Pesce "You can't handle a single one" and justified himself: "the stockbrokers had taken our time".\par \par \uc2 Back in April, Massa and Pesce had already had a hard confrontation between them due to the delays of the BCRA in the instrumentalization of the agricultural dollar. And another one on Saturday, when the whole economic team met after the INDEC announced the record inflation of 8.4% in April, the highest level since April 2002. Massa then blamed him for the BCRA's lack of reaction to the overheating of the dollar and prices in April.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020230519ej5j00941\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
