\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Inflation: what is the diagnosis for Argentina of one of the world's leading investment banks?\b0\par\par\uc2 693 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Mai 2023\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 With each official inflation figure released by the Indec, market pessimism for the short term deepens and the diagnoses regarding the unavoidable need to apply a comprehensive stabilization plan are repeated.\par \par \uc2 Such analyses are circulating locally and also in the international arena, where Argentina is beginning to attract attention -although without arousing interest-, due to the imminent electoral process that will eventually determine the implementation of a new economic plan.\par \par \uc2 However, there is still a long way to go and warnings are coming from abroad. Once again, one of the main Wall Street banks, \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2 , prepared a note on the recent developments of the Argentine economy. The investment bank focused on the effect of the measures adopted by the economic team during the weekend, essentially the new interest rate hike, in addition to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to prevent the dollar's financial quotations from soaring. "It is difficult for transitory measures to help," he argued.\par \par \uc2 The report for \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  clients written by economist Sergio Armella describes the critical outlook for the local economy. "The macroeconomic context in Argentina remains very complex. In our assessment, inflation is expected to remain in three digits, there are increasing levels of financial repression, and a significant slowdown in real activity is already being registered," said the analyst, who highlighted the Government's failure to meet the targets established in the agreement with the Monetary Fund. From that perspective, he highlighted that "policy credibility remains weak and the risk of an even more severe loss of monetary and price control is high".\par \par \uc2 The report thus refers to the failure to meet the fiscal and monetary targets of the program revised in March with the Fund. Paradoxically, the only goal achieved was the accumulation of reserves, after the requirement established last year was modified. This relaxation was agreed under the argument of the strong impact of the drought on the flow of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . However, the Fund still did not agree to modify the fiscal deficit target and, consequently, the monetary emission target. Both variables showed a significant deviation. The fiscal target, set at a deficit of $440 billion, was comfortably exceeded by an imbalance of $689 billion in the first three months of the year.\par \par \uc2 With respect to the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's financing of the Treasury, the target also became a dead letter: with the last drawing of temporary advances, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  issued $670 billion since March to finance the public accounts. This figure should be compared with an issuance ceiling set for the whole first half of the year by the \uc2 IMF\uc2 : $373 billion until the end of June.\par \par \uc2 That is what \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  is referring to when it explains that "ultimately, the high inflation environment in Argentina reflects deep structural macroeconomic policy imbalances" and rules out that, with that approach, the latest measures adopted by Econom\u237\'00\'EDa can have any degree of effectiveness. "Unless these imbalances are comprehensively addressed, it is difficult to expect that the policy of transitory measures will help to rebalance the economy in a meaningful and lasting way," said the bank's report.\par \par \uc2 The bank's diagnosis is related to the complaint expressed yesterday by the group that groups the creditors of the Argentine debt that entered the swap carried out by the former Minister of Economy, \uc2 Mart\u237\'00\'EDn Guzm\u225\'00\'E1n\uc2 . "\b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  has zero credibility. There is no interest rate or \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, price control or consumption stimulus that works under these circumstances. In fact, they make things worse. The solution is a stabilization plan: zero deficit, devaluation and free exchange rate" Argentina Exchange Bondholders argued in a post on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Importing to control inflation: the Central Market's doubts and the Government's strategy.\par \par \uc2 Debt: the Government will raise the rate of its bonds and will seek financing from the market with inflation-linked securities.\par \par \uc2 Knowledge industry: the sector warns about a growing "Argentine talent drain" to Uruguay\par \par \uc2 Due to the impulse of tourism, more than 3,300 "hotels and restaurants" companies opened in the last year.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020230518ej5i003zb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
