\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 After rumors of new measures, the dollar closed higher\b0\par\par\uc2 732 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Mai 2023\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The rumors that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BCRA) will increase its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and that it will manage the pace of the daily micro-devaluations of the peso generated doubts among economists, since the lack of official information led everyone to speculate on what could be the chosen path. For that reason, attention was focused yesterday on the behavior of the dollar in the different segments.\par \par \uc2 The free dollar gained nine pesos or 1.8% in its selling point, to $483 in the parallel market, its highest price since April 25. In the course of May, the blue dollar sustained an increase of 14 pesos or 3 percent.\par \par \uc2 With a wholesale dollar that rose 1.50 peso to $230.70, the exchange rate gap remained at 109.4 percent. In the last month, the rise of the official exchange rate reached 7.5%, while in the last year it accumulated an increase of 96.5%, in both cases, below the inflation rate.\par \par \uc2 "The gap between MEP and blue today is the main indicator of a massive dollarization of the black economy. The blue as a market must have tripled or quadrupled," said an experienced broker to the online newspaper Infobae.\par \par \uc2 Stock exchange dollars were also traded with a clear increase. Both the "contado con liquidaci\u243\'00\'F3n" and the MEP dollar gained close to four pesos, at $444.60 and $437.66, through the Global 2030 (GD30, species "C" and "D") in the PPT (Price-Time Priority) segment of ByMA (Bolsas y Mercados Argentinos), where the BCRA \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the offer of its portfolio bonds.\par \par \uc2 Quotation and crawling peg\par \par \uc2 Opinions on the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's attitude towards the exchange rate are divided. On the one hand, some believe that if the pace of devaluation is not accelerated, the exchange rate backwardness puts pressure on the demand for dollars, so that the monthly variation should at least keep pace with inflation. On the other hand, there are those who believe that accelerating the devaluation to that pace (or increasing it in case the gap is to be narrowed) would boost inflation, since the US \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would stop working as an anchor for prices.\par \par \uc2 "April's inflation put a new dilemma to the exchange market. If the BCRA accelerates the devaluation, it will be adding fuel to the fire. If it delays the exchange rate to use it as an anchor, it will be selling cheaper and cheaper reserves, where the net reserves are already more than 1 billion dollars negative", considered Roberto Geretto, analyst at Fundcorp. "The situation is complex and the commandment 'thou shalt not devalue' has more and more costs, but devaluing without a plan may be a leap into the void. In this context, raising rates only serves to gain some time, at the cost of continuing to enlarge the Leliq ball," said the economist.\par \par \uc2 Economist Federico Glustein points out that, based on yesterday's quotation, the peso devaluated 0.57% in the whole weekend, a low level considering that, in the last 15 days, the variation of the official exchange rate is 3.5%, when the floor should be at least 8.5% monthly (in line with inflation).\par \par \uc2 The same is observed by Invecq's economist, Juan Pablo Albornoz, who points out that "looking at an average of the last 5 days, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  let the official dollar run at an annual effective rate (AER) of 99.8%, considering the compensation for the weekend, and, in the last 5 rounds, the crawling advanced to 101% per annum".\par \par \uc2 This is a level far behind the benchmark interest rates. Especially, taking into account that the new rate hike established that Leliqs will accrue an APR of 154.88% from now on. Thus, taking the month as a period of time, "the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is letting the official rate run at 5.9% effective monthly average in the last five days, far behind the rest of the prices of the economy", pointed out Albornoz.\par \par \uc2 The economist is of the opinion that, possibly, this deceleration that the BCRA is marking in the pace of devaluation of the peso price aims at cooling the inflationary inertia we are having, although he warns that "it is hardly sustainable if the real exchange rate level is to be maintained".\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020230516ej5g005su\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
