\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Rate hikes, exchange rate  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  and lower tariffs:  \highlight22\uc2 Argentina \highlight\uc2  tests strategies against inflation\b0\par\par\uc2 748 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 2023\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  is no longer trying to lower inflation; it is at least trying to keep it from getting out of control. This Monday, the Government of \uc2 Alberto Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez\uc2  will present a package of economic measures to defend the peso, discourage savings in dollars and add international reserves to the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In five months there will be general elections and nobody expects a comprehensive stabilization plan or a change in expectations. It is a matter of reaching October with the ship afloat, while the responsibility for major surgery is transferred to the person who takes office on December 10. The polls take for granted that it will not be a Peronist. The Casa Rosada has tied its electoral future to a candidacy of the Minister of Economy, Sergio Massa. If Massa does not achieve economic results, he will hardly be a candidate.\par \par \uc2 April inflation reached 8.4% and raised the year-on-year inflation rate to 108.8%, the highest in 30 years. The CPI has not stopped rising for the last six months: 4.9% in November, 5.1% in December, 6.0% in January, 6.6% in February and 7.7% in March. April strengthened the rise and anticipated a May that will be dangerously close to double digits. There is no talk of hyperinflation yet, but the ghost of the great crisis of 1989 is there.\par \par \uc2 In March, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised the reference interest rate from 81% to 91%. This Monday a new increase came into effect, up to 97%. At the same time, the Ministry of Economy announced that it will "increase \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and will manage the pace of the crawling peg", that is, the policy of daily devaluation of the peso against the dollar in the official exchange rate, as required by the \uc2 IMF\uc2 . The issue is to convince Argentines to keep their savings in pesos: the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has its reserves close to zero and can no longer supply the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 To the tourniquet on the outflow of dollars, the Government will add a new negotiation with the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  (it intends to advance 11,000 million dollars foreseen for the end of the year), increase the swap with China and the support of Brazil. The \uc2 IMF\uc2  has so far limited itself to welcome the "constructive" negotiations with Argentina. China has already agreed to pay imports in yuan for some US$ 5 billion; Minister Massa will travel to Beijing on May 29 to raise this figure to US$ 9 billion. Brazil's aid, the fruit of \uc2 Alberto Fernandez\uc2 's lightning visit to \uc2 Luiz In\u225\'00\'E1cio Lula da Silva\uc2 , has so far been limited to a pat on the shoulder.\par \par \uc2 Food importsIn the list of measures against inflation there are also heterodox measures. To encourage consumption and lower the amount of pesos in cash, the Government will subsidize credit for the purchase of durable goods in installments. Against the rise in food prices, imports will be opened, an unprecedented decision in one of the world's largest producers. The Central Fruit and Vegetable Market will be in charge of foreign purchases, which will operate through a trust. In addition, a Trade \b \highlight22\uc2 Operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  Analysis Unit will be created to "monitor the purchase and sale of goods and services".\par \par \uc2 The Government's bet is to avoid an economic outburst that would dilapidate any possibility of electoral triumph in October. The crisis has ended up cracking Peronism, in a long process of political flagellation started at the beginning of the administration, in 2019. The president, \uc2 Alberto Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez\uc2 , has not spoken to his vice-president, \uc2 Cristina Kirchner\uc2 , for months. Both finally surrendered to Minister Massa, who never hid his presidential aspirations.\par \par \uc2 The disbandment reached the provinces where Peronism governs, which have separated their local elections from the national ones so as not to be infected by the general disaster. Last week elections were held in Neuqu\u233\'00\'E9n and R\u237\'00\'EDo Negro, in Patagonia, and candidates more or less aligned with the Casa Rosada won. This Sunday, Salta, Tierra del Fuego and La Pampa will vote, where the Government expects good results. A Court ruling suspended the elections in San Juan and Tucum\u225\'00\'E1n, strongholds of Peronism where the local caudillos were seeking reelections at odds with the Constitution.\par \par \uc2 Subscribe here to EL PA\u205\'00\'CDS Am\u233\'00\'E9rica's newsletter and receive all the latest news from the region.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020230515ej5f00dvv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
