\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Argentina announces economic measures to counter rising prices\b0\par\par\uc2 555 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Mai 2023\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Argentina will adjust interest rates to curb the dollarization of its economy, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will have more freedom to control foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and agreements with the \uc2 IMF\uc2  will be accelerated.\par \par \uc2 Those are some of the measures advanced on Sunday by the country's Economy Ministry, which will announce more initiatives during the week, after one of the worst inflation figures was released on Friday.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will adjust the rate, increase "\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and will manage the pace of the crawl" the progressive devaluation of the Argentine peso, the Economy Ministry said on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 This places Argentina in second place in the \uc2 World Bank\uc2 's ranking of countries with the highest food inflation after Lebanon.\par \par \uc2 Economy Minister Sergio Massa's team spent the whole of Saturday in meetings and advanced a package of economic measures to control price increases.\par \par \uc2 Economic analysts pointed out that April's consumer price index is the highest monthly inflation rate since April 2002, when the rise in prices exceeded 10%.\par \par \uc2 The Ministry announced the acceleration of the agreements with the \uc2 IMF\uc2 , the China swaps (Massa will travel to Beijing on May 29) and the guarantee scheme of the so-called BRICS block (Brazil, Russia, India, China and South Africa) for imports and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchange with Brazil.\par \par \uc2 There will be incentives to sustain the level of domestic consumption by promoting the consumption of products of national origin, such as decreases in interest rates for credit cards or the increase of reimbursements to vulnerable sectors for consumption with debit cards.\par \par \uc2 There will also be measures to sustain the country's level of economic activity, such as tax relief for small and medium-sized companies, elimination of tariffs and the creation of dumping and protection rules to improve competitiveness and reduce import prices of certain products.\par \par \uc2 Approvals for the importation of capital goods will be accelerated and a new Trade \b \highlight22\uc2 Operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  Analysis Unit will be created to coordinate with other national agencies and be able to respond more quickly to price increases and changes and speed up foreign trade, among other measures.\par \par \uc2 In addition, the Central Market will adopt a new role as a direct food importer with the objective of reducing the effective retail price of fresh produce such as fruits, vegetables and meats as well as non-perishable dry goods.\par \par \uc2 Soaring prices increased poverty, which now affects almost 40% of the population, or some 18.5 million people. Child poverty rose to 54.2%, covering six million children under the age of 15.\par \par \uc2 Inflation is one of the main concerns of Argentines, together with insecurity, according to public opinion polls published in the run-up to the October presidential elections, in which current President \uc2 Alberto Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez\uc2  will not run.\par \par \uc2 The long drought that the country is experiencing damaged crops by reducing the inflow of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is coupled with the strong depreciation of the peso in the financial markets in a context of strict capital controls.\par \par \uc2 Source: AP\par \par \