\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Argentina \highlight\uc2  announces 97% interest rate package and more  \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 458 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Mai 2023\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The Argentine government will announce on Monday (15) a package of measures to try to contain inflation and stabilize the peso against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 According to Reuters news agency and the Argentinean newspapers Clar\u237\'00\'EDn and La Nac\u237\'00\'EDon, the basic interest rate will rise from 91% to 97% per year. If confirmed, this will be the second rate increase in less than a month. On April 27th the rate rose from 81 percent to 91 percent, the highest level in 20 years.\par \par \uc2 At the same time, \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to increase its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange market in order to stabilize the peso. According to Argentinian publications, the measure is aimed at meeting the request of the \uc2 IMF\uc2  (\uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2 ) and accelerating agreements with the \uc2 IMF\uc2 , China and Brazil.\par \par \uc2 The package was defined after meetings between Economy Minister Sergio Massa and \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President \uc2 Miguel Pesce\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Currently, Argentina's inflation is at 109% in the accumulated between May last year and April this year. Last month alone, inflation was 8.4%, twice as high as in the whole of last year in Brazil (4.2%).\par \par \uc2 According to the newspapers Clar\u237\'00\'EDn and La Nac\u237\'00\'EDon, the government is still expected to announce other measures on Monday morning (15th). One of them is to negotiate with the bank of the Brics to facilitate \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchange with Brazil.\par \par \uc2 Massa is expected to travel to Beijing on May 29 to try to bring more resources to the country. Internally, the Argentinian government is expected to lower interest rates in the "Agora 12" program, with the aim of stimulating the consumption of national products.\par \par \uc2 According to the newspaper La Nac\u237\'00\'EDon, there will also be an increase in cashback on debit cards for payments made by the most vulnerable population. The publication states that other measures may be released this week to complement the package.\par \par \uc2 Last week, Massa had already announced increases in pensions and social benefits after 90 days, as well as in the floor for income tax payments.\par \par \uc2 If a year ago those earning more than 225,000 Argentine pesos had to file a tax return, now only those earning more than 506,000 (the equivalent of about US$1,100 at the parallel exchange rate) will have to do so. The increase is 125%, which is above the accumulated inflation rate.\par \par \uc2 Social Security and the scholarships given by the government to low-income families also had an increase of 130%, above inflation in the last year - a real increase of 7%, according to Massa. As a result, an Argentinian pensioner will earn from 121,407 pesos (US$260) in June.\par \par \uc2 With information from Reuters\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020230514ej5e00b2c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
