\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Argentina \highlight\uc2  increases interest rate and  \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention \highlight\uc2  to address inflation\b0\par\par\uc2 206 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Mai 2023\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Buenos Aires, May 14. \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced this Sunday a set of measures to face the shortage of dollars and the galloping inflation, 108.8% year-on-year in April, among which are a new increase in the interest rate and the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, as well as initiatives to sustain consumption and the level of activity.\par \par \uc2 The Ministry of Economy released a list with a series of measures that the head of the Ministry, Sergio Massa, finalized on Saturday with his team -one day after the last inflation figure was known, which exceeded the worst forecasts made by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 - and which, as confirmed to EFE by sources of the Ministry, will be made official on Monday by means of a resolution.\par \par \uc2 The plan includes adjusting the reference interest rate -according to reports, it will be 97%, just two weeks after having raised it from 81 to 91%-; the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will increase its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and will seek to accelerate the agreements with the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap with China and the talks with the BRICS bloc. EFE\par \par \uc2 rgm/enb\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020230514ej5e00b1p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
