\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Fixed term in dollars yields 5% in the U.S. but only a fraction in Argentina: why\b0\par\par\uc2 608 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Mai 2023\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Rate hikes in the United States caused one-month placements to yield an effective rate of 5% or more per annum. In Argentina, yields are close to 0% for savings and time deposits. Entities even avoid accepting placements in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to the complexities of re-lending those funds.\par \par \uc2 Despite the BCRA rate hike, corporate loans grew for the first time in 9 months.\par \par \uc2 Santi Maratea already exceeded $ 720 million with its collection in Mercado Pago but still does not generate interest: why?\par \par \uc2 The local market adds an additional difficulty: today there is a continuous dripping of dollar placements in banks, with a fall in deposits that reaches u$s 1,200 million in five weeks.\par \par \uc2 What is happening? There is a high correlation between the level of \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves and the stock of deposits in banks. Savers, seeing that the monetary entity is in difficulties as far as foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is concerned, are infected by the prevailing uncertainty and some choose to withdraw their holdings.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 IMF\uc2  spoke: the signal to make the program more flexible and a visit that \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  avoids\par \par \uc2 The BCRA's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to maintain the official exchange rate without abrupt jumps made its coffers weaken and there are even "negative net reserves", which adds more doubts to savers.\par \par \uc2 Remember that banks are obliged to deposit a percentage of the deposits they receive from savers in the BCRA as liquidity requirements.\par \par \uc2 The BCRA can obtain yields of 4% per annum against \uc2 US Treasury\uc2  bonds with those dollars transferred by the banks. For the entity presided by \uc2 Miguel Pesce\uc2 , it is pure profit on the u$s 11,386 million it has in its portfolio due to the non-interest-bearing reserve requirements on dollar placements in banks.\par \par \uc2 The departure of the then Minister \uc2 Mart\u237\'00\'EDn Guzm\u225\'00\'E1n\uc2  from the Treasury Palace and his replacement by the ephemeral Silvina Batakis also generated a fall in deposits that stopped at u$s 14,000 million.\par \par \uc2 Today the stock is around u$s 15 billion. The arrival of Sergio Massa and the launching of the soybean dollar I and II allowed the recovery of deposits to well over u$s 16 billion.\par \par \uc2 Another factor that triggered investors' distrust was the launching of the debt swap for government agencies with the "pesification" of their holdings, an accursed word in the local market. This launch coincided with the beginning of the first withdrawals of dollars from the entities.\par \par \uc2 In the previous occasions when there was an outflow of funds, the process stabilized at some point. The system is very liquid.\par \par \uc2 In any case, it is still an issue that is closely followed, especially when in the meantime there are presidential elections that add uncertainty. In fact, the transfer of pesos to dollars is a classic action in the run-up to every election in Argentina.\par \par \uc2 Massa: "We need political order for there to be economic order".\par \par \uc2 A factor that is repeated year after year is the increase of deposits in December, but for tax reasons. The rates to be paid for Personal Property are lower due to the holding of dollars in bank accounts than in foreign accounts.\par \par \uc2 In the short term, it is practically impossible for yields on dollar deposits in Argentina to come close to U.S. yields. Then the demand for dollar loans (limited to exporters) will rise and cause rates to rise. Depositors in banks are looking for custody rather than yields. Although today doubts are gnawing at them.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020230512ej5c00ayo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
