\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Massa called on businessmen and trade unionists to reach agreements for economic and social progress\b0\par\par\uc2 478 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Mai 2023\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The Minister of Economy, Sergio Massa, today called on businessmen and trade unionists to reach agreements to "define a process of economic and social development" in Argentina, and highlighted that with energy, mining and the agro-industrial sector the country will not have foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  problems in the coming years. Massa made this appeal during a meeting organized by the Ibero-American Institute for Education and Productivity (OEI), which took place this noon, informed the Treasury Palace. Among those present were Luis Scasso, director of OEI Argentina; Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Urtubey, director of \uc2 Celulosa Argentina\uc2 ; H\u233\'00\'E9ctor Daer, CGT General Secretary; Gerardo Mart\u237\'00\'EDnez, General Secretary of Uocra and member of the Board of Directors for the ILO Workers' Group; Rodrigo P\u233\'00\'E9rez Graziano, president of PSA GROUPE-\uc2 Peugeot-Citroen\uc2  Argentina; and Gustavo Idigoras, head of the Chamber of the Oil Industry and Grain Exporters' Center (Ciara/CEC), among others.\par \par \uc2  For Massa "if we do not understand that beyond the fight of political, economic, social, business and trade union leaders at the time of public debate, in some issues we have to choose a development path for the next 10 or 20 years, we will fall from the possibility of being global players". The minister made a reflection by assuring that "uncertainty may generate anger against the political class, which in turn may represent a candidate" that channels that discontent. In view of this, "my question is: is it not also time for all political actors to ask ourselves what we did wrong for someone with these characteristics to emerge? And when I say actors, I don't mean political party leaders, I mean businessmen actors, I mean social actors", Massa asked. He said that those leaders "are not aliens" who come to Argentina "and sit in the political parties", but that "they emerge from each of our communities, cities, provinces, states and in any case if we do not have the leadership we want it is because those who believe they have more capacity to occupy that place, do not occupy it and others with less capabilities end up doing it". "That inexorably forces us to think that in order to change things we have to participate", Massa stressed. He stressed that from the economic leadership "we feel that our responsibility is to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to guarantee stability and we understand that, in a country like Argentina, sometimes, from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , from the Ministry of Economy and from the different instruments that the State has to guarantee economic stability, we must \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ". "If \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  has high production levels in these sectors, the process of accumulation of reserves, even with the levels of indebtedness that the country has, is clearly guaranteed for the next few years", said the head of the Treasury Palace. (T\u233\'00\'E9lam)\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020230510ej590018a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
