                                        143\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ii\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Table of Contents\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PRESENTATION OF FINANCIAL AND OTHER INFORMATION\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Certain Defined Terms\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In this annual report, unless otherwise indicated or the context otherwise requires:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u8226\'20\'22 all references to "\f28 \uc2 \f2 Loma Negra\f28 \uc2 \f2 ", "our company", "the Group", "we", "our", "ours", and "us", or similar terms are to the registrant, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Loma Negra Compa\u241\'00\'F1\u237\'00\'EDa Industrial Argentina Sociedad An\u243\'00\'F3nima\f28 \uc2 \f2 , a corporation organized as a Compa\u241\'00\'F1\u237\'00\'EDa Industrial Argentina Sociedad An\u243\'00\'F3nima under the laws of Argentina, and its consolidated subsidiaries;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u8226\'20\'22 all references to "our controlling shareholder" or to the "InterCement Group" are to InterCement Participa\u231\'00\'E7\u245\'00\'F5es S.A. and its subsidiaries;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u8226\'20\'22 all references to the "InterCement Brasil" are to InterCement Brasil S.A.;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u8226\'20\'22 all references to "Yguaz\u250\'00\'FA Cementos" are to Yguaz\u250\'00\'FA Cementos S.A.;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u8226\'20\'22 all references to the "Guaran\u237\'00\'ED", "Guaran\u237\'00\'EDes" or "G." are to the Paraguayan guaran\u237\'00\'ED, the official \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of the Republic of Paraguay;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u8226\'20\'22 all references to "Cofesur" are to Cofesur S.A.U.;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u8226\'20\'22 all references to "Ferrosur" or "Ferrosur Roca" are to Ferrosur Roca S.A.;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u8226\'20\'22 all references to "Recycomb" are to Recycomb S.A.U.;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u8226\'20\'22 all references to "Argentina" are to the Republic of Argentina;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u8226\'20\'22 all references to "Paraguay" are to the Republic of Paraguay;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u8226\'20\'22 all references to the "Argentine government" or the "government" are to the federal government of Argentina;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u8226\'20\'22 all references to the "BCRA" or "\f28 \uc2 \f2 Argentine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 " are to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Argentine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ( \f28 \uc2 \f2 Banco Central de la Rep\u250\'00\'FAblica Argentina\f28 \uc2 \f2 ) ;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u8226\'20\'22 all references to the "FACPCE" are to the Argentine Federation of Professional Councils of Economic Sciences ( Federaci\u243\'00\'F3n Argentina de Consejos Profesionales de Ciencias Econ\u243\'00\'F3micas );\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u8226\'20\'22 all references to "CNV" refers to the Argentine securities regulator ( Comisi\u243\'00\'F3n Nacional de Valores );\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u8226\'20\'22 all references to "U.S. dollars", "dollars" or "US$" are to U.S. dollars;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u8226\'20\'22 all references to the "peso ", "pesos" or "Ps." are to the Argentine peso , the official \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Argentina;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u8226\'20\'22 all references to "IFRS" are to International Financial Reporting Standards, as issued by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Accounting Standards Board\f28 \uc2 \f2 , or the IASB;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u8226\'20\'22 all references to the "ITL" are to the Income Tax Law effective in Argentina; and\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u8226\'20\'22 all references to "AFCP" are to the Argentine National Association of Portland Cement Producers ( Asociaci\u243\'00\'F3n de Fabricantes de Cementos Portland ).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 All references in this annual report to "tons" shall also include "metric tons." References to "dmt" are to dry metric ton. References to "kt" shall mean "kiloton", equivalent to 1,000 tons. The term "MW" and "GW" refers to megawatt and gigawatt, respectively, and the term "GWh" refers to gigawatt hours. The term "m3" refers to cubic meter, and "kcal/kg" to kilocalories per kilogram. The term "FOB" refers to the Incoterm "Free on board".\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Financial Statements\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 We maintain our books and records in constant pesos, the presentation \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for our consolidated financial statements and also the functional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of our \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Argentina . We have prepared our annual audited consolidated financial statements included in this annual report in accordance with IFRS, as issued by the IASB. Unless otherwise noted, our financial information presented herein as of December 31, 2022 and 2021, and for the years ended December 31, 2022, 2021 and 2020 is stated in pesos, our reporting \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 This annual report includes our audited consolidated financial statements as of December 31, 2022 and 2021 and for each of the years ended December 31, 2022, 2021 and 2020, together with the notes thereto, or "our audited consolidated financial statements". All references herein to "our financial statements", "our audited consolidated financial information",\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 iii\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Table of Contents\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 and "our audited consolidated financial statements", are to or derived from our consolidated financial statements included elsewhere in this annual report.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Our audited consolidated financial statements as of December 31, 2022 and 2021 and for each of the years ended December 31, 2022, 2021 and 2020, comprehensively recognize the effects of variations in the purchasing power of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  through the application of the method to restate financial statements in constant \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  established by the International Accounting Standard 29, or IAS 29, as Argentina is considered a hyperinflationary economy starting July 1, 2018.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Financial information presented in constant \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 IAS 29, Financial Reporting in Hyperinflationary Economies ("IAS 29") requires that the financial statements of an entity whose functional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is one of a hyperinflationary economy be measured in terms of the current unit of measurement at the closing date of the financial statements, regardless of whether they are based on the historical cost method or the current cost method. This requirement also includes the comparative information of the financial statements.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In order to conclude that an economy is "hyperinflationary," IAS 29 outlines a series of factors, including the existence of an accumulated inflation rate in three years that is approximately or exceeds 100%. As of December 31, 2018, Argentina reported a cumulative three-year inflation rate greater than 100% and therefore financial information published as from that date should be adjusted for inflation in accordance with IAS 29. The inflation of the subsequent fiscal years continues to be high and above the 100% accumulated inflation trend for three consecutive years. Therefore, our audited consolidated financial statements and the financial information included in this annual report have been stated in terms of the measuring unit current at the end of the reporting year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In accordance with IAS 29, the amounts in the financial statements that have not been stated in constant \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as of the end of the reporting period must be restated by application of a general price index. To that end and in the manner established in FACPCE's Resolution JG No. 539/18, coefficients have been applied that are calculated on the basis of indices published by the FACPCE, resulting from combining national the consumer prices index ( \u205\'00\'CDndice de Precios al Consumidor-IPC ), or CPI, published by the Instituto Nacional de Estad\u237\'00\'EDsticas y Censos (the National Statistics and Census Institute), or INDEC, starting on January 1, 2017 and, looking back, domestic wholesale prices index ( \u205\'00\'CDndice de Precios Internos al por Mayor-IPIM ), or WPI, published by the INDEC or, if none is available, consumer price indices published by the General Directorate of Statistics and Censuses in the Autonomous City of Buenos Aires. The variation in the index applied to restate our audited consolidated financial statements for the years ended as of December 31, 2022, 2021 and 2020 was 94.8%, 50.9% and 36.1%, respectively.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Market Data and Other Information\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 We obtained the market and competitive position data, including market forecasts, used throughout this annual report from internal surveys, market research, publicly available information and industry publications. We include data from reports prepared by ourselves; the Argentine National Association of Portland Cement Producers ( Asociaci\u243\'00\'F3n de Fabricantes de Cementos Portland) , or AFCP; the BCRA; the INDEC (the only institution in Argentina with the statutory authority to produce official nationwide statistics); and the \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2 , or IMF.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 INDEC reported that the CPI increase was 36.1%, 50.9% and 94.8% for the years ended December 31, 2020, 2021 and 2022, respectively. INDEC has also published inflation figures for the WPI for the year ended December 31, 2020, reporting an increase of 35.4%, for year ended December 31, 2021 an increase of 51,3% and for year ended December 31, 2022 an increase of 94.8%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 See "Item 3.D Key Information-Risk Factors-Risks Relating to Argentina-If the current levels of inflation do not decrease, the Argentine economy could be adversely affected, negatively impacting our results of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and margins". Industry publications generally state that the information presented therein has been obtained from sources believed to be reliable, but the accuracy and completeness of such information is not guaranteed. While we are not aware of any misstatements regarding the industry data presented herein, estimates and forecasts involve uncertainties and risks and are subject to change based on various factors, including those discussed under the headings "Special Note Regarding Forward-Looking Statements" and "Item 3.D Key Information-Risk Factors" in this annual report.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Rounding\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 We have made rounding adjustments to reach some of the figures included in this annual report. As a result, numerical figures shown as totals in some tables may not be an arithmetic aggregation of the figures that preceded them.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 iv\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Table of Contents\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CAUTIONARY STATEMENT WITH RESPECT TO FORWARD-LOOKING STATEMENTS AND RISK FACTORS SUMMARY\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 We make forward-looking statements in this annual report within the meaning of Section 27A of the Securities Act of 1933, as amended, or the Securities Act, Section 21E of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934, as amended, or the Exchange Act, and the safe harbor provisions of the U.S. Private Securities Litigation Reform Act of 1995, that are subject to risks and uncertainties. These forward-looking statements include information about possible or assumed future results of our business, financial condition, results of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , liquidity, plans and objectives. In some cases, you can identify forward-looking statements by terminology such as "believe", "may", "estimate", "continue", "anticipate", "intend", "should", "would", "could," "plan", "expect", "predict", "potential", "seek", "likely," "forecast", or the negative of these terms or other similar expressions. There are important factors that could cause our actual results, levels of activity, performance or achievements to differ materially from the results, levels of activity, performance or achievements expressed or implied by the forward-looking statements. These factors include the principal risks relating to the Company and its business described in "Part I, Item 3. Key Information-D. Risk Factors," which are also summarized below:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u8226\'20\'22 general economic, political and business conditions, in Argentina, including government policies and as a result of the presidential and congressional elections taking place in 2023;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u8226\'20\'22 inflation, fiscal deficit, the devaluation of the peso and exchange rate risks in Argentina;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u8226\'20\'22 restrictions on the ability to exchange peso into foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and transfer funds abroad;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u8226\'20\'22 implementation of additional exchange controls and restrictions on capital inflows that limit credit availability;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u8226\'20\'22 government \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the Argentine economy;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u8226\'20\'22 developments in markets outside of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Argentina\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that may indirectly affect the Argentine economy;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u8226\'20\'22 the cyclical nature of the cement industry;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 