\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 What is the 'blue dollar' and why is its value high in Argentina?\b0\par\par\uc2 918 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 April 2023\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES - Anxiety, lack of prices and lack of goods in stores are generalized in Argentina due to the rise of parallel exchange rates, in a population accustomed to follow the 'blue dollar' (black market) due to the strong restrictions applied by the Government to access the official one.\par \par \uc2 The rise in the value of the US \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is in its second week, is followed up to the minute in portals and TV channels, in a country accustomed to use the dollar as a thermometer of economic crises.\par \par \uc2 What is the 'blue dollar' in Argentina?In Argentina there are several types of dollar exchange rates. The BBC explains that there is the official dollar and the blue dollar.\par \par \uc2 The official dollar price is determined by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Argentina\uc2 . And it has the lowest quotation, in addition to the fact that only financial and foreign trade entities have access to this official dollar.\par \par \uc2 But the real king is the blue dollar, notes the BBC: for many people in Argentina, such as traders, it is the most important reference. Its value is higher than the official dollar.\par \par \uc2 The price of the 'blue dollar'"In the moments of rise and fall of the 'blue dollar', some stores stopped selling, because they could not establish a sale price", since "the fabrics are all imported" and "the jeans stores changed the price three times in a period of two hours", Cecilia Weingardt, administrative employee of a textile importer that sells wholesale fabrics, told EFE.\par \par \uc2 Situations like this, the immediate increase in prices or the absence of the value on the menus of restaurants and supermarket shelves, so as not to have to change them several times a day, explained those establishments, are becoming commonplace.\par \par \uc2 For example, on Tuesday, April 26, Mar\u237\'00\'EDa Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Boga bought a stove online and explained to EFE that, in the period in which she completed the purchase process, "the price increased by 3000 pesos", to almost 53,000 pesos (241 dollars at the official exchange rate, 113 at the parallel rate).\par \par \uc2 The 'blue dollar' touched 500 pesos this Tuesday, in the second week of exchange tension triggered by a higher than expected inflation (104.3 percent annual in March), when there was already a shortage of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and net international reserves at minimum levels, deepened by a historic drought that reduces agricultural exports by some 20 billion dollars and a fiscal deficit financed with monetary emission in an economy that demands little local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Waiting for the opening of the market this Wednesday, the 'blue dollar' is down to 473 pesos per unit, "there is nobody buying", added Weingardt.\par \par \uc2 Those who sell non-essential products see how sales have come to a standstill: "People say it is very expensive," Bel\u233\'00\'E9n Lizzi, who sells scented candles, told EFE.\par \par \uc2 Blue dollar' soars in ArgentinaThe soaring parallel exchange rates fuel expectations of a jump in the official exchange rate, despite the fact that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has accelerated the daily depreciation, since it quotes 221.54 pesos per unit for sale, with a 106 percent gap with the so-called financial dollars.\par \par \uc2 The decision of the Minister of Economy, Sergio Massa, on Tuesday to use "all the tools" to order the exchange rate situation is bearing fruit on Wednesday, since the "cash with liquidation" dollar (CCL, which consists of buying locally with Argentine pesos stocks or bonds and selling them in dollars on Wall Street) is down 2 percent, to 456.72 pesos per unit.\par \par \uc2 In spite of the fact that the President ratified the President of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \uc2 Miguel Pesce\uc2 , the Treasury increased its interference in the exchange rate management, as a result of Massa's decision, and managed to contain the rise.\par \par \uc2 Argentina's political weaknessThe economic fragility has a political component, because the ruling Peronism has internal differences and manages with the only common vision of reaching the primary elections of next August and the presidential elections of October without an explosion.\par \par \uc2 The head of state, \uc2 Alberto Fernandez\uc2 , resigned last Friday to run for reelection and, very weakened, blames the speculation of "the right wing" of the opposition for this rise of the last days, while the vice-president, \uc2 Cristina Fernandez\uc2 , will only appear in public this Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Massa was negotiating concessions from the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  (\uc2 IMF\uc2 ), with whom the country agreed a program to refinance a debt of 45 billion dollars.\par \par \uc2 The minister notified the \uc2 IMF\uc2  of his decision to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the parallel exchange markets, since it implies not complying with the "restrictions" that weigh on \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which call for avoiding such \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , something that Massa said he plans to "change in the rediscussion" of the program.\par \par \uc2 The economic team will travel this week to Washington to negotiate with the \uc2 IMF\uc2 , since Argentina intends to receive the quarterly disbursement despite not having met the net reserves and fiscal deficit targets for the first quarter, while seeking access to more foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Despite the \uc2 IMF\uc2 's predisposition to maintain a "constructive" work with Argentina, the Peronist government's management is difficult until the elections, which adds to the usual search for coverage in election years.\par \par \uc2 Additionally, the proposals of the opposition candidates to dollarize the economy or to quickly end the restrictions (cepo) to operate in the official exchange market further fuel the purchase of dollars, increasing the exchange rate uncertainty.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020230427ej4r00e6x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
