\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 "Three price changes in two hours": Argentina experiences uncertainty with rising dollar blue\b0\par\par\uc2 733 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 April 2023\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Anxiety, lack of constancy in prices and of products in stores have become widespread in Argentina among a population used to following the quotation of the so-called "blue dollar" - usually the cheapest for buying and selling American \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but that has started to deal with the increase of parallel exchange rates because of severe restrictions applied by the government for negotiations with the official \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The rise in the price of American \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is monitored minute by minute on internet portals and television networks, in a country accustomed to using the dollar as a thermometer of economic crises.\par \par \uc2 "In the up and down moments of the blue dollar, some stores stopped selling because they couldn't set a price, since the fabrics are all imported. Jeans stores changed prices three times in two hours on Tuesday," said Cecilia Weingardt, an employee at a textile importer that sells wholesale fabrics.\par \par \uc2 The immediate increase of prices, or even the absence of them on restaurant menus and supermarket shelves - so they don't have to be changed several times a day - are becoming commonplace. For example, on Tuesday (25), Mar\u237\'00\'EDa Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Boga bought a stove over the Internet and told the report that in the period it took to complete the purchase process, "the price increased by 3,000 pesos," reaching almost 53,000 pesos, equivalent to US$241 in the official exchange rate or US$113 in the parallel one.\par \par \uc2 The blue dollar reached 500 pesos on Tuesday, in the second week of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tension triggered by higher-than-expected inflation (104.3% in the one-year period in March), when foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  shortages already reigned and net international reserves reached minimum levels.\par \par \uc2 DroughtArgentina's crisis is also deepened by a historic drought, which has reduced agricultural exports by about US$20 billion, along with a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -issuing fiscal deficit in an economy that demands little local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Those who trade in products other than basic necessities see how sales have stalled. "People say it's too expensive," said Bel\u233\'00\'E9n Lizzi, who sells scented candles.\par \par \uc2 DisparadaThe rise in the parallel exchange rate types is fueling expectations of a jump in the official exchange rate, even though the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has accelerated the daily devaluation, quoting the dollar at 221.54 pesos per unit for sale, a 106% difference from the so-called financial dollars.\par \par \uc2 Economy Minister Sergio Massa's decision on Tuesday to use "all tools" to resolve the exchange rate situation bore fruit on Wednesday (26), as the so-called settlement-counted dollar (CCL, which consists of buying locally, with Argentine pesos, stocks or bonds and selling them in dollars on Wall Street) even fell 2%.\par \par \uc2 Political FragilityEconomic fragility has a political component, as the ruling Peronism has internal differences and governs with the single common vision of reaching the primary elections next August and the presidential elections in October smoothly.\par \par \uc2 Argentina's President \uc2 Alberto Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez\uc2  announced last Friday, April 21, that he will not run for re-election and, greatly weakened, attributes the rise in the dollar in recent days to speculation by the "right-wing opposition".\par \par \uc2 Negotiations with the IMFArgentina's economy minister was negotiating concessions with the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  (\uc2 IMF\uc2 ), with which the country has agreed a program to refinance a US$45 billion debt. Massa notified the \uc2 IMF\uc2  of his decision to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the parallel \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, since this implies not complying with "restrictions" imposed on \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  that require the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to avoid such \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which he said he plans to "change in the program's rediscussion.\par \par \uc2 The economic team will travel to Washington this week to negotiate with the \uc2 IMF\uc2 , as Argentina seeks to receive the quarterly tranche [of loan] despite the country's failure to meet net reserves and fiscal deficit targets for the first quarter, while seeking access to more foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Despite the \uc2 IMF\uc2 's willingness to work "constructively" with Argentina, the government's management of the country's economy will remain in question until the October presidential elections, which increases the usual demand for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  protection in election years. In addition, opposition candidates' proposals to dollarize the economy or quickly end restrictions on trading in the official \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market are further fueling dollar buying and uncertainty about the direction of the exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020230427ej4r00aac\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
