\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Faced with lack of  \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange \highlight\uc2 , Massa activates swap with China\b0\par\par\uc2 1,033 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 April 2023\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 After Tuesday's exchange run, the Government seeks to reduce dependence on the dollar by switching trade with the Asian giant to yuan. It seeks to speed up imports to mitigate the effect of shortages on inflation.\par \par \uc2 The Minister of Economy, Sergio Massa, announced yesterday that an agreement was reached -with the participation of the \uc2 People's Bank of China\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a group of Argentine companies- whereby an import authorization system with shorter terms will be implemented and imports will be paid directly with yuans, thus avoiding Argentina the use of dollars to finance those purchases abroad.\par \par \uc2 The announcement was made at the Treasury Palace, in a ceremony attended by the Chinese ambassador in the country, Zou Xiaoli, and a group of Argentine officials, including the president of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Argentina\uc2  (BCRA), \uc2 Miguel Pesce\uc2 , the secretaries of Economic Policy, Gabriel Rubinstein, and of Trade, Mat\u237\'00\'EDas Tombolini, and the head of the General Directorate of Customs (DGA), Guillermo Michel.\par \par \uc2 Tranquility\par \par \uc2 The minister said that this "allows us for the coming months to work on the possibility of bringing forward the pace of imports, the vast majority of these authorizations were worked at 180 days and with the yuans they are worked at 90 days, and to schedule a volume of imports in yuans for more than US$1 billion as from next month, which replace the use of dollars from Argentina". He further assured that "this improves Argentina's reserve outlook in terms of net reserves" and "gives us greater freedom".\par \par \uc2 In these troubled days, he said that the agreement "adds operating capacity from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  [when] we had to make the decision to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  against those who, thinking that we did not have economic capacity as a State, speculated and overspeculated", he affirmed.\par \par \uc2 He also stated that "somehow it also allows us to maintain the level of activity, the volume of imports, the rhythm of trade between Argentina and China, and the levels of economic \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  that Argentina needs".\par \par \uc2 "This release of payment obligations of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , not only of a stock but of the flow, is greater strength for the reserves, greater capacity of State \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , greater freedom of our economy and above all it is the guarantee to continue producing with intermediate goods that are imported from China and that also no longer suffer the triangulation process that in some cases we had detected", he concluded.\par \par \uc2 The Chinese vision\par \par \uc2 For his part, Chinese Ambassador Zou Xiaoli assured that this agreement will aim "to continue strengthening cooperation between China and Argentina and reflects the strategic relationship and complementarity between Argentina and China, that was reflected in the visit of President \uc2 Alberto Fernandez\uc2  to China."\par \par \uc2 "China pays a lot of attention to bilateral trade with Argentina. We attach importance to the swap we have been working on, wishing to work together to protect and develop our global markets and companies so that they can use local \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and reduce risks and costs", mentioned the Chinese government representative.\par \par \uc2 "In 2020, the People's Bank and BCRA signed the new agreement to establish new swap tranches. We have been working closely to exchange data and information. We are confident that Argentina can maintain its economic and financial stability", he concluded.\par \par \uc2 Some numbers\par \par \uc2 Since the implementation of customs inspections, the import request monitor, the Import System of the Argentine Republic (SIRA) managed by the Federal Administration of Public Revenues (AFIP), the Secretariat of Commerce and the BCRA, there has been an increase in the use of yuans for the payment of imports from China itself. That number increased eightfold. "So far in April alone, SIRAs were authorized in yuans for the equivalent of US$217 million, compared to US$29 million in January", official data show.\par \par \uc2 Similarly, the number of SIRA procedures in yuan also increased, from 206 in January to 325 in February, 388 in March and 517 in April, accumulating 1,436 procedures so far this year. In 2023, 4,803 destinations for US$287,781,648 of imports of goods manufactured in China and re-invoiced in European countries have been analyzed.\par \par \uc2 Put in numbers, the new tranche of the swap announced by the Ministry of Economy implies the payment of imports with yuans for an equivalent of US$1,040 million for May, and that in the next months there will be a minimum of purchases from that country paid in yuans for a value equal to some US$790 million per month.\par \par \uc2 The blue dollar fell after two days of "fury". Yesterday, Wednesday, was a day of calm in the exchange market because the price of the free dollar fell, after the escalation that took it to almost $500 on Tuesday. "We had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  before those who overspeculated, this will give us more freedom", said Massa.\par \par \uc2 The blue registered a drop of 22 pesos and showed the first important drop after a week of extreme tension in the exchange market. Thus, the parallel \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  cost 473 pesos, after touching 500 pesos on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, it dropped as low as $467 in the selling segment and finally closed six pesos higher; for purchase it ended at $468. The exchange gap between the parallel and official dollars dropped to 114.4%.\par \par \uc2 The sharp fall of the US \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the illegal market occurred after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BCRA) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on financial dollars, reducing the price of the MEP dollar by 0.20% this Wednesday, to $446.43.\par \par \uc2 To do so, the BCRA used bonds and reserves, as indicated, managing to position the gap in the case of the stock exchange dollar at 101.3%, while the cash with liquidation (CCL) dropped to $458.11 and the spread with the official dollar is at 106.8%.\par \par \uc2 In this way, the national government managed to stop the rise of the blue dollar, which started on April 10 and has been going up since Tuesday of last week. This maneuver meant to violate the agreement with the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  (\uc2 IMF\uc2 ) and to put an end to the main aid available.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020230427ej4r0073m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
