\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Blue dollar, cash with liquidity and MEP: how will they continue after the \uc2 IMF\uc2  relaxation of the reserves target?\b0\par\par\uc2 1,900 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2023\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 A debt swap in pesos that left a bitter taste, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  drain and a more adverse international context make up a more complex scenario that will put upward pressure on the blue dollar and the financial \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded on the stock exchange, Contado con Liquidaci\u243\'00\'F3n and MEP.\par \par \uc2 Furthermore, analysts state that the \uc2 IMF\uc2  communiqu\u233\'00\'E9 stating that \uc2 IMF\uc2  technical staff and the Argentine authorities reached a technical agreement on the fourth review of the current program, for which a disbursement of u$s 5,300 million is expected and the relaxation of the reserves target may "bring some short-term relief, but "it is insufficient" to decompress the exchange rate front" since "the pressure will continue" due to the lack of dollars caused by the drought.\par \par \uc2 Even, some in the market foresee that since \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  committed itself not to use reserves to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  financial dollars -as the \uc2 IMF\uc2  statement says- "this may give more room to continue the upward path".\par \par \uc2 In this context, some analysts believe that the blue dollar could reach the $400 barrier this month, and see an upward path for the CCL, since they estimate that due to the stock of pesos in the economy, the theoretical value of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exceeds the $400 mark by a wide margin.\par \par \uc2 The blue dollar started the week bouncing $4 to close this Monday, March 13, at $377, while the CCL touched $400 during the day but then fell back and ended at $395. The rebound of the informal dollar took place in a day in which the BCRA continued losing foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by registering a negative balance of u$s 87 million due to its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, so that so far this month, the red balance amounts to u$s 404 million.\par \par \uc2 The specialist in finance and agribusiness Salvador Vitelli pointed out that the monetary entity has so far this year net sales for u$s 1,490 million and highlighted that "it is the worst start of the year (with the restriction) in the accumulation of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the BCRA".\par \par \uc2 Regarding the causes of the overheating of free dollars, financial analyst Christian Buteler said that "this is an electoral year and every electoral year the portfolio is dollarized and what better than starting when the dollar is calm, cheap, the rest of the variables moved much more than the dollar, I see it as a natural movement".\par \par \uc2 "Prices were perceived as cheap in the face of a 6% monthly inflation, with a strong issuance of pesos, the rest of the variables were still moving and the dollar was quite still, it was logical that at some point that stillness was going to end", he argued.\par \par \uc2 According to his vision, "what we are seeing is part of the market that, before prices start to rise aggressively, is now starting to dollarize, there are several data that have not been positive, such as the debt swap, last month's fiscal result, the level of activity, which is still weak".\par \par \uc2 The analyst remarked that the fact that the informal dollar "which used to be above the CCL, in the last few days has been trading below that financial \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , is showing that there is money in white that is going to the dollar, there is a greater genuine demand and a great part of that comes from investors who are starting to switch to dollars". Parallel dollars: the international seasoning\par \par \uc2 Economist Natalia Motyl attributed the rise of the blue and the recent rebound of financial dollars to "the bankruptcy of \uc2 Silicon Valley Bank\uc2  in the United States" since "beyond the fact that the FED has come to the rescue of savers, the truth is that it is a negative signal for international markets about the bubble that was generated as a result of the injection of liquidity in 2020".\par \par \uc2 "Today there is some fear of a crash like the one in 2008. In view of this scenario, and given the vulnerability to which our country is subject, capital is taking refuge in safer assets such as the blue dollar", he pointed out.\par \par \uc2 Likewise, Motyl said that "(the head of the FED, \uc2 Jerome) Powell\uc2  anticipated that the monetary policy could be more restrictive to lower the inertial inflation in the USA, which ended up affecting the value of local assets, generating a greater drop in the demand for the peso".\par \par \uc2 In tune, economist Federico Glustein assured that the upward trend of free dollars "is directly related to what is happening in the US and the fall of fintech banks mainly, which also dragged the rest of the banks and financial groups. "The local stock market fell, with bonds trading down, stocks with strong falls and country risk rising more than 4%, therefore, there is a greater demand for the dollar than in other opportunities", he added.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, Vitelli linked the rise of the blue "to the rebound of the MEP and the CCL in the last days" and agreed that "the international context put emerging economies in check, affected bonds that fell sharply, the country risk advanced significantly and that affects dollars". Parallel dollars: can the relaxation of the reserves target calm the exchange rate front?\par \par \uc2 The Government agreed with the \uc2 IMF\uc2  a reduction of almost u$s2,000 million in the international reserves accumulation target for 2023 due to the effect of the drought on exports.\par \par \uc2 Regarding the \uc2 IMF\uc2  communiqu\u233\'00\'E9, Nery Persichini, strategist at GMA Capital evaluated that "when addressing the exchange rate policy, there is no explicit criticism to the exchange rate ceiling or the multiple exchange rates, but now there is an official commitment not to use reserves to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in parallel markets", and he stated that "perhaps the biggest novelty is the request to the IMF Board to relax the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  accumulation goals in order to consider the impact of the drought".\par \par \uc2 When asked if this is enough to decompress the exchange front and calm the parallel dollars, Persichini considered that "not breaking with the \uc2 IMF\uc2  is always good news, but I do not believe that this program will work effectively as an anchor of expectations when the macro continues to be out of alignment every day and when we are entering the electoral prelude".\par \par \uc2 Likewise, Sebasti\u225\'00\'E1n Menescaldi, director of Eco Go, stated that "what it will allow will be to temper the adjustment that should be made in imports (given the drought), to pay the debt to the \uc2 IMF\uc2  and to avoid having to make an exchange rate adjustment".\par \par \uc2 "But the lowering of the reserves target would not be enough to avoid having to continue with the rationalization" of the exchange rate policy by restricting the access to foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  through the SIRAs, and it would be equally insufficient to decompress the exchange rate front and calm the uncertainty". And he highlighted: "let's think that with the drought and the payments to the \uc2 IMF\uc2 , the supply of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would decrease by more than u$s20,000 million".\par \par \uc2 Glustein considered that the announcement of the relaxation of the reserves target may "slow down a little the inclination towards the dollar but we must take into account that due to the drought and the frost there is a lack of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , there is a demand for imports, savings, investment and there are no dollars, the \uc2 IMF\uc2  and its light perspective do not move the market, but how to finance the activity to avoid brakes".\par \par \uc2 In turn, Juan Pablo Albornoz, economist at Invecq argued that "the reduction of net reserves targets was to be expected with the enormous deterioration of the crop expectation of the main export crops, soybean and corn.\par \par \uc2 "On the other hand, according to the communiqu\u233\'00\'E9 \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  committed not to use reserves to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  financial dollars (the buyback). This may give more room for the financials to continue on the upward path, even more so considering that they had been relegated", he predicted.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, Emiliano Anselmi, analyst at PPI stated that the agreement with the \uc2 IMF\uc2  "does not change much" the outlook "because it was something that the market already incorporated", and highlighted that "it is a program that does not anchor anything because they are constantly modifying the goals", so he believes that "it does not contribute to clear the exchange rate front or calm the uncertainty because credibility is already broken". Parallel dollars: will they continue to rise?\par \par \uc2 For Buteler, it is positive "to have an agreement with the \uc2 IMF\uc2  to modify the reserves target, but I do not see that this can stop (the exchange tension) because the lack of dollars is the same, and it is a problem beyond the target, because they are dollars that you need to import, so I do not think that by making this guideline more flexible the (parallel) dollars will stop rising".\par \par \uc2 Glustein foresees that beyond the relaxation of the reserves target, "there is no doubt that the exchange rate pressure will continue because due to the drought approximately u$s 18,000 million will stop coming in, around 3% of the GDP, so the \uc2 IMF\uc2  disbursement allows to temporarily loosen the pressure but it does not fill the gap produced by this natural phenomenon".\par \par \uc2 In this context, Glustein estimated that by the end of the month the CCL "would be close to $400 and the Blue between $380 and $390, but with the demands of importers, of the productive sector itself that demands intermediate goods and with a notorious exchange rate delay, the expectations on the quotations are that they will soon make a small jump to accommodate with the local inflationary context and the lack of reserves".\par \par \uc2 Motyl projected that the blue "this week could exceed $400" while "dollars will continue to rise up to $410-$415 by the end of the month" and listed among the factors that will drive them to "the drought that anticipates a lower inflow of dollars and, therefore, a lower support for the peso, in addition to the higher outflow of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for imports in a context in which the economy has been stagnant for four months".\par \par \uc2 "One estimates that they will facilitate the access to foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the private sector, as in fact has been registered in the last weeks, added to the need to import energy in a time of high temperatures, this hinders the level of reserves and pushes up the demand of dollars for hedging", he said.\par \par \uc2 Likewise, Vitelli affirmed that "many variables show us that the CCL has a certain upward path, especially if the international context does not continue to be supportive". And he specified that "the monetary variables indicate that (the theoretical value) of the CCL would give $460". According to his view: "when the IMF Board formally approves the fourth review of the agreement, US$ 5,300 million would be disbursed, which is undoubtedly a relief for the BCRA, but that is only a quarter of the dollars that will be lost due to the drought, so it may provide some relief, but not much, I do not see it as a factor that may calm uncertainty, it may be short term, but not in the long term".\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020230314ej3e00agh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw94\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1410\pichgoal600
