\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Opposition offensive in Congress against Massa's debt repurchase plan increases\b0\par\par\uc2 1,339 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Januar 2023\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The Minister of Economy, Sergio Massa, is the new target of the opposition in the National Congress. While all eyes are focused on the impeachment trial that the Frente de Todos is promoting against the Supreme Court, a large part of the coalition Juntos por el Cambio (Together for Change) is calling for an investigation and questioning of the leader of the Frente Renovador, after he announced that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will repurchase Argentine foreign debt bonds "for more than one billion dollars".\par \par \uc2 Let us recall that last week the head of the Treasury announced the repurchase of debt securities for u$s1,000 million with the purpose of "continuing to improve the profile of the Argentine foreign debt", lowering the country risk and "improving the possibilities of Argentine companies and the Argentine State to access the capital market". This announcement caused a stir among the opposition leaders, who sowed doubts about Massa's actions.\par \par \uc2 The criticisms to the super minister were so many that hours after the announcement he himself requested the National Securities Commission (CNV) to investigate possible maneuvers in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and securities markets; however, Juntos por el Cambio considers that Massa's requests to the CNV "were very superficial".\par \par \uc2 In that sense, this last week the opposition presented three bills in the National Congress focused on the purchase of bonds and the role of the Minister of Economy. The most recent one entered the lower house on January 24, in which Juntos por el Cambio requested that the investigation for the purchase of bonds be expanded and that a follow-up mechanism be implemented in Congress to guarantee transparency. Debt buyback: inexplicable measure, according to JxC\par \par \uc2 The request was made by a group of JxC legislators, headed by National Deputy Germana Figueroa Casas, who, when presenting the project in Congress, considered that Sergio Massa's measure "was inexplicable from the very beginning".\par \par \uc2 For the opposition, Massa's plan does not match Argentina's economic reality, questioning that "in a context of low reserves of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Minister chose to allocate dollars to an \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  that does not respond to the productive needs of the country".\par \par \uc2 "It is necessary to take a close look at the consequences of the measure", warned Figueroa Casas, who was supported by other opposition figures such as Ricardo Lopez Murphy, Graciela Oca\u241\'00\'F1a, Ricardo Buryaile, Lisandro Nieri, among other legislators. What the opposition is requesting\par \par \uc2 Through a request for information, the deputies of Juntos por el Cambio (Together for Change) requested, among other issues, precise information on the stock exchange guarantees made in the days prior to the announcement. At the same time, they also request that the \uc2 Caja de Valores\uc2  be asked for the movement of bonds to and from abroad and to exchange information with the SEC (\uc2 Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2 ) and FINRA (\uc2 Financial Industry Regulatory Authority\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, they also ask the Ministry of Economy, Sergio Massa, to conduct an internal investigation to determine who had access to the information within the same agency.\par \par \uc2 "Report whether internal investigations have been initiated within the Ministry of Economy to determine whether there were officials or personnel who may have leaked privileged information to operators about the bond repurchase announced by Joint Resolution 1/2023", the text describes.\par \par \uc2 In addition, they requested an explanation as to"why the decision was made to use the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reserves when there were restrictions on access to foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for importers and others". And in another fragment of the project it adds: "Report the results expected when making the announcement prior to the repurchase \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the results obtained".\par \par \uc2 Likewise, the opposition requested that taking into account Sergio Massa's request to the CNV, "to formally invite the parliamentary blocks of the opposition to follow up and become aware of the ongoing investigation and detail the mechanism that will be applied to facilitate such access to the investigation process and reports", and in the same line the opposition added: "Sergio Massa requested the CNV to formally invite the parliamentary blocks of the opposition to follow up the ongoing investigation. This has not yet been implemented, we need to implement a follow-up mechanism urgently to guarantee transparency". They want to question Sergio Massa\par \par \uc2 Another request presented by the opposition in Congress goes directly against Minister Sergio Massa, since they asked Sergio Massa himself to explain the reasons for the repurchase of Argentine securities and to detail the procedure by which the \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be carried out and financed.\par \par \uc2 In the project, they request Massa's presence in Congress to explain:\par \par \uc2 1.What are the reasons for the repurchase of Argentine securities maturing in seven years at a time of maximum scarcity of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reserves and restrictions to the purchase of dollars to be used in the purchase of the necessary inputs for the \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the productive apparatus.\par \par \uc2 2. Describe the procedure to be followed and how the effective \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the resolution will be financed and what will be its costs.\par \par \uc2 3.List the reasons that led you to make an announcement of purchases, instead of making them directly, causing a foreseeable rise in the prices of the same securities that you are now preparing to purchase with public funds.\par \par \uc2 4.State whether you have previously communicated your decision to other members of the Government, the reason for such communications, their dates and the names of such officials.\par \par \uc2 In addition, they ask Massa to clarify if there was any type of communication on his part to financial operators that may have accelerated the purchase of those securities "in the terms punished by the Penal Code (307 to 309) as "'abuse of privileged information'" and in that sense, they demand that he inform if other members of the cabinet were previously aware of the \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In the Senate there are also doubts\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, the Upper House also received a request regarding the repurchase of debt securities announced by Massa. It was the National Senator Juan Carlos Romero (Cambio Federal) who presented an initiative requesting the Government to inform who benefits from the purchase of bonds and the reasons for it.\par \par \uc2 For Romero, the Government "seeks to gain time" by deteriorating and aggravating the vulnerability of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's balance sheet, and denounced that Massa's strategy is nothing more than "a scheme for the election year".\par \par \uc2 As the national legislator does not trust Sergio Massa, he wondered if the announced measure "is it not just a scheme for the election year, a justification that the \uc2 IMF\uc2  can accept, and thus have a mechanism to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the dollar price of \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's external bonds, with which the Country Risk is calculated and with which MEP and CC are made?\par \par \uc2 In turn, the senator argued that since the resources to buy the debt will come directly from a Treasury dollar account, "the vulnerability of the BCRA's balance sheet will be aggravated, in a context of extreme fragility", taking into account that the minimum net reserves barely reach u$s6,000 million; and he reiterated: "is it not a risky \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the country?\par \par \uc2 To argue his request, the opposition senator continued sowing doubts, and in that line, he asked: "What were the reasons to announce, in advance, that the State would go out to buy back debt in dollars for US$ 1 billion (at market value), a decision communicated in advance through a tweet and prior to the reopening of the market?".\par \par \uc2 "The truth is that this seems to be an \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  diagrammed in advance and from which some sectors could have become aware of the announcement and benefited", reflected the senator, who asked to know "not only the fine print" of the \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but also who acquired bonds at a low price in the last three months, detailing name and surname, either legal entities or individuals.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020230128ej1s007d8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
