\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Sergio Massa announced the repurchase of US$ 1 billion of Argentine foreign debt\b0\par\par\uc2 1,436 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Januar 2023\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The announcement was made yesterday morning. What does the move imply and what are the specialists' views. The Minister of Economy, Sergio Massa, announced yesterday that he entrusted the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to "carry out on behalf of the Treasury" a "process of repurchase of Argentine foreign debt for more than US$ 1 billion, which starts today (yesterday)".\par \par \uc2 He said that he made the decision "to improve the debt profile and continue lowering the country risk", and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  is "a first step very focused on global (bonds), especially on short maturities", among which he mentioned those of 2029 and 2030, ignoring the problem of the peso debt maturing in the next months.\par \par \uc2 Massa's announcement - A process of repurchase of the Argentine foreign debt for more than 1 billion dollars was decided.\par \par \uc2 - It is a decision to continue improving Argentina' s external debt profile in order to continue lowering the country risk, which improves the possibilities of Argentine companies and the Argentine State to access the capital market.\par \par \uc2 - This is a first step very focused on the global ones, especially those of short maturity; 2029, 2030. "We understand that this is where we have to attack for the best debt management, the debt profile and the maturity profile of Argentina," said the minister.\par \par \uc2 - "We saw a drop of a thousand points or a little more in Argentina's country risk. That means a window of opportunity for Argentina."\par \par \uc2 - "The fiscal order has very much associated with what concerns liability management. In that sense, throughout 2022, in the last tranche we did a very strong work that was accompanied in the first days of 2023 and today with a new tender of an improvement in the maturity profile of Argentina's peso curve."\par \par \uc2 - "Throughout the last five months we worked very hard on Argentina's macroeconomic normalization so that the process of Product growth, employment generation and increase or recovery of consumption is not affected by those measures to be taken, that we had to take or that we have to take in macroeconomic matters."\par \par \uc2 - "We set four premises at that time : fiscal order, the accumulation of reserves, the increase or growth of Argentine exports and development with inclusion. In that sense, we bet that public investment and private investment will help development with inclusion. We achieved a process of accumulation of reserves from export promotion measures and we also increased and achieved in some sectors such as the automotive or the agricultural sector, record levels of exports."\par \par \uc2 - "The 2022 numbers allowed us to close with compliance and over-compliance of some of the goals; both in the fiscal case and in the case of reserves accumulation."\par \par \uc2 - "For 2023, some of the projections we had have been modified; some that have to do with inclement weather, but also some that have to do with growth in the value of export products or with lower import levels. Such is the case, for example, of the lower levels of energy imports that Argentina will have to make with respect to what was projected in the 2023 Budget".\par \par \uc2 Economists' opinion Gabriel Caama\u241\'00\'F1o, from Ledesma consulting firm, said that the \uc2 National Administration of Social Security (Anses) \uc2 has been buying bonds in dollars for several weeks and that made prices go up 24%, something that kept the gap between the official dollar and the MEP and the cash with liquidation (CCL) at bay.\par \par \uc2 "What is clear is that this is an election year and they are putting together a mechanism that the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  (\uc2 IMF\uc2 ) can accept. A justification that it can accept in order to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  mechanism in the price in dollars of \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's external bonds, with which the Country Risk is calculated and with which MEP and CCL are made. With this mechanism they seek to support the price of those bonds and contain the gaps", he explained.\par \par \uc2 "They are showing the toolbox they have. It is something that Anses has been doing, which is not the same as what the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BCRA) is doing. They are showing the market the tool they have and they are going to seek the Fund's approval. If the \uc2 IMF\uc2  approves it, it is as if they will be able to show that in an election year they have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the parallels", he added.\par \par \uc2 The mechanism is the same one used so many times by \uc2 Mart\u237\'00\'EDn Guzm\u225\'00\'E1n\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, but with much less pomp.\par \par \uc2 For his part, economist Diego Mart\u237\'00\'EDnez Burzaco called the move "intelligent", because it reinforces the good moment of local financial assets. "As a sign, it is auspicious; and they seek to improve access to the markets. But I have the feeling that there is still a long way to go if the final objective is to return to external financing", he said.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, financial analyst Christian Buteler said thatthe repurchase of bonds at such low prices is something positive, although the information may have already been circulated because "it is not for nothing that bonds rose from US$18 to US$30 in the last months".\par \par \uc2 Another point is the issue of financing. "Where are the dollars coming from? From theCentral Bank's net reserves of $6.5 billion. Details are lacking and it sounds optimistic, especially because the BCRA has very few dollars," said economist and FMyA partner Fernando Marull.\par \par \uc2 "The official argument is that it serves to improve the maturity profile, but that does not seem logical: the country has much more imminent problems to deal with something that happens during the next term. So yes, this indirectly aims to lower the gap. The problem is that it is not known how they are going to finance it, because the reserves target in 2022 was met with just enough and there is a very important drought in 2023\u8243\'20\'33, added Francisco Mattig, portfolio manager at Consultatio Plus.\par \par \uc2 Finally, Juan Ignacio Paolicchi, from Empiria Consultores, said that the US$ 1 billion would come from the \uc2 IMF\uc2 's Special Drawing Rights, which would be "risky" with scarce net reserves and drought ahead, although, from the Treasury's point of view, it is logical to buy back bonds at these parities, although it was more reasonable four months ago, when they were worth less than US$ 20.\par \par \uc2 Reactions in networks On the origin of the financing to consummate the repurchase, Marcos Buscaglia was critical. "'Massa desendeuda', pseudo-economists from Kirchner are saying. By buying bonds you do not lower the debt, you change the creditor. To reduce debt you have to have a fiscal surplus, but this government, adding the government and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , had fiscal deficits higher than 10% of GDP per year", he pointed out.\par \par \uc2 Although the market reaction was positive, with a 6% increase in the value of Argentine bonds, some economists were not convinced with the measure published in the Official Gazette, in a joint resolution with the Finance and Treasury Secretariats. "Delirious. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not have dollars to import inputs and they go out to buy foreign debt. With this maneuver do they intend to stop the distrust in the peso?", asked consultant Roberto Cachanosky, who usually expresses himself harshly against the economic policies of \uc2 Alberto Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez\uc2 's administration.\par \par \uc2 Also critical of the Frente de Todos, economist Gustavo L\u225\'00\'E1zzari considered that the liquidity to make the repurchase is going to be obtained through the issue. "We pay with printing what we have to pay with savings", said the liberal, who considered that this is part of campaign measures for this year's presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Dario Epstein, from Research for Traders, listed the positive points that for him this implementation of the Treasury Palace would bring. "My reading of Massa's announcement: it increases the firepower to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  the MEP dollar and the CCL via bond purchases, from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  were limited by the \uc2 IMF\uc2 ; supposedly alternative dollars will go down; the gap would shrink", he enumerated.\par \par \uc2 For his part, \uc2 Mauricio Macri\uc2 's former Minister of Economy Alfonso Prat Gay sowed doubts about the Government's motives to carry out the debt bond buyback announced by Sergio Massa yesterday morning.\par \par \uc2 "It is not understood: weren't the few dollars of the reserves "for production"? It turns out that now they are to "improve the country risk and the maturities...of 2029/30? There are 7 years left to pay them! Let's hope that no official has bought those securities recently...", wrote Prat Gay.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020230119ej1j004nx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
