\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Argentine market closes the year with active role of the  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  and stock market as star performer\b0\par\par\uc2 527 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Dezember 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Dec 30 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's financial market ended 2022 with an active \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BCRA), to reinforce its reserves, and the Buenos Aires stock exchange standing out among the most important rises at a global level in dollars for hedging against the repeated devaluation of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Typical year-end round, portfolios are offset and positions are released to start 2023, liquidity is controlled and only what is necessary is done", summarized a banking agent.\par \par \uc2 The BCRA accumulates 1,853 million dollars as December balance until Thursday, while in the year it adds purchases for 5,690 million dollars against 5,524 million dollars in 2021.\par \par \uc2 For its part, the stock market is up 143% in the year and yields around 33% in dollars, which makes it one of the world's best-returning investments.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Treasury surprised investors with the call for a debt swap in pesos with the beginning of 2023 under the objective of clearing the way in the next first quarter. It is an exchange of eight securities for two baskets composed of either 'Ledes' bills or 'Duals' bonds.\par \par \uc2 * The wholesale peso devaluated 0.18% to 177.11/177.12 units with the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the BCRA, which recognizes soybean exporters a differential exchange rate of 230 pesos per dollar sold until this Friday, although there will be pending \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  committed for next Monday and Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 * The national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dragged a fall of 5.5% in the month and its loss climbed to 42% in the year, also far from a retail inflation that will accumulate a level close to 100% in the last 12 months, a differential that worries investors due to the exchange rate delay.\par \par \uc2 * The peso in the influential marginal or "blue" circuit rose to 347 per dollar, after marking a historic low of 359 units on Wednesday. The market devalued 9.5% in the month and lost 40.1% in the course of 2022 with a gap of 95.9% with the official parity.\par \par \uc2 * In other official alternative markets for the usual dollar hedging, the peso fell to 334.6 units in the stock market "contado con liquidaci\u243\'00\'F3n" (CCL) and rose to 332.9 units in the "d\u243\'00\'F3lar MEP".\par \par \uc2 * The benchmark S&P; Merval index of the Buenos Aires stock exchange fell by 1.4% due to profit taking, to 196,580.46 points at 12:30 local time (1530 GMT), after reaching its intraday record at 205,953.37 units in the previous session. In December, this benchmark is up 16.6%.\par \par \uc2 * Over-the-counter debt averaged a 0.4% retracement on short-covering earnings, with \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2 's country risk down slightly by two basis points to 2,160 units. Bonds posted a 5.5% gain in December.\par \par \uc2 * The complexity of the Argentine economy led the country risk to climb to almost a record high of 3,000 points at the end of July, prior to Sergio Massa's inauguration at the head of the Ministry of Economy.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020221230eicu00fdt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
