\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Argentina strikes $5 bln China  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  swap extension\b0\par\par\uc2 323 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 November 2022\par 19:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds comments from Argentina's president, background details)\par \par \uc2 By Eliana Raszewski\par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Nov 15 (Reuters) - Argentina has agreed to expand its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap deal with China by $5 billion, the South American country's President \uc2 Alberto Fernandez\uc2  said on Tuesday, a move that would give it more firepower to defend the embattled local peso.\par \par \uc2 Argentina's government needs to rebuild depleted foreign reserves to cover trade costs and future debt repayments. Rebuilding reserves is also a key objective of a major debt deal with the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  (\uc2 IMF\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 "Today President Xi (Jinping) informed us that he authorized the Chinese government to make 35 billion yuan, meaning $5 billion, freely available to Argentina," Fernandez said after meeting Xi at the \uc2 Group of 20\uc2  (G20) summit in Bali.\par \par \uc2 China is Argentina's second biggest trade partner and the second most important destination for Argentine exports.\par \par \uc2 Argentine Economy Minister Sergio Massa added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap will give the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  more foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange market and strengthen the peso.\par \par \uc2 Despite strict capital controls, Argentina's foreign reserves have fallen due to strong demand for dollars, both from importers and savers looking to buffer themselves from inflation expected to reach 100% this year.\par \par \uc2 Even with daily \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso has weakened close to 40% versus the U.S. dollar so far this year in the official market. In popular alternative markets in Argentina, the peso is far weaker.\par \par \uc2 Xi said China will deepen cooperation with Argentina in areas including agriculture, energy, infrastructure and aviation, state broadcaster CCTV said.\par \par \uc2 Massa projected that Argentina will have an $8 billion trade deficit with China in 2022. ($1 = 7.0440 Chinese yuan renminbi) (Reporting by Eliana Raszewski and Maximilian Heath; Additional reporting by Jorge Otaola; Writing by Anthony Esposito and Adam Jourdan) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-11-15T19:24:21.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020221115eibf046m9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
