\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 The dollar card is already in force for foreign tourists arriving in Argentina.\b0\par\par\uc2 385 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 November 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Tourists from abroad visiting Argentina and spending with credit cards will be able to access as from Friday the MEP dollar exchange rate, which on Thursday closed at $ 293, instead of the retail rate of $ 158, with which they operated until now, in order to facilitate their \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  and prevent them from exchanging their bills for cash in the informal market.\par \par \uc2 As informed by the BCRA through Communication "A" 7630, the measure exempts payments made by "non-residents by means of debit, credit, purchase or prepaid cards issued abroad" from the settlement in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 Among them are included the charges for any type of tourist service in the country contracted by non-residents, including those contracted through wholesale or retail travel and tourism agencies in the country, as well as the charges for non-resident passenger transportation services with destination in the country by land, air or water.\par \par \uc2 According to official sources explained to T\u233\'00\'E9lam, the procedure implies that the dollars with which tourists pay will be exchanged into pesos through the financial market and then they will pay in pesos to the businesses or services with the MEP dollar exchange rate calculated "with the most liquid bonds".\par \par \uc2 "Until today, the \uc2 Banco Naci\u243\'00\'F3n\uc2  exchange rate was used. The card companies will be able to charge a commission for such \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 ", explained the sources, since it is not the banks that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the expenses of foreigners in \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but the card companies.\par \par \uc2 Although it will not be mandatory for card companies to offer this service, those that do are obliged to settle the dollars through the MEP dollar.\par \par \uc2 The latter is a key factor, since MEP dollar \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  -unlike those of cash settlement- imply that the person or entity that buys those dollars through the stock market \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  then deposits them in a bank in Argentina, through its broker.\par \par \uc2 In this sense, although the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will no longer receive the dollars that entered the country through the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, they will be used to increase the gross reserves, since part of the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that enters the country will be part of the reserve requirements of the dollar deposits in the sellers' accounts.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020221104eib4009f1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw77\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1155\pichgoal600
