\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Qatar, dollars and the difficult figurines in Massa's album\b0\par\par\uc2 740 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 September 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Eyes widened, eyebrows raised. Lionel Scaloni, the head coach of the Argentine national soccer team, did not spare any gestures.\par \par \uc2 Journalist Elizabeth Perez, from CNN en Espanol, was asking him about how he manages the expectations generated by the team. "There is a topic that seems superficial, but in Argentina it is like a state issue, and that is the Panini album, which is out of stock," Perez mentioned.\par \par \uc2 The episode occurred days after the publication of an official photo, to testify a two-hour meeting arranged by the Secretary of Commerce, Mat\u237\'00\'EDas Tombolini, who together with officials of his area assumed the unusual role of mediator between the Union of Newsstand owners (Ukra) and executives of New Rita, the company that manages Panini \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It is difficult not to hear in this \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  the music of bread and circuses or the noise caused by the disconnection with the deep needs and urgencies.\par \par \uc2 The problem of supply and demand of figurines due to the World Cup in Qatar, in addition to multiplying the shortage of this product, to stress the nerves in the distribution chain and to generate frustration among consumers, was immediately translated into prices, with increases and a brutal dispersion.\par \par \uc2 The distortion is one more of the many that have colonized an economy beset by high inflation and lack of dollars. The thermometers are broken. Setting the price of a good or a service has become a chimera of discretion.\par \par \uc2 Everything increases, but people find it difficult to discern whether what they are paying for is expensive, very expensive or relatively cheap if they advance the purchase.\par \par \uc2 From the "soybean dollar" to the "soybean trap".The Qatar effect is not only in the form of a figurine. It is also beginning to be the symbol of the dollars that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BCRA) gives for tourism expenses abroad.\par \par \uc2 The competition will start in less than 60 days, and the issue is flying over all the conversations of the productive sectors, which are asking for priority in the use of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for inputs to be purchased abroad.\par \par \uc2 The Government, which extended the import limitations until the end of the year, responds with promises. It is aware of the fleeting nature of the new balance achieved with the "soy dollar".\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which implied a fiscal effort (the difference of buying dollars at 200 pesos to sell them later at 140), has already exceeded the goal of five billion dollars. The subway cost of this unprecedented result was exacerbated by the "soybean clamp".\par \par \uc2 The versions that explain the reasons why the BCRA restricted access to dollars to those who sold beans at the differential rate range from malpractice to an alleged intention to grind down the Minister of Economy, Sergio Massa.\par \par \uc2 In any case, the message exposed the precariousness and left floating the suspicion of an untidy ambush to the sector that has a decisive participation in the contribution of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 That the effect can be seen today in the rise of the "cash with liquidation" dollar rate may seem a movement far from the real economy, but it stretches the exchange rate gap and, therefore, increases the devaluation pressure.\par \par \uc2 There is a clear and deliberate objective: to close as many doors and windows as possible so that pesos are not converted into dollars, and to stretch as much as possible this temporary umbrella that is giving oxygen to the BCRA to recover reserves. But the stock is one thing and the flow is another.\par \par \uc2 What will happen when the "soy dollar" window closes on the last day of September? The Government assures that there will be no extension or discretionary devaluation.\par \par \uc2 There is a rumor of a probable exchange rate split that would affect the "tourist dollar" or "card" and that could even affect the "savings dollar". But nobody takes charge of the rumor.\par \par \uc2 The economic team is asking for time. In the meeting with industrialists, Massa slipped that they are working on a plan to cut inflationary inertia. The relationship between price increases and mini-devaluations is like a merry-go-round that is spinning faster and faster.\par \par \uc2 Although no one in the Government is thinking of an abrupt brake, there is an urgent need to slow down. Nothing good can come out of an economy dizzy to the point of fainting.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220924ei9o009zc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
