\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Daniel Marx, the architect of the "shielding", is back: will he be looking for a "cushion" of dollars as in 2000?\b0\par\par\uc2 1,057 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 August 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Of the many names that Sergio Massa chose to accompany him in the economic management, possibly the most surprising was that of Daniel Marx. He was one of the great protagonists of the '90s: he led the renegotiation of the debt through the Brady Plan at the beginning of that decade and then in 2000 he was the architect of the "blindaje", a cushion of USD 40 billion that was not enough to save the Convertibility.\par \par \uc2 The appointment of Marx marks the pragmatic tone that Massa wants to give to his administration, almost totally stripped of ideological considerations. He is possibly the first official who held a high position in Domingo Cavallo's administration at the head of the Ministry of Economy to join a Kirchnerist government. Massa did not even care that Marx's name was linked to the long-criticized "megacanje" of 2001 by Kirchnerism. That \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  sought to exchange short term debt for long term bonds but with higher interest rates in dollars. But the crisis was already unleashed and a few months later the "1 to 1" debacle occurred.\par \par \uc2 The exception may have been Mart\u237\'00\'EDn Redrado, who was president of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  during part of N\u233\'00\'E9stor and then \uc2 Cristina Kirchner\uc2 's administration. In the government of Carlos Menem he had occupied a second rank role as president of the National Securities Commission. His name was vetoed on several occasions by the Vice President.\par \par \uc2 The return of Daniel Marx to executive management is a strong sign of Sergio Massa's pragmatism, who is seeking a better approach to Wall Street investors and international organizations. He has the very difficult task of raising fresh funds to strengthen the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reserves.\par \par \uc2 The former Secretary of Finance will be in charge of strengthening the level of reserves, managing the debt and encouraging the growth of the local capital market. Clearly, the urgency is to give more support to the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and to obtain the necessary dollars for this purpose.\par \par \uc2 The option of something similar to a "shielding" as the one of a little more than 20 years ago seems very far away. On that occasion, there were strong contributions from multilateral organizations, which today are not available beyond the \uc2 IMF\uc2  disbursements to repay its own debt. Then international banks and even the Spanish government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 . With \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  falling into total disrepute and most investors seeing it in default again, these fresh money options would be extremely difficult to obtain.\par \par \uc2 Massa let it be known that he would add Qatar as a destination for his first international trip, an addition to the typical meetings in Washington, New York and a couple of European capitals. The search for investments from Arab sovereign wealth funds is an open option, but for now it also seems somewhat distant.\par \par \uc2 Mauricio Macri\uc2  tried it in 2018, when he received the presence of important officials from that country. However, he did not manage to materialize a single investment. Chancellor Santiago Cafiero also tried when he traveled to Dubai, which manages another billionaire state investment fund. But as it happened to Macri, he also came back empty-handed.\par \par \uc2 Will there be something to offer that particularly interests the Arabs? The investments of that origin today are directed to hotels and especially to large extensions of land in the south of Argentina. However, the risks of "sinking" money in Argentina are very high, which explains the reluctance of millionaire sovereign wealth funds such as those of Qatar, Dubai and other countries to disembark in the country.\par \par \uc2 Another option that has been circulated, but without official confirmation, is the negotiation of a "repo" with international banks. The problem is that the guarantee of fresh dollars that the entities may provide would be Argentine bonds with default value, i.e. very unattractive and hardly applicable as collateral.\par \par \uc2 The option of something similar to a "blindaje" as the one of a little more than 20 years ago seems very far away. On that occasion, there were strong contributions from multilateral organizations, which today are not available beyond the \uc2 IMF\uc2  disbursements to repay its own debt.\par \par \uc2 Beyond the possibility of getting fresh money, it is clear that Marx brings a wealth of experience in debt management issues, including restructuring plans. He also has important international contacts in Washington and Wall Street, although clearly the interlocutors today are different from those of 20 or 30 years ago. However, he continued to be linked to the New York market through his advice to private companies that in recent years have carried out bond and stock placements or even debt renegotiations with the private sector.\par \par \uc2 With Leonardo Madcur as chief advisor to the Ministry of Economy, Massa makes it clear that Roberto Lavagna's stamp will be behind the future measures to be adopted. Madcur occupied a key position during the administration of the former Minister of Economy until 2005, in the last years he worked in the private sector and he is also the son-in-law of \uc2 Guillermo Nielsen\uc2 , currently ambassador in Saudi Arabia and who was also mentioned as a possible member of the new economic team.\par \par \uc2 Another key appointment is that of Lisandro Cleri, who used to work at the Sustainability Guarantee Fund and will move to the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . This means that Massa was able to keep a key chair in the institution, despite the fact that the BCRA did not figure in the offensive he took to the Economy. It is now clear that he will also have a say in the management of key issues such as \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , interest rate management and bond trading. These are all central issues in the midst of the critical financial situation Argentina's economy is going through.\par \par \uc2 Why Argentina's country risk is close to 3,000 points and rises much more than in the rest of the region.\par \par \uc2 IMF\uc2  warning on Argentine inflation: "Lowering it must be the main priority".\par \par \uc2 Miguel Pesce\uc2 , President of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 : "We expect to obtain USD 2,500 million, it is a possible figure".\par \par \uc2 How much will the soybean producer receive for the harvest with the new measure of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220802ei820039v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
