\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Dollar: financial guru anticipates the next movements in the price of the dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 836 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juli 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 A week of high tension began in the financial market, with the blue dollar reaching its intraday nominal record high of $350 on Friday, but still closing at high levels. However, after an agitated week, the parallel dollar dropped $16 and closed at $322.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the financial dollars managed to stop the escalation after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to include the holding of Argentine Certificates of Deposit (Cedears) in the limit of availability of 100,000 dollars that companies accessing the official \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market can have.\par \par \uc2 Within this framework, the city started a new week amid rumors that encourage speculation and uncertainty. The Government resumed talks and new measures are expected.\par \par \uc2 In this context, Salvador Di St\u233\'00\'E9fano in his weekly report predicted what is expected for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week.\par \par \uc2 Follow the price of the blue, official, CCL and MEP dollar in \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market will cause sales of financial assets to take place, which could push back the stock market dollar or MEP and the spot with liquidation. This added to the fact that we are at the end of the month, sales in stores were not very good and companies need to finance working capital", began Di St\u233\'00\'E9fano announcing that perhaps, the volatility of the dollar could ease this week.\par \par \uc2 In that sense, the analyst recommended what to do with savings. "Personally I do not recommend selling dollars, it is the last thing I would do, in this instance I prefer that you take bank financing. The rates in the market are around 60% per annum, it is a forward rate lower than inflation, which could be around 90% per annum. I would exhaust all instances in order not to sell any type of merchandise, including dollars, I would first take financing since the rates are negative against inflation", he said.\par \par \uc2 "At current prices I sell dollars and keep merchandise. I believe that merchandise is a scarce commodity, and therefore I prefer to hold stock and not dollars and bills. Buying merchandise is the best business in the medium term," he said.\par \par \uc2 "We have a severe monetary policy problem, the State \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the peso market and lowered interest rates too much, this does not make these instruments attractive, therefore, economic agents remain positioned in dollars. The ghost train invites citizens to stay in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and omit investments in local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ", he analyzed.\par \par \uc2 The economist assured that in order to revert this scenario "the rate of increase of the wholesale exchange rate and the interest rate should be higher than the inflation rate. But this recipe is not in the DNA of this government. There is no way to discipline the market at this juncture. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not have dollars, therefore, it cannot offer dollars to lower the exchange rate gap that stands at 160% if measured with the blue dollar."\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  at this juncture has two tools, on the one hand, the interest rate and on the other hand, the possibility of increasing the wholesale exchange rate. We believe that sooner or later the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will have to abandon the ghost train and generate incentives for investors to seek to position themselves in the peso market. To give a signal of confidence, the government should show that it can lower the fiscal deficit and manage to increase the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reserves. If none of this happens, the market will continue to bet on the dollar and the forecasts of a dollar at $ 400 by the end of the year will become a reality, as well as inflation above 90% per year", he concluded.\par \par \uc2 Short-term outlook A recent Ecolatina report focused on what the next weeks will be like for the Ministry of Economy: "We are in the presence of a scenario of greater fiscal austerity going forward: without a relevant margin to finance itself with Transitional Advances (even breaching the targets with the \uc2 IMF\uc2 ), the financial program will continue to rely heavily on debt biddings. For this reason, normalizing the financial front as soon as possible becomes even more important, and we will surely see interest rate hikes, which have been postponed."\par \par \uc2 "Finally, even if the economic program is put back on track (the BCRA accumulates reserves again and devaluation expectations are deactivated) the second half of the year will be one of higher inflation, lower activity and tighter fiscal limits than the first, indicating that the financial/political/social balance will continue to be unstable. With little time to make fundamental corrections that will yield positive results, but with still too much time to repress costs, the current financial crisis is forcing the Government to stop prioritizing profit maximization and focus on cost minimization. And avoiding a devaluation of the official dollar will be at the top of the list of priorities in the coming days", the report added.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220726ei7q009nc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
