\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 For the Fed, Argentina could not withstand another rate hike\b0\par\par\uc2 348 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juli 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The future for the world economy does not look promising with the sharp increase in global prices. For this reason, the \uc2 United States Federal Reserve\uc2  (FED) is seeking to curb the increase in prices by raising interest rates. However, a recent report warned that Argentina would not be able to withstand the impact this measure would have on its economy.\par \par \uc2 Published by the \uc2 Dallas Fed\uc2 , the document makes a survey of the most important emerging markets and compares them to their situation before the so-called"Tequila effect", an economic crisis that occurred during 1994 in Mexico after the United States abruptly raised interest rates.\par \par \uc2 In this sense, the report evaluates the capacity of emerging economies to face the rapid interest rate increases that the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could implement in the coming months to alleviate record inflation, even at the cost of generating a recession.\par \par \uc2 For this reason, in order to withstand these potentially damaging measures for emerging markets, countries must have high government reserves and low current account deficits, qualities that Argentina currently lacks.\par \par \uc2 Among the 13 emerging market countries examined in the paper, Argentina is one of the few that does not meet the requirements set by the Fed:"Reserve adequacy is negative only in Turkey and Argentina, with their low stocks of reserves and high amounts of short-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt," he explained.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves So far in July, the Banco de la Rep\u250\'00\'FAblica \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  maintains a negative net balance due to its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in the order of 641 million dollars. With these numbers, gross international reserves fell USD 273 million and ended at USD 40,131 million this Friday.\par \par \uc2 So far in 2022, the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  has accumulated net purchases in the wholesale market for about USD 1,201 million, an amount that represents 16.3% of the net balance in favor obtained in the same period last year, which accumulated about USD 7,350 million as of July 15, 2021.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220717ei7h005tr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
