\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 When did we start talking about 'country risk'? When Mingo dreamed of a 1 to 1 exit and the euro.\b0\par\par\uc2 879 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juli 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 "Let's go with the euro".\par \par \uc2 February 2001. Closed meeting at the \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2  tower in Manhattan. Domingo Cavallo told a group of investors that the time had come to modify the 1 peso = 1 dollar ratio (Convertibility) in Argentina. And that the current legal scheme had to take into account the price of another \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , besides the dollar. "The Euro".\par \par \uc2 The market took the news in the best way.\par \par \uc2 The 'danger' for Argentina in those days was not a depreciation of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as it had happened in other experiences. Rather, it was whether the country had the dollars to repay its debts without the possibility of devaluation. And Cavallo thought that if the peso floated between two bands (euro and dollar), well, the chances of repayment improved because the peso was too appreciated. Ergo, there was a risk of default.\par \par \uc2 The traffic light that measured this fear was none other than the difference between the yield on ten-year bonds of a \uc2 US Treasury\uc2  security and one of Argentina. It was 900 points at the beginning of 2001. We started to talk about country risk.\par \par \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2  analysts wrote down the words of the then former Minister of Economy in a memo to their clients. The terror began.\par \par \uc2 Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Luis Machinea was the Minister of Economy at that time. A few weeks later he left. Ricardo L\u243\'00\'F3pez Murphy arrived, who also left soon after, and Cavallo arrived with his euro idea under his arm.\par \par \uc2 "The dollar was very expensive," he once explained.\par \par \uc2 At that time, 90 cents of a dollar was received for each euro. In 2008 that ratio reached 1.5. This week it went back down to 1 to 1. Today there is again talk of a strong dollar.\par \par \uc2 "We were in the midst of a financial crisis in 2001 - recalled Cavallo to Econ\u243\'00\'F3mico -, expectations among bondholders and depositors were of doubts about the economy's repayment capacity".\par \par \uc2 Within a month, in April 2001, Cavallo made a road show with his euro idea. It was even before the bill to extend convertibility was sent to Congress and passed in the Senate (June). He was accompanied on his tour by his team: economists Daniel Marx, Guillermo Mondino and Federico Sturzenegger.\par \par \uc2 Marx, who was negotiating with the creditors, watched from the trenches how the noise of the proposal to extend convertibility caused the country risk and market fears to rise.\par \par \uc2 The first stop on that road show was a 22-story building in Manhattan, very close to the \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2  building where he had gone in January. Cavallo had breakfast at 33 Liberty Street, in the Federal Reserve building, with its president, William McDonough, and about fifteen other bankers, including William Rhodes, from Citibank. Between coffee and fruit salad, he told them about his idea of modifying convertibility by introducing the euro and explained why this would be beneficial for \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Those present took note without commenting.\par \par \uc2 His second \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  took place at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Monetary Days in April 2001. He participated in a round table called "The Finance Ministers of Convertibility". He had just landed from the US.\par \par \uc2 Machinea, Roque Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez and L\u243\'00\'F3pez Murphy were sitting there. Cavallo entered walking down the middle of an aisle and stepping on a red carpet, just like a leader. After listening to them and telling them that "they had not understood convertibility", he explained his idea of the euro. "If that had been the Argentine monetary system at the end of 1993, this crisis of fruit production and regional economies would not have occurred or its impact would have been much less".\par \par \uc2 Finally, Cavallo flew to London. When he arrived, he read that the \uc2 Financial Times\uc2  and The Economist, two of the three most prestigious economic publications in the world, claimed that Cavallo wanted to modify the only element that gave stability to the Argentine economy and that it would be a mistake: the introduction of the Euro.\par \par \uc2 Cavallo requested a car and traveled to the FT editorial office, then located in London Bridge. He talked to the editors of the newspaper about why it was a good idea to introduce the euro into the convertibility. The Financial Times published a column of his the next day in which he defended his position and answered the critics.\par \par \uc2 The country risk had already crossed 1,000 basis points. Argentina surpassed Turkey and Brazil for the first time. " The markets do not understand neither the policy nor the real economy of Argentina", said Cavallo in London.\par \par \uc2 In those days, on April 19, 2001, N\u233\'00\'E9stor Kirchner announced his candidacy for president in 2003. It was at the Unione e Benevolenza club. In the front row were \uc2 Alberto Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez\uc2  and \uc2 Cristina Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez\uc2 . Kirchner was in favor of 1 to 1.\par \par \uc2 The euro finally reached 1 to 1 as Cavallo thought. But it happened two years later. "Trichet told me that the euro was going to appreciate," Machinea recounted some time later. \uc2 Jean-Claude Trichet\uc2  was then president of the \uc2 French \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . And a couple of years later, he would become president of the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220716ei7g005fy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
