\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 How import controls affect Argentineans\b0\par\par\uc2 1,145 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juli 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (AP) - What do a toilet paper manufacturer, a veterinarian, a coffee shop owner and a sushi chef have in common in Argentina? The dollar or, rather, the headaches they suffer to get it.\par \par \uc2 The dollar shortage is a long-standing problem in the country and is associated with Argentines' distrust of their own \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to successive crises, especially in periods of accelerated inflation and political instability such as the current one.\par \par \uc2 In order to preserve purchasing power, citizens save in that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while companies and investors dollarize their profits. The problem is that now there are no dollars for everyone.\par \par \uc2 With restrictions already in place to buy dollars for savings or travel, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  limited in June the use of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for imports, a measure that is hurting industry, causing product shortages and price increases that are pushing the country dangerously towards triple-digit annual inflation.\par \par \uc2 Daniel Rosato manufactures toilet and kitchen paper at a plant located in a southern suburb of Buenos Aires and employing 140 people. Its production is affected by difficulties in importing cellulose, which is already in short supply because of the war in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 "We have been warning that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has the power to allow who is going to import and who is not and to put limits on imports. And that is not normal. We knew it was going to generate problems of shortages," the 61-year-old businessman told The Associated Press. "If it doesn't improve, we know that these restrictions are going to fall into a recessionary process."\par \par \uc2 The official resolution was taken after the increase in the index that measures the risk of Argentina's debt bonds and a dollar that soared in the informal exchange market due to distrust in the government.\par \par \uc2 The background is the fight between President \uc2 Alberto Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez\uc2  and his powerful vice-president and former president \uc2 Cristina Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez de Kirchner\uc2  (2007-2015) over the direction of the economy.\par \par \uc2 This dispute led to the resignation of the minister of the area, \uc2 Mart\u237\'00\'EDn Guzm\u225\'00\'E1n\uc2 , who is close to the president, and his replacement by Silvina Batakis, a heterodox economist closer to Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez de Kirchner's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventionist\b0 \highlight\uc2  vision.\par \par \uc2 In practice, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulates \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign trade since it decides, according to criteria of invoicing and importance of the input, among others, how many dollars it releases to importers and in what term.\par \par \uc2 Importers who have access to these bills pay 130 pesos per dollar. If they do not have the approval of the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they are forced to resort to the so-called dollar with settlement, a legal mechanism through which they can obtain foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by buying shares or debt securities. The problem is its price: 300 pesos per unit. This difference in price makes the input more expensive, reduces production and, as a domino effect, causes supply problems.\par \par \uc2 Coffee is another raw material that Argentina imports in its entirety, with an average consumption of one kilo per capita per year. Seventy percent of Argentines have coffee for breakfast.\par \par \uc2 "Coffee is a commodity that rose 120% in the last year and a half. By giving us quotas in dollars, we bought less coffee for the same dollars... today we are working with the stock at the limit," detailed Mart\u237\'00\'EDn Cabrales, vice-president of the family company Caf\u233\'00\'E9 Cabrales. "There have been problems (in the past), but with these high restrictions never."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's mistrust with dollars responds on the one hand to a commitment assumed by the South American country to accumulate some 5.8 billion dollars in reserves as part of the agreement signed with the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  (\uc2 IMF\uc2 ) in March to renegotiate a debt of 45 billion dollars. And on the other hand, to prioritize energy imports in winter.\par \par \uc2 The economic analyst Marcelo Elizondo, specialized in international trade, said that "the restrictions are basically a way to contain the rise in the exchange rate so that this does not affect the inflation rate".\par \par \uc2 "Clearly the economy is very affected, companies with several problems, limits to the access of capital... on the other hand, by aggravating this regime that everyone considers unsustainable and by widening the exchange rate gap, there is an enormous fear among the economic actors that at some point this system must be changed and inflation will accelerate", indicated the director of the consulting firm DNI.\par \par \uc2 Analysts forecast that an acceleration of inflation in July will be inevitable, among other reasons, due to the impact of import restrictions. June inflation was 5.3% and accumulates almost 36.2% so far this year.\par \par \uc2 A \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  survey in June raised the inflation projection for this year to almost 80%.\par \par \uc2 Juan Pablo Ravazzano, president of the Argentine Chamber of Animal Nutrition Companies (CAENA), said that since two weeks ago "micro ingredients" -vitamins, minerals and amino acids, among others- essential in the animals' diet cannot be imported.\par \par \uc2 "They took out a regulation where they are prohibiting you from paying for what the same State had allowed you 15, 20 days ago," he lamented. "It never happened to us, I have been in this industry for 20 years and we have gone through critical times with previous governments... but not even in those moments did we have this situation."\par \par \uc2 CAENA said that in less than a month there will be a shortage of pet food in veterinaries and that in the longer term this will cause an increase in animal mortality.\par \par \uc2 The family-owned metallurgical company Metalcrom produces parts for agricultural machinery and the oil sector with imported steel bars and valves. A supplier in Italy already warned it that it is not willing to wait the 180 days, the deadline set by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to release the dollars.\par \par \uc2 "There is no supplier in the world that will lend to Argentina for 180 days", said its owner, Alejandro Bartalini, 61 years old. He regretted that the industry "came out of the pandemic very well, with a 10% growth, but these restriction measures due to the lack of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  may bring a decline in the growth of production. Today we are working at 80, 90% of the productive capacity".\par \par \uc2 As in so many other economic crises throughout their history, Argentines have resorted to ingenuity to get out of the crisis.\par \par \uc2 Chef Sergio Asato, of Japanese descent, is the owner of the Social Sushi Izakaya restaurant, specializing in sushi. Salmon, the main ingredient of the menu, is imported mainly from Chile and in the last week its price increased 100%.\par \par \uc2 As it is impossible to transfer this cost to the final price and for fear of closing the restaurant, Asato and other gastronomes agreed to offer sushi with local fish varieties such as sea bass, trout, silverside and mackerel, among others.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220715ei7f0045k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
