\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 The Financial Times described Batakis as "a relatively unknown former provincial official".\b0\par\par\uc2 670 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juli 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The Financial Times stated that "Argentina has appointed a relatively unknown former provincial official as its new finance minister, following the abrupt departure of her predecessor, \uc2 Martin Guzman\uc2 , who negotiated a $44 billion debt restructuring deal with the \uc2 IMF\uc2 ".\par \par \uc2 The FT highlighted that the official replaces a close ally of President \uc2 Alberto Fernandez\uc2 . "Deep divisions within Argentina's ruling leftist coalition have pitted the country's powerful vice president and former leader, \uc2 Cristina Fernandez de Kirchner\uc2 , against the president, just as Argentina's economic woes worsen," it noted.\par \par \uc2 "Financial analysts noted that the appointment of Batakis, a former economy minister of Buenos Aires province who recently worked at the Interior Ministry, will do little to calm negative market sentiment, given her ties to the more radical wing of the Peronist government allied with Fernandez de Kirchner," he clarified.\par \par \uc2 "Market reaction on Monday was subdued due to the 4th of July holiday in the United States, where Argentine bonds are most frequently traded. Argentina's official \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is kept artificially high in an attempt to control inflation, weakened 0.5 percent to 126 pesos to 1 dollar. The parallel exchange rate widened by almost 15 percent in early trading to 280 pesos to 1 dollar," he said.\par \par \uc2 "The market was already fragile and now it's going to be terrified," Riccardo Grassi, head of risk management at Swiss-based hedge fund Mangart Capital Advisors, which participated in the Guzman-led debt restructuring in 2020, told the FT.\par \par \uc2 The market was already fragile and now it's going to be terrified," said Riccardo Grassi, head of risk management at the Switzerland-based hedge fund.\par \par \uc2 On Batakis' appointment, economist Fernando Marull assured that markets "will take it badly" and added: "She is not well known... and our most pessimistic scenario for the economy now seems more likely."\par \par \uc2 As indicated "Batakis is a career civil servant who, as Minister of Economy of the province of Buenos Aires between 2011 and 2015, defended price controls, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the markets and the increase in the estate and inheritance tax."\par \par \uc2 In addition, the article noted that "Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez de Kirchner and her allies have repeatedly criticized the agreement with the \uc2 IMF\uc2 , in which Guzm\u225\'00\'E1n served as an intermediary, and have called for higher spending and greater government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to combat inflation and poverty."\par \par \uc2 Deepening crisis\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  is mired in a worsening economic crisis, with inflation forecast to exceed 70% this year. Its sovereign bonds have traded at deeply distressing levels, hovering just 20 cents on the dollar. Pressure on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is mounting despite exchange controls, and a costly energy import bill is preventing Buenos Aires from accumulating dollar reserves," the FT stressed.\par \par \uc2 "Guzman's departure after more than two years in office is a further blow to the president, whose popularity ratings have plummeted."\par \par \uc2 William Jackson\uc2 , chief emerging markets economist at \uc2 Capital Economics\uc2 , pointed out to the English medium that Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez de Kirchner's growing influence could move Argentina "away from the path of macroeconomic stability", and that "a sovereign default is starting to become increasingly likely".\par \par \uc2 In addition, it was noted that "it is unclear whether further cabinet changes are foreseen. \uc2 Miguel Angel Pesce\uc2 , head of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , confirmed on Sunday that he expected to remain in his post."\par \par \uc2 "Pesce and the new finance minister pledged Monday to pursue a sustainable fiscal program, aiming to address investor concerns following Guzman's resignation. Batakis and Pesce shared the importance of continuing to work on a sustainable fiscal program and the accumulation of reserves," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement, adding that both also agreed on the need to strengthen local capital markets." it concluded.\par \par \uc2 Silvina Batakis met with \uc2 Mart\u237\'00\'EDn Guzm\u225\'00\'E1n\uc2  to order the transition at the Ministry of Economy\par \par \uc2 Dollar today: free quotation rose to $260 after changes in the Ministry of Economy\par \par \uc2 Increases, lack of reference prices and paralyzed sales: trade suffers due to economic uncertainty\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220704ei7400aqq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
