\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Argentine bonds close June with heavy losses,  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  manages to consolidate reserves\b0\par\par\uc2 676 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Juni 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Jun 30 (Reuters) - Argentina's bonds closed June with a significant drop of 13% on average, leading the general weakness of the market, only recovering on Thursday due to speculative buybacks in an environment affected by the growing uncertainty about the local and external economic future.\par \par \uc2 The economy of the South American country suffers a galloping inflation that would be around 35% in the semester and would rise above 75% in the year, in a context of exchange rate hedge and internal disputes in the ruling coalition, while the global markets are also fearful of a growing rise in prices, firm rates and a potential recession.\par \par \uc2 "Caution and defensive postures continue to prevail among traders in the current external and domestic context," said Gustavo Ber, economist at Estudio Ber.\par \par \uc2 "Traders perceive a climate of accentuated nervousness in the face of the challenges imposed by continuing to manage fiscal, monetary and exchange rate imbalances, within a context that increasingly requires greater regulations", he added.\par \par \uc2 In the midst of recent restrictions on imports, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BCRA) managed to put strong pressure this week to add dollars to its battered reserves.\par \par \uc2 * Bonds in the over-the-counter market improved by an average of 1.2% due to opportunity purchases, after accumulating a decline of more than 10% in the last eight sessions with parities at historic lows.\par \par \uc2 * In this context, the country risk prepared by \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2  was down 60 units, to 2,374 points by 2000 GMT, after reaching its historical maximum of 2,508 units on Tuesday, in a scenario of fears of debt default.\par \par \uc2 * The market opens the possibilities that the current prices could be an entry point as they test supports near minimums and very low relative prices; however, local instability enables a risk to be considered for every investor," said Javier Rava from Rava Burs\u225\'00\'E1til.\par \par \uc2 * The leading stock index S&P; Merval of the Buenos Aires Stock Exchange gained a slight 0.36%, to provisionally close at 88,449.89 points, to show a decrease of 4.16% in the month and accumulate a 5.93% increase in the semester.\par \par \uc2 * In the exchange market, the interbank peso maintained a controlled depreciation with a key role in the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the BCRA, which managed to buy some 536 million dollars from the market, thus accumulating purchases of some 950 million dollars in June.\par \par \uc2 * In the semester, purchases exceeded 1.8 billion dollars", said an official source, and pointed out that "in this way the goal of accumulating reserves for the first half of the year was reached".\par \par \uc2 * This week the BCRA made modifications to the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  access policy to restrict import \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which allowed it to accelerate with the accumulation of reserves.\par \par \uc2 * As the saying goes, in Economics there is no such thing as a free lunch and in this case (of the limitation) the cost will come from a greater deterioration in activity, accompanied by higher inflation in the medium term", said the brokerage Stonex regarding the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently received the endorsement of a first revision of an agreement with the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  (\uc2 IMF\uc2 ), although the outlook is difficult given the commitment to strengthen the BCRA's reserves, reduce the fiscal deficit, lower inflation and cut subsidies, among others.\par \par \uc2 * The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the interbank market fell 0.14% to 125.22/125.23 per dollar, accumulating a depreciation of 4.02% in the sixth month of the year.\par \par \uc2 * The peso in the informal market hovered around historic lows, ending at 238 units to the dollar, and fell by a worrying 13.03% in June, with a gap of 90.1% with respect to the wholesale rate.\par \par \uc2 * In the alternative markets, the peso traded at 254.5 per dollar in the stock market "contado con liquidaci\u243\'00\'F3n" (CCL) and at 249.4 in the so-called "d\u243\'00\'F3lar MEP".\par \par \uc2 (Report by Walter Bianchi; additional collaboration by Hern\u225\'00\'E1n Nessi; Edited by Jorge Otaola)\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220630ei6u00av7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
