\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Patricia Bullrich at the Stock Exchange: "Our objective in C\u243\'00\'F3rdoba is a change".\b0\par\par\uc2 1,357 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juni 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Patricia Bullrich gave a talk this Monday at the C\u243\'00\'F3rdoba Stock Exchange in which she stated that the intention of Juntos por el Cambio for the 2023 elections is to beat Peronism and govern the province.\par \par \uc2 "We are in a delicate situation in the country. It is not a conjunctural reality, but a reality that we have been dragging. We need deep changes", affirmed the president of PRO. "Changes that put an end to these comings and goings of an Argentina that does not find a definitive course".\par \par \uc2 For Bullrich, the country needs a leadership that not only generates confidence, but that dares to break down all the barriers and obstacles that the country has had for a long time. "It is necessary not to be afraid of changes that will not be easy. There are no changes without efforts," he assured.\par \par \uc2 "We have lived it and we have suffered it", he remarked.\par \par \uc2 For the PRO politician, this change will not depend on a single person. "Not only a national government will be needed, but also the provinces. Our goal in C\u243\'00\'F3rdoba is a change. It is not to maintain the same structure that 24 years ago is", he anticipated.\par \par \uc2 Before an audience that included senators Luis Juez and Carmen \u193\'00\'C1lvarez, together with national deputies Rodrigo de Loredo, Soher el Sukaria, Laura Rodr\u237\'00\'EDguez Machado and H\u233\'00\'E9ctor Baldassi, among other figures of Juntos por el Cambio, Bullrich said that change has to come from the hand of ideas.\par \par \uc2 "Our basic idea, in Juntos por el Cambio, is a competitive capitalism whose base is the private economy," she explained. "Today, there is a crony capitalism, mafia-like."\par \par \uc2 And on this, Bullrich said that \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  needs a "brutal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 " to bring down a wall that has, for example, more state employees than private ones. "What Argentina can live like this, how can it be sustained that Cordoba maintains with its co-participation to Formosa, which is not their fault, public employees," he complained.\par \par \uc2 Austerity"Politics has to be the construction of a capacity to generate confidence in others that politicians have to have austerity, to end privileges," he described about the future. "There is no politics without exemplarity."\par \par \uc2 And she recalled that, when she was Minister of Security, she set the example. "You cannot have double standards. The first commitment has to come from those of us who intend to lead the country," Bullrich affirmed.\par \par \uc2 "The changes that need to be made are not only in the national government. There are 3 million working in the provincial states. We need to lower the deficit," he explained about the intentions of Juntos por el Cambio.\par \par \uc2 "What is coming has to be without fear, without half measures... we have to be 'let's change' instead of 'let's go on'. When we were afraid, they realized, they threw 14 tons of stones at us and we were paralyzed," he warned.\par \par \uc2 Together for Change: three lawsBullrich said that Juntos por el Cambio will promote three laws if it becomes government. The first one would be one of debureaucratization to get "the mafias" out of the State and eliminate all the "brutal" web of organizations that co-opt governments.\par \par \uc2 The second is to "get out of the anomy" that the country is experiencing in relation to the economy. It is a reform of the Organic Charter of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "We are full of little pieces of paper that are worthless," he explained. "And we pay for a house in cash with green bills (for dollars).\par \par \uc2 "The banking system is in jail. Enough of it working for the state. It has to work for the people", he warned. And he put forward a disruptive idea: "We are going to have to anchor our reserves outside the country".\par \par \uc2 Finally, he proposed a strong reform of the State, so that the entrance to a government's staff would be different.\par \par \uc2 He also spoke of seeking justice with a system that has a rational relationship between public and private employment. "We cannot have 8 million jobs that pay all the social security of all Argentina", he complained.\par \par \uc2 Social plansBullrich ratified that he wants to "discontinue" social plans. "Yes, that's right. Because it is a failure. It is a disaster. We have kept crushing people. They are inactive people, who live in a ghetto, who do not go out to work. That their life ends up being a disgrace," he criticized.\par \par \uc2 "We want society as a whole to grant all the mechanisms so that, in 6 months, schools, universities and institutions become available to train people, so they can go out to work," he promised.\par \par \uc2 Dollars"We have to allow transactions in dollars, which is not dollarization. We want the possibility of the use of both \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he anticipated. "This way we will be able to free the 'cepos' and the 'cepitos'. So that every Argentine can do what he/she wants with his/her money".\par \par \uc2 Minutes later, Bullrich clarified that if it were possible "not to touch the reserves", the country would have a possibility of reassembling a support base for the whole economic policy. "Without that support, with the lack of dollars, it is not possible to move forward", he exemplified.\par \par \uc2 At the end, he remarked again that Juntos por el Cambio wants its own governments in provinces such as Entre R\u237\'00\'EDos or C\u243\'00\'F3rdoba.\par \par \uc2 "We know what we have to do. We are going to be concrete, and we are going to be brave. This time we are going with clear ideas, and we are going to do them fast, with intelligence", he predicted. "Therefore, I say to you: are we determined, willing to assume the change, or to maintain the status quo? I'm betting on the risk of change."\par \par \uc2 Together for ChangeBullrich then took questions. One of them was about how candidates should be defined in C\u243\'00\'F3rdoba next year. "Polls can be a reasonable system," she answered. "By the end of this month, we have to have the system defined."\par \par \uc2 Melconian and Cristina"Me, no," he said on whether he would push for a meeting of \uc2 Guido Sandleris\uc2  with \uc2 Cristina Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It was to answer whether he shared the decision of Carlos Melconian, from the Fundaci\u243\'00\'F3n Mediterr\u225\'00\'E1nea, to take his economic plan to \uc2 Cristina Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez de Kirchner\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In his turn, Sandleris added that the differences with Cristina "are unbridgeable".\par \par \uc2 Sandleris Earlier, Sandleris, advisor to the Stock Exchange, spoke. The former president of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , during the administration of \uc2 Mauricio Macri\uc2 , reviewed the economy of \uc2 Alberto Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez\uc2 's government, with harsh criticism for the increase of the fiscal deficit in the last months.\par \par \uc2 In addition, he remarked the problems that monetary issuance is bringing to the economy. "Much of the acceleration of prices has to do with that," Sandleris stated.\par \par \uc2 He also remarked on the problems the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is having in adding reserves, despite record export numbers in recent months.\par \par \uc2 Sandleris said, in any case, that the national government still has time to avoid a spiral of the crisis, with more fiscal adjustment and exchange rate correction.\par \par \uc2 TagleManuel Tagle, president of the Buenos Aires Stock Exchange, also spoke.\par \par \uc2 Tagle congratulated Sandleris and remarked that the Stock Exchange is interested in expanding its gaze to the whole country. "We have doubts because there are many variables that are starting to get nervous," said the businessman.\par \par \uc2 For Tagle, the country's central problem is the deficit. "One meaning is that of fiscal deficit, where revenues are not enough to cover costs. These policies can generate a certain level of welfare, some reactivation.... Reactivation that begins to generate a second deficit: that of the balance of payments," he described.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, the businessman criticized the latest measures taken by the national Government in relation to an adjustment of the cepo for the importation of goods and services.\par \par \uc2 "What this Government is looking for is to achieve a precarious balance to reach the next elections", concluded Tagle. "Because there is nothing it can do to generate credibility".\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220627ei6r00925\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
