\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 The blue rose again and set another record high\b0\par\par\uc2 423 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juni 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The blue dollar rose another two pesos and reached a new high of 226 pesos. Financial quotes such as the cash with liquidation ended at 237 pesos, almost unchanged with respect to the previous day. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  registered a new day of strong sales in the exchange market. It sold 95 million dollars and in the week it accumulated sales for 250 million dollars, while in the month it has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for 600 million dollars.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stock market assets showed new setbacks, mainly in sovereign bonds in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The quotations of these securities, which were restructured, registered falls close to 5 percent and once again gave a jump to the country's risk. This index prepared by \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2  ended the week at 2347 points, with a daily increase of 1.7 percent, an increase of 21.1 percent in June and a rise of 37.3 percent in the year.\par \par \uc2 The last day of the week also saw a sharp fall in the price of inflation-adjusted peso securities (i.e., with the cer index). For example, the TX26 fell 7.5 percent and accumulates a 28 percent decrease for the year. This puts pressure on the Treasury's debt renewals, one of the variables closely followed by the market, due to its possible impact on the cash with liquidation.\par \par \uc2 The Ministry of Economy announced the menu of instruments for the next bidding on Tuesday, June 28. "In the reopening of all the Ledes offered, minimum rates that guarantee a positive real yield to the investor are fixed", it was indicated.\par \par \uc2 In turn, it was mentioned that the menu of instruments offered in this tender consists of the following instruments:\par \par \uc2 - Lelite maturing on July 29, with an adhesion price resulting in a TNA of 51 percent and a TEA of 61.72 percent for the 29-day term.\par \par \uc2 - The reopening of the Ledes maturing at the end of August, October and November with maximum subscription prices which implies for the investor to guarantee the following minimum rates: TNA 55.57 percent/TEA 70.06 percent; TNA 58.43/TEA 70.46 and TNA 60.01/TEA 70.80.\par \par \uc2 - Reopening of the Lecer maturing October 21 and December 16, 2022.\par \par \uc2 - New Lecer maturing November 23, 2022 with a maximum subscription price that guarantees the investor a real rate of 2.75%.\par \par \uc2 - The reopening of the dollar-linked bonds maturing on 4/28/2023 and 4/30/2024.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220624ei6o00dpt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
