\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 The \uc2 IMF\uc2  created a new "resilience fund" and Argentina will receive a significant sum of money\b0\par\par\uc2 1,152 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 April 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  (\uc2 IMF\uc2 ) approved the creation of a new Resilience and Sustainability Trust Fund, which will be aimed at helping low- and middle-income countries such as Argentina, in the context of "climate change and pandemics".\par \par \uc2 Argentina will receive u$s1,300 million in Special Drawing Rights (SDR) from this initiative, which the Executive Director of the Monetary Fund, Kristalina Georgieva, described as an "aid for vulnerable countries to face longer-term challenges, such as climate change and pandemics, which pose risks to economies and people".\par \par \uc2 "We seek to help countries build a resilient and sustainable future. The Trust will amplify the impact of the $650 billion SDR allocation implemented last year by channeling resources from economically stronger members to countries where the needs are greatest. The aspiration is to build a Trust of at least $45 billion in resources," Georgieva explained. \uc2 IMF\uc2  dollars: when to pay them back\par \par \uc2 The amount granted may be repaid over a period of up to 20 years, and will "help build resilience to long-term risks to balance of payments stability," said the \uc2 IMF\uc2  director in a statement.\par \par \uc2 About three-quarters of \uc2 IMF\uc2  member countries will be eligible for this financing, "including low-income members, as well as most middle-income countries and all small developing states," Georgieva said.\par \par \uc2 The Resilience Trust, which will become \b \highlight22\uc2 operational\b0 \highlight\uc2  on May 1, was created to provide financial assistance to vulnerable countries and joins other \uc2 IMF\uc2  tools, such as the General Resources Account and the Poverty Reduction and Growth Trust.\par \par \uc2 "Our members asked us to enhance our existing lending toolkit to address a growing need to build resilience and sustainability now to reduce economic risks in the future," Georgieva stressed.\par \par \uc2 As of August 2021, Argentina had received u$s4,334 million in SDRs, which were deposited as \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves and used to repay debt with that organization. \uc2 IMF\uc2  warning on inflation in Argentina.\par \par \uc2 " Inflation is paralyzing the economy" in Argentina. Ceyla Pazarbasioglu's word is important because this Turkish economist is in charge of assessing the consistency of local figures in view of the agreement signed with the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 For Pazarbasioglu, "inflation is harder for the most vulnerable people" and it is imperative to "tame it". In this attempt to tame the rise in prices, "rates are being raised", the specialist clarified.\par \par \uc2 During an interview with \uc2 Bloomberg Television\uc2 , the Turkish economist clarified that Argentina's decision to raise interest rates to 47% "is part of the agreement that Argentina signed with the \uc2 IMF\uc2 ".\par \par \uc2 Pazarbasioglu put international context to the local scenario: "We are seeing shock after shock in the world economy", including financial crisis, coronavirus and war. And in this sense he added: "There are many countries that have an unsustainable debt" that requires careful work by the \uc2 IMF\uc2 , governments and the private sector.\par \par \uc2 In the last hours and via \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , the \uc2 IMF\uc2 's Turkish economist made a post in which she called "the international community to urgently support vulnerable countries through coordinated actions ranging from the provision of emergency food supplies, financial support, increased agricultural production and open trade". The Argentine situation\par \par \uc2 Rushed by the soaring CPI -which closed March with a historical mark of 6.7%- and in the midst of internal tensions within the Government over the management of inflation, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised the economy's reference rate on Wednesday for the fourth consecutive time. The increase was discounted in the City, but it was a little higher than expected: it was 250 basis points, which takes the Leliq yield to 47% per annum, while raising the minimum rate for fixed term deposits to 46%. Who is Ceyla Pazarbasioglu and why is she important for Argentina?\par \par \uc2 Ceyla Pazarbasioglu is in charge of monitoring the balance and viability of Argentine variables in view of the recent agreement signed between the country and the Fund. She will report on the local situation to the Managing Director for the Western Hemisphere, the Brazilian-Israeli Illan Goldfjan.\par \par \uc2 The Turkish economist returned to the \uc2 IMF\uc2  this year but had previously worked at the organization, the \uc2 World Bank\uc2  (WB) and in the private financial market on Wall Street. She is now Director of the Strategy, Policy and Review Department. Quarterly review: very close to being met\par \par \uc2 The agreement with the \uc2 IMF\uc2  contemplates targets for the accumulation of net international reserves, which for the first quarter of the year implied achieving an increase of u$s1,200 million with respect to the stock of December 2021. Analysts warn that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  managed to meet the quarterly guideline in a "tight" manner and it was exclusively thanks to the first disbursement that the international organization made after formally approving the new program with \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  on March 25.\par \par \uc2 They also consider that the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the official \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market (MULC) left "little taste" since March closed with a buying balance of only u$s275 million despite the record liquidation of the agricultural sector due to the rise in the price of commodities as a result of the war between Russia and Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 In this scenario, the market's focus will be on the dynamics of the BCRA's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases, given the challenging target set for the year in the agreement with the \uc2 IMF\uc2 , which contemplates an increase in net reserves of u$s5,800 million. \uc2 IMF\uc2 : tight compliance\par \par \uc2 Following the green light to the new agreement with Argentina, the \uc2 IMF\uc2  disbursed on March 25 the first disbursement of 7 billion Special Drawing Rights (SDRs) equivalent to US$ 9,656 million.\par \par \uc2 "Net of the payments to be made to the \uc2 IMF\uc2 , some u$s2,904 million, u$s6,752 million entered the BCRA's coffers. Gross reserves went (that day) from u$s37,075 million to u$s43,186 million, while net reserves also improved, but to a lesser extent", stated a report by EconViews.\par \par \uc2 In this regard, the consultant explained that "this is due to the fact that it was agreed that only u$s3,166 million SDRs (u$s4,367 million) can be used in its calculation".\par \par \uc2 "With this income, net reserves reach u$s 3,784 million, that is u$s 1,459 million above the December level. In this way, the target for the first quarter is met, which establishes an increase of u$s 1,200 million", he specified.\par \par \uc2 In this context, analysts at Facimex Valores pointed out that "the BCRA met the net reserves target for the first quarter of 2022 set at u$s3,500 million in the agreement with the \uc2 IMF\uc2 , although it did it with the right amount".\par \par \uc2 "The goal was met exclusively due to the net financing provided by the \uc2 IMF\uc2  itself, which reinforced net reserves by some u$s4,300 million", they emphasized.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220414ei4e0091s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
