\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Argentina's latest "mystical delirium": a proposal to create a state-owned food company\b0\par\par\uc2 1,197 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Februar 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' s government remains determined to control and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the economy despite the disastrous results that its populist policies have been reaping for decades. The main cause of the country's widespread impoverishment is inflation\par \par \uc2 , a monster that Argentine politicians continue to feed with their ill-advised decisions. The proof is in the fact that, as of today, more than 40% of Argentines are poor and the country leads the misery index among the world's leading economies In 2021, Argentina's official inflation reached a whopping 50.9% - the highest rate in the Americas, only behind Venezuela -\par \par \uc2 and everything points to price escalation continuing at similar levels in 2022. The measures taken by Peronist \uc2 Alberto Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez\uc2 , together with the pandemic, have further aggravated the country's inflationary situation. Thus, the reckless monetary policies of its \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  or the governmental "stimulus" plans have been joined by the bottlenecks generated by the coronavirus crisis or the rise in energy prices\par \par \uc2 . All these factors have continued to push prices upwards , hurting, as inflation always does, Argentina's lower incomes.\par \par \uc2 The consequences: submission to the State and an axe to familiesDaniel Rodr\u237\'00\'EDguez Asensio From Flan Royal to Maggi Puree That is why, in 2021, the escalation of prices overflowed the shopping basket in the country, which led the Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez government to take a measure as desperate as unsuccessful: freezing food prices\par \par \uc2 . Specifically, the Peronist Executive decided last October to freeze for three months the price of 1,500 foodstuffs and other basic consumer products in an attempt to curb inflation. In this link you can see the more than 800 pages of price tables set by the State. From "Royal Vanilla Flan" to "Maggi's Creamiest Texture Mashed Potatoes", the Argentine Executive's blow to entrepreneurial freedom was total. And as usual when governments \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in economies, the freeze on 1,500 products has been extended.\par \par \uc2 Living the drama of hyperinflation: "My salary in the morning had a value and at night it was worth half of it "C.Jord\u225\'00\'E1 As expected, in these three months, the situation has not been reversed and prices continue to burden the pockets of Argentines day after day\par \par \uc2 . When this freeze was announced, inflation in September was 37%, while last January, the Argentine CPI closed at 50.7%. Fulminan del mapa econ\u243\'00\'F3mico mundial a Argentina: "Nos pone al borde de la quiebra "Beatriz Garc\u237\'00\'EDa Peter Hyland is manager of several companies in the agri-food sector in the country, which supply raw materials to the beer company Quilmes, among many other companies. His experience with price limitations is dire. "It is a recipe that has never worked. It has been 10 years since the government of \uc2 Cristina Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez de Kirchner\uc2  created the "Precios Cuidados" and the shopping basket continues to rise. Now, the only thing they have achieved by limiting the price of those 1,500 products is that their manufacturers lower the quality and that people do not want to buy them\par \par \uc2 . If they have to sell milk at X price, they mix it with water. They have no choice. No one wants to buy a product whose price is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  because they are worse," explains Hyland.A state-owned food company Despite this evidence, the Fernandez government does not intend to change its strategy to help make food products cheaper. Instead of promoting the free market, facilitating competition among companies or lowering the taxation of products, it is already considering another crazy plan: to create a state food company\par \par \uc2 . The idea is being promoted by Rafael Klejzer, the National Director of Integrating Policies of the \uc2 Argentine Ministry of Social Development\uc2 . Klejzer is one of the leaders of the radical left-wing party La Dignidad and the visible face of the Confederaci\u243\'00\'F3n de Trabajadores de la Econom\u237\'00\'EDa Popular (CTEP). Now, he is part of the Argentine Executive. He himself has explained that the "National Food Company", whose acronym would be ENA, would aim at controlling the food sector, which he considers to be dominated by the "hands of the big corporations"\par \par \uc2 . Klejzer does not hesitate to harshly attack food companies and capitalism to justify his crazy idea. "We could also generate a reference price on mass consumption products and that would mean putting a stop to the greed of capitalist companies\par \par \uc2 that understand food as a commodity and not as a right" he points out. Klejzer's public company already has a logo. The National Director of Integrating Policies of the Ministry of Social Development has not given details on whether his hypothetical national company would have its own production or would be formed by selecting a few local partners to do some of the work for the State. Nor has it presented any economic report explaining how much its idea would cost Argentine taxpayers. The Argentine government spokeswoman, Gabriela Cerruti\par \par \uc2 , also welcomed the project without elaborating on the details. "Another bunch of bums". Peter Hyland assures that "this idea lacks any logic other than to create another bunch of bums . The entire agri-food and industrial chain in Argentina rejects it because it has already failed in Venezuela or Cuba". Another Argentine businessman, Gustavo Lazzari, owner of the sausage and ham company Frigor\u237\'00\'EDfico C\u225\'00\'E1rdenas , agrees. "In Argentina there are 15,000 companies in the food sector that employ 500,000 people, to think that we need a national food company is a mystical delirium"\par \par \uc2 , he assures. Lazzari, who is also an economist, links inflation as a strictly monetary phenomenon and does not doubt that the state food company that will be loss-making. "We are seeing that the State is a producer of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and produces it badly or that it loses 2 million euros a day with \uc2 Aerolineas Argentinas\par \par \uc2 , and that it has the power to regulate the prices of the competition. \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  issuance and inflation have a one-to-one correlation and limiting food prices or creating state-owned companies will have no effect on it because we are talking about a macro phenomenon, not a micro one". The media \u193\'00\'C1mbito gives more details. According to the bill to which this publication has had access, the Argentine government's plan would be to create "Alimentos Argentinos", not ENA as suggested by Klejzer. It would be a company with a majority participation of the State of 51% which "will have as its object to carry out, on its own account or through strategic association with third parties, the production, manufacture, fractioning, distribution, marketing and industrialization of food products in the Argentine Republic". Lazzari is blunt and assures that this idea "is made to steal, not to produce. And if they carry it out, we will not take long to see the corruption it generates", he predicts.\par \par \uc2 As we published in Libre Mercado\par \par \uc2 , it is striking that monopolistic services, protected by legislation or offered by the Government, are the ones that almost always systematically increase in price due to the lack of incentives to innovate or compete. La inflaci\u243\'00\'F3n que nunca vemos o c\u243\'00\'F3mo comprar un televisor un 95% m\u225\'00\'E1s baratoD. Soriano\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220225ei2p004l4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
