\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Corruption excludes, disintegrates and impoverishes peoples and countries.\b0\par\par\uc2 970 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Januar 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The increasing perception of corruption is turning Argentina into an increasingly disintegrated country, alienating people from the decisions that matter to them. Even the negotiation with the \uc2 IMF\uc2  is opaque because the government wants to keep the funds it controls out of the public's reach. Our rulers exclude the majority of the people from the resolutions that determine the distribution of income with changes in regulations and accumulate powers to the point of tolerating the usurpation of private property.\par \par \uc2 Countries combine different decision centers: the level of politicians, the level of private individuals, and their links with each other. The greater the control of private individuals, the less and more efficient public spending becomes. The collapse of communism precipitated a contraction of decisions that politicians keep out of the public eye. However, in this 21st century, politicians have regained space. In \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they have never had so much profitability and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in decisions as now.\par \par \uc2 The greater the control of the private sector, the less and more efficient public spending becomes.\par \par \uc2 Last Tuesday, Infobae published the world map of the perception of corruption in the State prepared by \uc2 Transparency International\uc2 , which allows us to understand our difficulties, because it reveals that the least corrupt countries are those with the highest per capita income. Western Europe, Singapore, Japan, New Zealand, Australia. In the Americas, Canada, USA, Chile and Uruguay.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, the advance in the perception of corruption in Argentina: it dropped to 96th place in the table among the 180 countries analyzed annually by TI, corresponds to a notable decrease in the GDP per capita equivalent in dollars, particularly when estimated at the free exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 In several articles in Infobae and books I have been developing two antagonistic concepts: Corruption and Competition. Competitive sports teach. In soccer, there is only one rule, stable and equal for all players, with a specific distinction for the goalkeeper. Messi does not stand out because of a private rule that privileges him, but because of his skills in playing with the same rule as the millions of players who enjoy the game.\par \par \uc2 The competition\par \par \uc2 Confused, some colleagues focus competitiveness on the exchange rate or on granting privileges to certain activities. They did not realize that every difference, every regulatory leap, is a barrier to transactions, disconnecting them from the whole. Competitiveness is the achievement of integrating, including, all participants, with the same stable rules for all, without exclusions. This ensures that individual incomes reflect the contribution of each one to the satisfaction of the individual needs of the population and that GDPs are the maximum possible.\par \par \uc2 Why is this the case? Differences characterize humans and competition with the same rules induces the development of valuable personal skills, such as outstanding players in soccer. Specialization, learning, favors training to meet personal needs. Many of our politicians do not seem to understand this; they consider it a fallacy that wealth creation is a quality of individuals. That people mutually and simultaneously benefit from voluntary exchanges. That is why they privilege their followers and despise private property. They did not read Adam Smith, "The Wealth of Nations", edited in 1776, the year of the Independence of the USA.\par \par \uc2 Societies advanced where Justice consists of the same and identical rule for all. For only by keeping the rules the same for all, without alterations, transactions are voluntary and value-creating.\par \par \uc2 Differences characterize humans and competition with the same rules induces the development of valuable personal skills.\par \par \uc2 In total contrast, for autocrats Justice is the best rule for them who rule and march against the Supreme Court. Corruption are non-consensual acts, as the rules differ depending on who is involved. Forced redistribution. The opposite of a value-creating transaction.\par \par \uc2 Wealth creation is favored with securities, certainties, knowledge. The best possible education decided by the learners and their families; jobs freely contracted, without redundant interference from governments, unions, pickets. Justice to prevent violations, crimes, and sudden changes of norms. Monetary and fiscal stability to ensure prices, tariffs, taxes. Government budgets sanctioned with the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of freely elected representatives.\par \par \uc2 Failure of the Republic\par \par \uc2 Very broad powers over private property are granted to officials without credentials or guarantees, with only an oath to comply with the Constitution. The expansion of populism and the increase of poverty should not be surprising.\par \par \uc2 I call corruption to all the breaking of particular rules for the benefit of a few.\par \par \uc2 Transparency International\uc2  measures annually the perception of corruption of businessmen and experts, but only in relation to the conduct of the public sector, in the political and administrative sphere, a narrower concept.\par \par \uc2 Its Corruption Perceptions Index (CPI) in the public sector ranks countries on a scale of zero for the most corrupt and one hundred for the cleanest, based on 13 external sources, including the \uc2 World Bank\uc2 , the \uc2 World Economic Forum\uc2 , private companies specializing in risk analysis, consulting firms and expert committees.\par \par \uc2 In the book "For a Fairer and Flourishing Country" I detail 30 measures to integrate the economy. A set of commercial, labor, tax, exchange, monetary, labor union and political rules, which make up monetary and regulatory stabilities, realistic budgets that give certainty to individual plans.\par \par \uc2 These proposals seek to level the rules, favor Competition, Justice and Efficiency, as a necessary condition to expand the income of society as a whole and be able to get out of stagnation and the state of widespread poverty.\par \par \uc2 CONTINUE READING:\par \par \uc2 "The Government is in a left-wing populism that is leading us to ruin": the harsh warning of a renowned financial expert\par \par \uc2 Argentina asked China to extend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap by USD 3 billion to strengthen its reserves.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Balance Sheet exposes the vulnerability and urgencies of the economy\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220129ei1t002q0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
