\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Future Dollar:  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\uc2  Reaches its Limit\b0\par\par\uc2 751 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 November 2021\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Since the elections passed, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BCRA) stopped \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the stock market and the MEP soared above $ 200.\par \par \uc2 However, this does not mean that the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been unconcerned with what happens with the proxies used by the market to see where the official \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  can go. In fact, on the contrary, in the futures market it took its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the maximum of the Pesce era.\par \par \uc2 According to market estimates, the selling position of the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be between u$s 6200 and u$s 6700 million. Until now, the highest value was the one observed in October 2020, just below u$s 5700 million.\par \par \uc2 In this way, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to bet on moderating the rates in the Rofex and the Electronic Open Market (MAE), in order to reduce exchange tensions in the official market.\par \par \uc2 "As of Friday, November 19, the open interest between Rofex and MAE was u$s 8076 million, growing u$s 2919 million compared to the end of October", stated a report by 1816 Consultancy.\par \par \uc2 The document argues that if all this increase is explained by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , then the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  is sold in u$s 6534 million. "But if again the movement of open interest underestimated the BCRA sales, then the short position of the Central is even higher".\par \par \uc2 If these numbers are confirmed, the sales position would be growing by leaps and bounds. It is worth noting that the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed September with sales of u$s 1770 million and in October that number jumped to u$s 3615 million.\par \par \uc2 In addition, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be taking its possibilities of selling to the limit: due to regulatory issues it can only put on the table up to u$s 5000 million in Rofex and up to u$s 4000 million in MAE.\par \par \uc2 For the moment, the BCRA is winning the arm wrestling with the market, given that no discrete jump in the exchange rate has been validated and even the crawling peg is still in slow motion. It is estimated that between the beginning of the year and October Pesce's team raised about $ 14,500 million pesos for its shares.\par \par \uc2 "It is logical that the market seeks refuge and, somehow, ends up shorting the peso," said Andres Reschini, of F2 Soluciones Financieras.\par \par \uc2 And he added that agents are betting against the peso because they see "the exchange rate lagging behind inflation, a critical level of reserves, a gap above 100%, increasingly greater and less effective exchange restrictions, more financing to the Treasury via issuance and the absence of an economic plan".\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Tom\u225\'00\'E1s Ruiz Palacios, fixed income strategist at Cohen Aliados Financiero, estimated that the BCRA's sales position could be between US$6.2 billion and US$6.7 billion.\par \par \uc2 And indicated that, for the moment, the Central managed to lower the values of future dollar seen in Rofex: "The implicit rates were compressing quite a lot, as well as prices. The market was very bought, expecting an exchange rate adjustment and, not only it didn't happen, but the BCRA reduced even more its devaluation rhythm, hitting hedging assets".\par \par \uc2 Ruiz Palacios added that this action, added to fears about a possible split, "made investors become cautious and greatly reduced the volume in these assets".\par \par \uc2 "Even so, we are very cautious with this market: the situation is still as fragile as before and it will take very little to reignite the appetite for hedging, especially considering that the BCRA's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  capacity in Rofex is almost exhausted," he said.\par \par \uc2 Currently, the future dollar to March is trading at $ 121.20 on Rofex. That value reaches $ 126.10 for April and $ 131.25 for May. The longest position, that is, October 2022, is at $ 156.90.\par \par \uc2 "I think there was a strong compression of futures rates, both for the continuity of the BCRA \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and for the change of expectations implied by the Government decisions after the elections," said Juan Pablo Di Iorio, economist at ACM.\par \par \uc2 Regarding the latter, the analyst mentioned: "Reducing \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in parallel markets marginally improves the BCRA's net reserves position for the coming months. On the other hand, the messages about reaching an agreement with the \uc2 IMF\uc2  in the short term not only give a horizon, but also reduce the potential source of demand for dollars that imply capital payments from March next year".\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020211125ehbo001pd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
