\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Dollar Continues to Rise, Market Sees Devaluation as a Key Factor in Dollar's Rally\b0\par\par\uc2 939 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 November 2021\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The dollarization of portfolios persisted on Thursday in the Argentine market, as a purchasing power hedge against the weakness of the battered peso and the expectations generated by Sunday's legislative elections, where the government could lose control of Congress if the PASO results are repeated.\par \par \uc2 This morning, the blue dollar set a new record high, three days before the legislative elections next Sunday, and reached $ 207 for purchase.\par \par \uc2 Once again, President \uc2 Alberto Fernandez\uc2 's entourage had to insist that there is no devaluation in the offing, given the risk generated by an exchange rate gap of over 100% with the informal exchange rate and record levels of country risk.\par \par \uc2 "The Argentine problem is not so much the type of public policies, but rather the type of consensus that is generated to move towards a comprehensive economic plan, whether it is more centrist, more \b \highlight22\uc2 interventionist\b0 \highlight\uc2  or more market-oriented (...) \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  needs much more political clarity, more political anchoring and credibility," said Javier Timerman, a partner at the consulting firm AdCap , in a radio interview. Gabriela Cerruti, spokeswoman for the presidency, said this morning at a press conference: "There is no need to agitate for a devaluation (...) Monday (next Monday after the elections) is Monday, we govern every day.\par \par \uc2 The peso quoted in the reduced marginal market was devalued by 0.97%, to a record low of 204/207 per dollar, traders said, resulting in a gap of 106.8% against the official exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 "We know that this is an illegal dollar, which is managed with other expectations," Cerruti said at his weekly press conference at Government House.\par \par \uc2 In the wholesale band, the national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gave up 0.04% to 100.17/100.19 units, where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BCRA) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to avoid a much more aggressive fluctuation. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has lost about 290 million dollars of its reserves in the last two days.\par \par \uc2 The peso in other alternative markets also lost ground: it fell to 185.7 per dollar in the "Contado con Liquidaci\u243\'00\'F3n", to 184.5 in the "d\u243\'00\'F3lar MEP" and up to 220 per dollar in the bilateral negotiation "Senebi", where the BCRA is now also trying to influence with the sale of bonds, according to market sources.\par \par \uc2 The Buenos Aires stock market was up 1.41% to 96,465.58 points at 12:30 local time (1530 GMT) in its S&P Merval stock index, against the intraday record of 97,024.42 units last Tuesday. There was a shortage of liquidity due to a partial holiday in the United States.\par \par \uc2 This stock market continues to be a refuge for those seeking to position themselves in dollars abroad, given the weakness of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The over-the-counter debt did not show genuine values due to the U.S. inactivity, although the country risk prepared by the bank JP.Morgan soared nine units to a record of 1,753 basis points, to exceed the previous 1,747 of a week ago.\par \par \uc2 The market sees as inevitable an acceleration in the pace of devaluation after the elections, at the gates of the end of the year. This is the opinion of the Delphos Investment consulting firm, which points out as triggering factors the level of net reserves that is "at the limit" and the impossibility of reaching an agreement with the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  (\uc2 IMF\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 The forecast considers for its analysis the scenario of the future dollar and bonds. According to the prices traded in the Rofex futures market, the nominal exchange rate increase for December would be 5.2%, while for January it would increase to 6.2%. Thus, the official quotation of the North American \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be $113.2. The rate would be reduced in February (4.4%) and March (5.3%), leaving the wholesale for that date at $130.4. The wholesale crossed, for the first time in history, the $100 pesos and closed yesterday at $100.15.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, in bonds, the real devaluation (measured between Lecer and TV22) is 7.2% which would indicate a rise in the nominal exchange rate far higher than inflationary levels.The report takes the periods 2008-2009 and 2013-2014 to compare those scenarios with the current one ?because they were under a government whose policies are similar to the current ones, with some macro and micro characteristics that allow projecting a similar outcome to those of that time?\par \par \uc2 Regarding the period '08-'09, whose context was marked by an international crisis derived from a bubble in the mortgage market, the report indicates that in terms of the nominal exchange rate a devaluation jump can be noticed, starting in September and a greater expression in October 2008, where the values reached 3.3% and 7.64% respectively.\par \par \uc2 The consultant highlights that the mentioned values, together with an inflation around 1%, denoted a more solid macroeconomic situation than the current one, where even the real exchange rate was higher.\par \par \uc2 In reference to the scenario that occurred in '13-'14, the document analyzes that it can be highlighted that the rise of the nominal exchange rate had already brought an upward path that seemed controlled until November 2013, where it began to gain momentum to reach the peak of rise in nominal term of 22.63% in January '14. This rise in the nominal exchange rate was then surpassed by the inflationary context, leaving the real devaluation in negative territory.(*Report by Jorge Otaola; Additional reporting by Hern\u225\'00\'E1n Nessi; Edited by Walter Bianchi. Published by Reuters)\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020211111ehbb00bz2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
