ified in a \uc2 Fitch\uc2  report were involved in, but are not solely responsible for, the opinions stated therein. The individuals are named for contact purposes only. A report providing a \uc2 Fitch\uc2  rating is neither a prospectus nor a substitute for the information assembled, verified and presented to investors by the issuer and its agents in connection with the sale of the securities. Ratings may be changed or withdrawn at any time for any reason in the sole discretion of \uc2 Fitch\uc2 . \uc2 Fitch\uc2  does not provide investment advice of any sort. Ratings are not a recommendation to buy, sell, or hold any security. Ratings do not comment on the adequacy of market price, the suitability of any security for a particular investor, or the tax-exempt nature or taxability of payments made in respect to any security. \uc2 Fitch\uc2  receives fees from issuers, insurers, guarantors, other obligors,\par \par \uc2 14 Oct 2021 15:39 ET  Press Release: \uc2 Fitch\uc2  Affirms Argentina at '\uc2 CCC\uc2 ' -3-\par \par \uc2 and underwriters for rating securities. Such fees generally vary from US$1,000 to US$750,000 (or the applicable \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  equivalent) per issue. In certain cases, \uc2 Fitch\uc2  will rate all or a number of issues issued by a particular issuer, or insured or guaranteed by a particular insurer or guarantor, for a single annual fee. Such fees are expected to vary from US$10,000 to US$1,500,000 (or the applicable \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  equivalent). The assignment, publication, or dissemination of a rating by \uc2 Fitch\uc2  shall not constitute a consent by \uc2 Fitch\uc2  to use its name as an expert in connection with any registration statement filed under the United States securities laws, the Financial Services and Markets Act of 2000 of the United Kingdom, or the securities laws of any particular jurisdiction. Due to the relative efficiency of electronic publishing and distribution