\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 More tightening: the market warns about the widening of the exchange rate gap while the market presses for dollarization\b0\par\par\uc2 955 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Oktober 2021\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The new exchange restrictions made financial analysts to recalculate what are the ways that have investors and sophisticated and savers who only seek protection from inflation and a hypothetical devaluation to dollarize their pesos. Once the new regulations are understood, the conclusion is that there are still alternatives to dollarize without limits, although they are more expensive and more difficult to access\par \par \uc2 . Naturally, analysts anticipate that we will have to expect a widening of the exchange rate gap.The magnifying glass on the gap and on the nooks and crannies left free by the tightening of the exchange-rate restrictions indicate the size of the problem faced by the government, which is still betting, by dint of a greater exchange-rate tourniquet, to avoid a sudden exchange-rate jump, with what that means for inflation, economic activity and the welfare of Argentines, especially those who have no tools to defend themselves from exchange-rate and financial turbulence.\par \par \uc2 The gap accentuates the incentive to delay the liquidation of imports and to demand more dollars to import at the official exchange rate. This was the reason why the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  restricted the sale of dollars to importers.\par \par \uc2 The initial reaction of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was cautious: trading volume fell on the stock market as players digested the impact of the measures. Even several exchange houses and brokerage firms (Alyc) momentarily suspended their activities with bonds,\par \par \uc2 while adjusting their systems to the new rules.Traders agree that the first impact of the measures will be a much less liquid market, and thatalthough a priori the BCRA may manage to reduce its reserves dripping, the relief will be momentary\par \par \uc2 .Diego Martinez Burzaco\par \par \uc2 , from Inviu, said: "If the government's goal is to stop losing reserves by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the Ley \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  bond market, it is likely to achieve it or at least reduce the pace of its sales, but at a cost of more distrust and more distortions in the market. In this line, another operator remarked: "The government will manage to manage the price of a dollar that in practice will be fictitious and new gaps will be generated".As the measures made official in the Official Gazette on Wednesday put a ceiling on bond transactions of 50,000 nominal values, some US$18,000 per week, in truth, this new chapter of the exchange restrictions only impacts the big players\par \par \uc2 . So far, this limit was in force for the \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  for cash with liquidation, now both CCL and MEP dollar purchases were unified under this weekly cap.Retail savers who had turned to the MEP will not see changes in their \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although they were affected by the interruptions to the purchase and sale of bonds that occurred in banks and brokerage firms. However, they will have to add one more paper to their purchases and sign an affidavit stating that they have not traded foreign law bonds or other assets against dollars in the last 30 days\par \par \uc2 , nor will they do so during the following month.The agency chaired by Adrian Cosentino also placed restrictions on transactions with Argentine law bonds, such as the Bonar 2030 (AL30), the most used to make the purchase of dollar exchange and cash with liquidation. The regulation establishes that whoever has operated with these bonds, for a period of 30 days before and after the purchase, will not be able to transfer assets or operate with these species\par \par \uc2 ."Now investors will have to choose in which cash to operate: if they choose the "subsidized" dollar of the AL30, which trades around $175, they should know that for more than a month they will not be able to make other \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . If you want to buy freely, you can operate with global bonds, but the exchange rate of this \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  is higher," explained in strict off a trader.\par \par \uc2 At the end of Wednesday, the MEP dollar made with the Global 30D, exceeded $180; while the cash with liquidation made with this species closed at $189.84, with more than $12 difference with the "screen" ccl. The gap is consolidated above 90%, and is expected to widen.\par \par \uc2 In addition to \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  with global bonds, foreign law, the other alternative to continue getting dollars in the financial market will be the purchase of ADRS or Cedears\par \par \uc2 . On average, the spot with liquidation via ADRs closed this Wednesday at $192.31; while the one arising from the purchase of Cedears (local certificates that follow the quotation of foreign companies) closed at $191.53.Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Echag\u252\'00\'FCe, from Consultatio said: "Cedears are instruments that have a much broader value than the exchange rate . There we can access shares of the most successful companies in the world. Thinking of them in terms of exchange rate and short term is a distortion\par \par \uc2 . Today we see very attractive opportunities in the map of global stocks that go beyond the convenience or not of using this instrument as a vehicle for dollarization "Meanwhile, several traders agreed that as of these new restrictions, "the curl is dead":\par \par \uc2 "The new regulations completely cut the option of making arbitrage with the different legislations, that is, buying a bond under Argentine law and selling it under foreign law", pointed out a trader.Although most of them agreed that it is still too early to know if there will be a new way to replace it, they anticipated that the controls as they are established will not be able to be extended too much in time and that the market will look for another way to make its arbitrages\par \par \uc2 . See also\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020211007eha60007w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
