\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 The Financial Dollar Rallied Again and Reached Another Record Price\b0\par\par\uc2 501 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 2021\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Although the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BCRA) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  strongly in the bond market, so that the MEP and the cash with liquidation (CCL) that agents carry out through government securities do not escape, the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  can do nothing with the gap between these and the CCL of shares or Cedear.\par \par \uc2 Proof of this is that there is a distance of $ 17 between the MEP dollar obtained by buying an AL30 bond and selling it as AL30D with respect to the CCL that is carried out with shares and ADR.\par \par \uc2 In the last few rounds, the cash with liquidity of stocks have been renewing record prices and today some of them crossed the $ 190 mark.\par \par \uc2 To cite a case, the CCL made through Banco Galicia shares reached a value of $ 190.41.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, Clave Burs\u225\'00\'E1til developed a formula that averages the cash settlement of the most used shares for this purpose (Banco Galicia, \uc2 Banco Macro\uc2 , Banco Franc\u233\'00\'E9s YPF and \uc2 Pampa Energ\u237\'00\'EDa\uc2 ) and it was at $ 189.20 at yesterday's close.\par \par \uc2 For those who choose to dollarize by buying an Apple Cedear and then sell it in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  is located at a value of $ 189.96.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the average CCL of Cedear (adding to Apple the underlying of \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , Tesla, \uc2 Coca Cola\uc2  and \uc2 Barrick Gold\uc2 ) closed the trading session at $ 188.44.\par \par \uc2 Looking at these values allows us to have a proxy of where the CCL and MEP of bonds could go if the BCRA does not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It is worth noting that, since the sovereign debt swap in 2020, the Central participates in the financial dollar market by selling bonds against pesos and buying them back against dollars.\par \par \uc2 The issue overheats: the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  returned to assist the Treasury\par \par \uc2 According to market estimates, this \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  used by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the gap at bay is costing between u$s 12 and u$s 20 million dollars a day, depending on the day.\par \par \uc2 Dollar: what are the three exchange fronts that pressure the BCRA\par \par \uc2 This is a fact that is not minor for the BCRA's weakened reserves and even more so if we take into account that throughout September the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also became a seller in the Single and Free \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Market, given that agricultural settlements were reduced due to seasonal reasons.\par \par \uc2 In addition, the entity presided by Miguel Angel Pesce has been adding regulations that restrict the exchange activity through bonds, but that does not prevent agents to keep looking for the greenback to cover themselves from the fluctuations of the Argentine \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In yesterday's trading, the MEP dollar obtained through the AL30 in T+2 closed at $ 172.99, while the one bought in immediate spot was at $ 173.51. Likewise, the AL30 spot with liquidation in T+2 closed at $ 173.13 and the immediate spot at $ 173.55 pesos.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020210923eh9m000r8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
