\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 The blue dollar "calmed" at $186: back to the same level as before the PASO\b0\par\par\uc2 376 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 September 2021\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The parallel or "blue" dollar, which is traded outside the formal market in financial caves, closed at $186 on Friday, September 17, in the third consecutive day marked by the political crisis in the government of \uc2 Alberto Fernandez\uc2 , checkmated by the questioning of Vice President \uc2 Cristina Fernandez de Kirchner\uc2  to his cabinet.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the parallel market had shown a tendency to rise as the internal dispute in the ruling coalition increased, surpassing $187, the highest value so far in 2021. The figure in which it remained this day equals that of the previous Friday, in the run-up to the primary elections, open, simultaneous and mandatory (PASO) in which the ruling party was defeated.\par \par \uc2 After the election result, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had even lost value against the peso. However, the subsequent political crisis was accompanied by three consecutive days in which it rose $3.50.\par \par \uc2 At the end of the week, sources in the Buenos Aires city estimated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange market, injecting 140 million dollars to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  price stable.\par \par \uc2 Analysts also agree that the demand observed in recent days may be due to the intention of some entities to increase the liquidity of banknotes to respond to any demand during the next days. This reason would make it possible that in some days there will be a disarmament of positions and an increase in the supply of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . This would have an impact on the price of the dollar, which would lower its price.\par \par \uc2 The behavior of the "different dollars The MEP dollar, which is acquired through the Buenos Aires stock exchange by buying and selling bonds, traded with an upward trend, at $173.34.\par \par \uc2 The cash with liquidation, similar to the stock exchange dollar, but to take foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  out of the country, traded higher and reached $173.52.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the retail dollar was offered at an average of $ 97.474 for the buying end and $103.771 for the selling end.\par \par \uc2 If taxes and surcharges are taken into account, the so-called "solidarity" dollar consolidates above $171, reaching $171.22.\par \par \uc2 LC CP\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020210918eh9h000b4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
