\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina forms agency to manage cargo river, grain exporters worry\b0\par\par\uc2 546 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 August 2021\par 20:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Aug 25 (Reuters) - Argentina said on Wednesday it had formed a new government agency to manage dredging \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  needed to ensure navigation of the Parana River, which carries about 80% of the country's grains exports from the Pampas farm belt out to sea.\par \par \uc2 For decades, cargo ships have paid tolls directly to the private dredging company in charge of keeping the river open.\par \par \uc2 Industry executives worry that government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the waterway will heap bureaucracy and extra costs on the grains export sector, which is the main source of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  needed to refresh \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar reserves strained by a three-year recession exacerbated by the COVID-19 pandemic.\par \par \uc2 Grains powerhouse Argentina is the world's No. 3 corn exporter and top supplier of soymeal livestock feed, used to fatten hogs and poultry from Europe to Southeast Asia.\par \par \uc2 The National Ports Administration has been given authority over the next 11 months to subcontract management of the waterway, while the Transportation Ministry evaluates bids from dredging companies for the long-term concession to follow.\par \par \uc2 "The strengthening of policies on the management of inland waterways is a priority objective of the national executive," the government said in a decree published on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The tolls paid by ships for dredging services performed by the company that wins the upcoming Parana contract will be received by the newly established agency, the decree said.\par \par \uc2 "This decree looks like the government does not only want to set up conditions for the tender and the dredging tariff. It looks like an excess of bureaucracy that might mean additional costs for export \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the river," said Gustavo Idigoras, head of the CIARA-CEC export companies' chamber.\par \par \uc2 "We welcome the idea of having a control agency, but we are concerned abut additional bureaucracy and costs. So we need to have close conversations with the government," Idigoras said.\par \par \uc2 A Transportation Ministry source, who asked not to be named, said the new dredging oversight board could actually make it less expensive to ship grains from Argentina.\par \par \uc2 "The price of tolls paid by cargo ships to the dredging company is something that will be determined in the bidding process. The tolls could end up going down," said the source. "One of our objectives is to lower logistics costs."\par \par \uc2 This is the latest chapter in a long saga of farmers and exporters opposing government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the sector.\par \par \uc2 The dredging of the Parana gives \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  an edge over rival exporters Brazil and the United States, which rely more on less efficient trucks and slow-moving barges.\par \par \uc2 The new agency has inflamed exporters and farmers already worried about the policies of center-left President Alberto Fernandez, a Peronist whose administration has curtailed beef exports as a way of controlling domestic food price inflation.\par \par \uc2 The industry is fretting that if the flow of toll money goes through the state, it would dilute and increase dredging costs.\par \par \uc2 The river at Rosario is dredged to about a depth of 34 feet (10 meters), and industry leaders want the next long-term contract to provide for a deeper, wider shipping channel. (Reporting by Hugh Bronstein and Maximilian Heath; editing by Jonathan Oatis) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2021-8-25T19:46:18.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020210825eh8p03fue\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
