\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Once again Argentine stocks have a rally ahead of the PASO: can 2019 be repeated?\b0\par\par\uc2 1,086 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 August 2021\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 In the last three business days, the Merval index -which groups the leading local stocks- rose more than 6% and marked an incipient change of climate on the part of investors, who had been escaping the local market. Some papers, especially the energy sector such as Edenor and Pampa, rose 10.4% and 7.6%. But banking stocks that had been lagging behind also stood out, with gains of almost 9% in the cases of Macro and Supervielle.\par \par \uc2 Ariel Sbdar, CEO of Cocos Capital, is one of the brokers who has been insisting for some time on the opportunities presented by Argentine stocks due to their low prices. "There is nothing in particular that drives them. There is the fact that valuations are too low even within the uncertainty of the local market. That is why it is logical to go to more reasonable values. Afterwards, we will see what happens with everything else.\par \par \uc2 The Merval index surpassed the 70,000 points barrier and is now close to USD 400, when a few months ago it reached the equivalent of USD 300. Yesterday it had the most important rise in recent times, 3.3% to 71,353 points. And it accumulates a rise of 6% in just three days.\par \par \uc2 On August 12, 2019, after the PASO, the Argentine market fell 50% in dollars, a historical fall rarely recorded globally. Many stocks would still have to rise between 40% and 140% to reach those levels.\par \par \uc2 In short, behind the recovery of the stock market there are some specific aspects that should be taken into account. Especially to answer the question whether there can be a new blow like the one the local market already suffered in 2019, right after the PASO. These are some central aspects:\par \par \uc2 Suggestive pre-election polls: when there are less than three weeks to the PASO it is logical for investors to start looking closely at what the projections say. Although there is no unanimity by far, the most relevant data from the different political polls is that people are very unhappy about their economic situation and that the scandal generated by the photos and videos of the Olivos party in which the President himself took part has also fallen very badly. To complete this picture, in the province of Buenos Aires everything indicates that the Government would have a favorable result but at the same time much tighter than in 2019, so it would not be enough to win a majority in the Chamber of Deputies. These data have generated enthusiasm among investors who follow Argentina closely, although most recommend moving with "caution". It is still too fresh the memory of what happened in the run-up to the PASO of 2019, when an even result was predicted and finally \uc2 Alberto Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez\uc2  won by 14 points, generating a real collapse in the quotations. The danger of repeating this scenario is minor because the values are already very low, but if the result is more favorable than expected for the ruling party, it could also have a negative impact on quotes.\par \par \uc2 The agreement with the \uc2 IMF\uc2  seems closer: the signals from the government are quite clear about the need to agree with the organization, if only to kick forward the maturities of 2022 and 2023. The expectation is that the commitment will also serve to accommodate the main imbalances, particularly the fiscal deficit, but also how exchange controls will continue. If progress is made, it would be key to reduce the levels of distrust and it would also be of vital importance to avoid a new exchange rate crisis after the legislative elections, which will be held on November 14.\par \par \uc2 The signals from the government are quite clear about the need to agree with the \uc2 IMF\uc2 , if only to kick forward the maturities of 2022 and 2023.\par \par \uc2 Stock prices are "given away": most of the papers are still well below the value they had reached on August 12, 2019, after the blow suffered by the local market due to the result of the last PASO. That day, the Argentine market fell 50% in dollars, a historic drop rarely recorded globally. Many stocks would still have to rise between 40% and 140% to reach those levels. Very few have even managed to stay above those values, among the few that did are \uc2 Pampa Energ\u237\'00\'EDa\uc2 , \uc2 Cresud\uc2  and \uc2 Tenaris\uc2 . Even measured in dollars, the Merval index is at very low values, trading at around USD 400 taking as exchange rate the "contado con liquidaci\u243\'00\'F3n". This is a little higher than the USD 300 floor that historically acted as support, but it is clearly lower than the average of the last ten years. Of course, the fact that stocks are being given away doesn't assure anything either. If distrust increases, it is clear that this is an illiquid market in which "going out at any price" can generate a disaster in prices.\par \par \uc2 Funds are pouring into emerging countries: Brazil was one of the main beneficiaries in recent days. The persistence of low rates in the United States and the rebound in oil prices had a favorable impact on the Brazilian market and a small portion of those flows also spilled over into the local market, as happened in the middle of the year. That rebound was then overshadowed by MSCI's decision to recategorize Argentina as a "standalone" market, even below the "frontier" category.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  gained firepower after the Fund's dollar transfer: the USD 4.3 billion that the agency delivered to Argentina as part of its capitalization process increased the level of gross reserves to USD 46.3 billion. Although only a fraction can be used to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange market, it is clear that the entity presided by Miguel Pesce is in a position to avoid at least until the elections a surprise with the price of the dollar. In addition, the entity retains some "firepower", not only through reserves, but also through new regulations that limit access to the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the futures market.\par \par \uc2 KEEP READING\par \par \uc2 OECD\uc2  says \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economy still 2.8% below pre-pandemic level\par \par \uc2 Dollar Today: Free Trade Ends Stable at 182 Pesos for Third Day in a Row\par \par \uc2 More Tension Between the Government and the Countryside: Government Bill Seeks to Remove Rural Farmers from the Management of INTA\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020210825eh8p002ju\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
