\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Argentina spawns another  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  rate as government clamps down\b0\par\par\uc2 575 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juli 2021\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Government steps to regain control over Argentina\u8217\'20\'19s chaotic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market has led a new unofficial exchange rate to rise to prominence.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s the third rate to become relevant since capital controls were put back in place in Argentina in September 2019, all running parallel to the official rate controlled by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here is a brief explainer:\par \par \uc2 1. What\u8217\'20\'19s the new \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate? Traders have started focusing on the blue-chip swap rate that trades over the counter on a platform known as SENEBI. The rate is determined by taking assets that trade locally and selling them in offshore markets for dollars. Traders prefer to use government bonds due 2030 (AL30 and GD30) because they\u8217\'20\'19re the most liquid. The rate that comes from that \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  is only known by the two parties involved, and doesn\u8217\'20\'19t appear on online platforms.\par \par \uc2 2. What is the impact? The new exchange rate is now starting to stray away from the blue-chip that trades on open platforms and that traders can see on their screens. On Wednesday, the peso traded at 172/USD on the OTC market, according to people with direct knowledge of the matter, 3.4 percent weaker than on the open platforms. That spread has widened from 0.25 percent in the past week.\par \par \uc2 3. Why is there a spread? On July 12, the local securities regulator, known as CNV, set a limit to the amount of bonds that traders can sell on open, regulated platforms. The balance can\u8217\'20\'19t be larger than 100,000 nominal bonds weekly, per individual or company, which is equivalent to around US$35,000 or US$40,000, depending on the bond used for the calculation. On the other hand, OTC trades made in the SENEBI platform don\u8217\'20\'19t have any limits and can\u8217\'20\'19t be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  by regulators. As a result, broker demand for dollars has moved to the OTC market, pushing down the peso.\par \par \uc2 4. What\u8217\'20\'19s the aim of these measures? The reduction to trading volumes on the open platforms make it easier for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market to keep the peso strong. The measures also curbs retail investor access to purchases of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  through parallel markets.\par \par \uc2 5. Why now? Argentina has midterm elections in November and local investors have started purchasing dollars to protect themselves from the volatility that comes with political uncertainty. Also, seasonal dollar sales by crop exporters end in July, reducing the supply of dollars and adding to pressure to the country\u8217\'20\'19s foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates. The government also considers that a slower depreciation of the peso contributes to reducing inflation expectations, another factor that could influence voters.\par \par \uc2 6. Is it the first time this happens? \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a long history of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. The most recent set of major restrictions were put in place in 2019 and focused on reducing dollar purchases in spot markets to a minimum. That led dollar demand to turn to other markets, like the sale of cash dollars on the black market, or through \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  like the blue-chip swap.\par \par \uc2 The most recent measure was on June 30, when the CNV president Adrian Cosentino called brokers to a meeting to request that they reduce their \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in open platforms and channel liquidity through bilateral trading.\par \par \uc2 by Ignacio Olivera Doll, Bloomberg\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020210715eh7f0083c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
