\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Why Argentine traders now look at the parallel peso 'OTC'\b0\par\par\uc2 671 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juli 2021\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Argentine traders are beginning to monitor a new exchange rate in the market,which emerged from the latest exchange restrictions and has already been added to the extensive list of indicators they monitor daily.\par \par \par \par \uc2 1. What is the new indicator?\u160\'00\'A0Since the return of capital controls in September 2019, traders have closely followed the cash settlement, a parallel exchange rate that arises from the buying and selling of securities in the local and foreign capital markets.\par \par \uc2 But in recent days traders are focusing on the cash settlement "over the counter", which arises from \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  carried out in bilateral rounds, called SENEBI and bilateral MAE. This type of change began to distance itself from the one that is negotiated in the direct wheel and that is seen on the screens.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the exchange rate bilaterally agreed between the agents stood at 172/USD, according to two people with direct knowledge, and the gap between the two widened to 3.4%, from 0.25% on July 8, prior to the measures.\par \par \par \par \uc2 2. How is it calculated?\u160\'00\'A0The cash with settlement is calculated by dividing the value in pesos of a share or a public security in the local market by the dollar value of the same asset abroad.\par \par \uc2 To calculate the OTC exchange rate, traders prefer to use dollar sovereign bonds maturing in 2030 (AL30 and GD30) because they are the most liquid.\par \par \uc2 The cash settlement that arises in that market is only known by the parties involved and does not trade on the screens.\par \par \par \par \uc2 3. Why is there a gap?\u160\'00\'A0The local regulator, the National Securities Commission, this week set a limit for bond sales that traders can make on the wheel on open platforms, which are the regulated ones.\par \par \uc2 The balance sold can be up to 100,000 nominals per week per company or individual, equivalent to between 35,000 and 40,000 dollars, depending on the bonus used for the calculation. On the other hand, the \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in SENEBI have no limits and the official body does not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in them. As there is a limit on the regulated market, the demand of the agents is transferred to the bilateral market and the costs of the \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  become more expensive there.\par \par \par \par \uc2 4. What is the government's objective?\u160\'00\'A0The limit reduces the volume traded and, consequently, facilitates the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  carries out to keep the peso stronger in the spot market. In addition, the measures limit retail investors' access to foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying opportunities through parallel markets.\par \par \par \par \uc2 5. Why now?\u160\'00\'A0Argentina has midterm elections in November, and local investors are already taking precautions by buying dollars to protect themselves from political uncertainty. In addition, the seasonal dollar sales season for the agricultural sector ends in July, and the supply of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to start to decline, increasing pressure on exchange rates. The government also believes that a smaller depreciation of the peso contributes to reducing inflation expectations, another factor that could influence voter sentiment.\par \par \par \par \uc2 6. Is this the first time?\u160\'00\'A0\b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a long history of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. The most recent restrictions were put in place in 2019 and focused on minimizing dollar purchases in the official \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. They also resulted in the demand for dollars being transferred to other markets, such as the sale of tickets in the informal segment or dollarization through cash with settlement.\par \par \uc2 In order to control these markets, the government carried out raids on financial institutions in the Buenos Aires microcenter and sought, at other times, to limit the purchase and sale of bonds in the capital market, establishing a minimum period for holding bonds, known as "parking." The most recent measure had been on June 30, when CNV President Adrian Cosentino summoned the agents to a meeting to ask them to reduce their \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the direct round and channel them through the bilateral round.\par \par \par \par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A92021 \uc2 Bloomberg L.P\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020210715eh7f006oj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
